1788362337166514	sigil-dev	itc:v3:AWLOeSZkkyTnmRAAAAAAQd3q2q1d7QAAAAExCw		item.create	bn-15tj	{"description":"In /home/bob/src/sigil, maw ws merge bn-7c0x and maw merge promote adca706412db both ran cargo check --all-targets with captured stdout/stderr. Cargo became blocked in anon_pipe_write while Maw slept in hrtimer_nanosleep. The first attempt timed out after exactly 600 seconds with empty validation output; the promotion showed the same state after 12+ minutes. A verbose successful Cargo check can fill Maw capture pipes before child exit. Drain output concurrently or stream it while retaining bounded captured diagnostics and timeout behavior. Reproducer and discussion anchor: rite history --thread 01M1HA5VGG6N9ZX6X6PPB7D2W0.","kind":"bug","title":"Prevent merge validation pipe backpressure deadlock"}	blake3:L_wpsbvW4OeqkvU6uo6k3ski8jDJglkB9ECjFhRZLxA
1788736108713788	maw-dev	itc:v3:AWKTmSTM_JOSSTQAAAAAQa7Vbfq6qsAAAAEylBc		item.create	bn-1uif	{"description":"Outcome\nMake maw ws merge and maw ws merge --check resolve source workspaces through the selected layout/backend inside the active-change ancestry guard. Consolidated repositories must never be redirected to the legacy ws/<name> tree.\n\nObserved reproduction\nOn maw 1.0.0-pre.14 in /home/bob/src/sigil, a healthy source is registered by both maw ws list and git worktree list at /home/bob/src/sigil/.maw/workspaces/bn-4d8r. Running:\n\n  maw ws merge bn-4d8r --into default --check --format json\n\nfails with:\n\n  failed to open repo at /home/bob/src/sigil/ws/bn-4d8r\n\nSetting MAW_LAYOUT=consolidated produces the same failure. The source workspace is committed, current, and ready to merge.\n\nRoot cause\ncrates/maw-cli/src/workspace/merge.rs function guard_unbound_sources_against_active_change_ancestry reconstructs each source as root.join(\"ws\").join(ws_name). This bypasses LayoutFlavor and WorkspaceBackend. The guard is reached for a default/epoch-updating merge when active-change ancestry must be checked, so other commands can correctly discover .maw/workspaces/<name> while this merge path fails.\n\nImpact\nThis blocks merging approved Sigil structured-data work at commit 2354be75 (Sigil bone bn-4d8r). It can block any unbound source merge in a consolidated repository when active changes exist.\n\nAcceptance\n- Resolve the source path via the authoritative layout-aware/backend path already used by the merge pipeline; do not add a second path convention.\n- Add a regression test using a consolidated repository, an unbound source workspace, and active-change ancestry so both --check and the real merge open .maw/workspaces/<name>.\n- Preserve the safety refusal when an unbound source actually contains active-change ancestry.\n- Preserve legacy v2 ws/<name> behavior and all workspace backends.\n- Ensure diagnostics name the authoritative resolved path.\n- Run the focused merge tests and the full project check.","kind":"bug","labels":["merge","consolidated-layout","regression"],"size":"s","title":"Fix active-change merge guard hard-coded legacy workspace path","urgency":"urgent"}	blake3:hcZ1ijTXsLAn4fKHb_fWy_9Y94ZAq44qj0Rm9THiwqs
