1790197309362617	edict-6jkvat	itc:v3:AWKZJOSZmZmZ8lAAAAAAQbVdW222-oAAAAExAQ		item.create	bn-31u8	{"description":"Requested by edict (bn-2f92). maw ws merge snapshots the live source workspace, including uncommitted additions and deletions (confirmed with maw 1.0.0-pre.15). That is right for zero-loss merges, but a reviewed merge must equal the reviewed commits: Seal approves committed history, so uncommitted files merge unreviewed. edict now refuses to merge when git status shows anything outside the review log, chained with && to maw ws merge, but a writer can still act between that check and maw's snapshot. Ask: a flag such as --committed-only (merge HEAD, refuse or ignore a dirty tree) or --commit <sha> (merge exactly this commit), applied inside maw's merge lock. edict would then pass it for reviewed workspaces.","kind":"task","title":"ws merge: option to merge committed content only (or an exact commit)"}	blake3:mYnRJsXzRBaVyXDcHqJiICpzOq1Xi1RYKnnRuQUOjzs
1790376279433125	bones-imvgpj	itc:v3:AWLzPOTyZPOcQAAAAAAAQfb3XrXu4AAAAAEsAQ		item.create	bn-1ijl	{"description":"Seen in bones (2026-09-25). 'maw ws sync bn-12ta' rebasing 4 commits onto a new epoch replayed the first, then failed:\n\n  Error: Failed to extract patchset for 21aa7debbe09: git repo error: not found: blob 05c543611e79e9be646cc98c09a44ef5d6edb134: Object named 05c543... was supposed to be of kind blob, but was kind tree.\n\nCommit 21aa7deb deletes the tracked .crit/ directory (.crit/.gitignore, .crit/reviews/*/events.jsonl, .crit/version, .critignore) and adds .seal/. The epoch it was rebasing onto already contained the same migration from another workspace. The patchset extraction appears to treat a directory (tree) entry as a file blob.\n\nConsequences: the workspace stays stale; 'maw ws merge' refuses a stale workspace, so it cannot merge at all. Workaround used: new workspace from main plus git cherry-pick of the other commits. After that, 'maw ws destroy' refuses (14 unmerged changes) because the cherry-picked hashes differ, although content is identical.\n\nRepro sketch: two workspaces from epoch E each commit the same directory deletion + additions. Merge the first. 'maw ws sync' the second.","kind":"bug","size":"s","title":"ws sync fails replaying a commit that deletes a directory: blob expected, found tree"}	blake3:Heh4-KrCbaCq8mAH1sCQ24CO9G3yyYRIBIM99HdCzLY
1790464277527574	maw-lsz75n	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-2ws4	{"description":"OBJECTIVE\nPoint maw's formal-verification tooling at the code that has actually produced\ndata-loss and containment defects, and make every verification gate run\nsomewhere automatically so it cannot silently rot again.\n\nWHY (survey 2026-09-26)\nmaw already has Kani (24 harnesses, src/merge/kani_proofs.rs, merge algebra),\na Stateright protocol model (crates/maw-assurance/src/model.rs), proptests and\nDST. But:\n  - The recent defect classes are NOT in the merge algebra. They are path\n    predicates (FF-absorb dir/file prefix collision, recovery --restore-file\n    symlink escape, D/F clashes) and the FF-absorb sibling decision logic\n    (4 data-loss defects: bn-p3m9, bn-286g, bn-mq3b, prefix-collision).\n  - None of the formal gates run in CI, and they have rotted:\n      * `cargo check --no-default-features` fails (13 errors; build_phase.rs\n        imports for the not(ast-merge) branch are incomplete), so\n        `just kani-fast` does not compile.\n      * src/merge/determinism_tests.rs + pushout_tests.rs are behind the\n        `proptests` feature which nothing enables.\n      * `just formal-check` (Stateright) is #[ignore] + local-only, and the\n        model has drifted from the real commit protocol.\n\nTOOL ROUTING (rust-formal-verification skill)\n  - Kani: pure decision functions and path predicates with small bounded\n    domains; bounded codecs (LFS pointer <= 1024 bytes); finite state tables.\n  - proptest: glob/attr matching that goes through gix-glob; generators\n    must be able to produce component-prefix path pairs.\n  - Stateright: multi-process protocol (merge/sync/destroy/gc/auto-sync +\n    agent writes) sharing refs and flock locks.\n  - loom: NOT needed (no real in-process concurrency; only one-shot latches).\n  - Verus: deferred; only candidate is PatchSet::join associativity with\n    conflicts. Revisit after Kani/Stateright work lands.\n\nDISCIPLINE (applies to every child bone)\n  - Every new harness must be shown to go RED on a deliberate mutation of the\n    code under test before it is reported green (record the mutation in the\n    bone comment).\n  - Harnesses must call the real production function, never an inline copy.\n  - Bounded harness names must not overclaim (e.g. `..._paths_le_3_comps`).\n  - Extract pure functions into maw-core where practical so Kani does not have\n    to compile gix/maw-cli.\n\nDONE WHEN\n  All child bones closed; `just check` (or a dedicated CI workflow) runs\n  kani-fast, the proptests feature and the Stateright model; confirmed bugs\n  found along the way are fixed with regression tests.\n","kind":"goal","labels":["verification","assurance"],"size":"xl","title":"Formal verification where the bugs actually are: path predicates, FF-absorb decisions, protocol model"}	blake3:dspuyCULU9legnhin9NGLFEcJZE_fTHmbEpEl_M8MZg
1790464377693090	maw-lsz75n	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-86hd	{"description":"OBJECTIVE\nMake the existing formal gates compile, pass, and run automatically.\n\nFINDINGS (2026-09-26)\n1. `cargo check --no-default-features` fails with 13 errors. src/merge/build_phase.rs:64-67\n   imports ConflictReason/ConflictRecord/ResolveError/ResolveResult only under\n   cfg(feature = \"ast-merge\"), but they are used unconditionally. `just kani-fast` /\n   `just kani-full` (Justfile:113-118) both use --no-default-features, so the 24 Kani\n   harnesses in src/merge/kani_proofs.rs have not compiled for some time.\n   Also an unused-imports warning at kani_proofs.rs:53.\n2. src/merge/mod.rs:46-50 gates determinism_tests.rs and pushout_tests.rs behind\n   feature \"proptests\"; `just test` (Justfile:80) never enables it. They never run.\n3. `just formal-check` (Stateright, Justfile:97) is #[ignore] + local-only.\n\nAPPROACH\n- Fix the imports so the not(ast-merge) build compiles (import unconditionally, or\n  gate correctly). Verify `cargo check --no-default-features` and\n  `cargo clippy --no-default-features` are clean.\n- Run `just kani-fast`; fix any harness rot. Record run time. Do NOT run kani-full\n  (~49 min) in the gate; note if it still passes if you can afford it.\n- Run `cargo test --features proptests`; fix any rot.\n- Wire into the gate: add a `verify` Justfile recipe (proptests feature + kani-fast +\n  formal-check) and call proptests from `just check`. kani-fast/formal-check go in a\n  GitHub workflow (.github/workflows/verify.yml, using model-checking/kani-github-action\n  or `cargo install --locked kani-verifier && cargo kani setup`) triggered on push to\n  main + PR, modelled on dst-faithful.yml. If kani is too slow for per-push, make it\n  nightly + workflow_dispatch.\n- Add `cargo check --no-default-features` to `just check` so the feature matrix\n  cannot rot again.\n\nACCEPTANCE\n- `cargo check --no-default-features` green; `just kani-fast` green (all harnesses\n  VERIFICATION:- SUCCESSFUL); `cargo test --features proptests` green.\n- `just check` exercises no-default build + proptests.\n- New workflow file exists and is syntactically valid (actionlint if available).\n- Sanity mutation: flip one branch in classify_shared_path, confirm kani-fast goes\n  red, revert. Record in a bone comment.\n","kind":"task","labels":["verification","ci"],"parent":"bn-2ws4","size":"m","title":"Restore rotted verification gates: fix --no-default-features build, run kani-fast + proptests in the check gate"}	blake3:vdraUPIaqfn6XN0Yy53OLeptAFbzrk1y6qtKKs6sJZc
1790464377848022	maw-lsz75n	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-2jml	{"description":"OBJECTIVE\nMake file/directory clash detection complete, and make the property tests capable\nof finding this class.\n\nDEFECT (confirmed by reading, not yet reproduced)\ncrates/maw-core/src/merge/partition.rs:304-410 (`partition_by_path`, bn-2dy1 D/F\ndetection). `all_path_ws` includes unique AND shared non-deletion entries, but both\ndetection directions loop only over `unique` (`for (path, entry) in &unique`). If\nws1+ws2 both add FILE `a` (shared) and ws3+ws4 both add `a/b` (shared), neither\nloop runs for either path, so no DfClash is emitted. Shared-vs-unique IS caught\n(direction 1 scans all_path_ws; direction 2 binary-searches all_path_strs).\nPrefix check is string-based (`format!(\"{p}/\")`) — correct for normalised\n'/'-joined relative paths, but verify there is no `./` or trailing-slash input.\n\nAlso: proptest generators `arb_path` in src/merge/determinism_tests.rs:85 and\nsrc/merge/pushout_tests.rs:139 append `.rs` only to the last segment, so a generated\npath can never be a directory prefix of another — no proptest can ever produce a\nD/F clash. (These tests are behind the `proptests` feature; see sibling bone\nrestoring gates.)\n\nAPPROACH\n1. Write a failing regression test first (unit test in partition.rs tests module\n   with 4 workspaces as above). Then check what happens END TO END: does the merge\n   fail at tree build, silently drop a path, or produce a bad tree? Document it.\n2. Fix: iterate every non-deletion (path, ws) in unique AND shared for both\n   directions (or restructure as: sort all non-deletion paths; for each adjacent\n   component-prefix pair with differing workspace sets, emit clash). Keep output\n   deterministic and deduped.\n3. Specification property: clash reported for P iff exists non-deleted P, Q from\n   workspaces such that P is a strict component prefix of Q and not all\n   (P-ws, Q-ws) pairs are the same single workspace. Add a proptest with a generator\n   over a tiny alphabet {a, b, a.rs} x depth<=3 x 2-4 workspaces so prefix pairs are\n   common. Optionally a Kani harness if partition_by_path's types are Kani-friendly\n   (it lives in maw-core, which is a lighter crate) — bounded to <=4 entries.\n4. Fix arb_path in determinism_tests.rs / pushout_tests.rs to sometimes produce\n   prefix pairs (e.g. last segment optionally without extension, shared prefixes).\n5. Mutation check: remove the fix, confirm the new property goes red.\n\nACCEPTANCE\n- Regression test red before fix, green after.\n- Property test with prefix-capable generator passes; mutation shown to fail it.\n- `just check` green.\n","kind":"bug","labels":["verification","merge","data-integrity"],"parent":"bn-2ws4","size":"m","title":"Bug: D/F clash detection misses shared-vs-shared paths; proptest generators cannot produce D/F pairs"}	blake3:QbTytKyECwN5ICEH3HFzL_TiX8zxp2QKWzR6ArjwUtQ
1790464377997248	maw-lsz75n	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-1cth	{"description":"OBJECTIVE\nValidate quarantine merge ids and make quarantine paths layout-aware.\n\nDEFECT 1 (confirmed by reading)\nsrc/merge/quarantine.rs:212-238: `quarantine_workspace_name`,\n`quarantine_workspace_path` (repo_root/ws/merge-quarantine-<id>), `state_dir`\n(manifold_dir/quarantine/<id>) join the CLI-supplied merge_id without validation.\n`maw merge abandon <id>` (crates/maw-cli/src/merge_cmd.rs:357) then calls\nabandon_quarantine -> remove_dir_all(state_dir). `../..` escapes\nmanifold/quarantine/. Severity is limited: merge_cmd::abandon returns early when\nQuarantineState::read is NotFound and ws_path does not exist, so deletion needs a\n`state.json` (any content — a parse error falls through to a WARNING and proceeds)\nat the escaped target. Still a containment hole; ids are also printed as copy-paste\ncommands for agents.\nAlso: merge_id_from_name(quarantine_workspace_name(id)) round trip, and the name must\nbe a valid WorkspaceId, which requires id.len() <= 47 (64 - 17-char prefix) — no\nvalidator enforces that.\n\nDEFECT 2 (unverified — confirm first)\nquarantine.rs:220, :284, :293 hardcode `repo_root.join(\"ws\")` (legacy v2 bare\nlayout). In the consolidated layout the repo root IS the default workspace checkout\nand agent workspaces live in .maw/workspaces/. Called live from\ncrates/maw-cli/src/workspace/merge.rs:5699 (create_quarantine_workspace on\nvalidation failure with quarantine policy). Suspected effect: quarantine worktree is\ncreated at <root>/ws/merge-quarantine-<id>, i.e. inside the user's trunk checkout.\nReproduce in a /tmp consolidated repo with a failing [merge.validation] command and\non_failure = quarantine (check config.rs for exact keys).\n\nAPPROACH\n- Add `validate_merge_id(&str) -> Result<(), QuarantineError>`: non-empty, <= 47\n  bytes, [a-z0-9-] only (match what compute_merge_id in\n  crates/maw-core/src/merge/plan.rs:154 actually produces — check it), no leading\n  '-'. Call it at every public entry taking a merge_id (read, abandon, promote,\n  path helpers via a checked constructor). Clear error with the exact list command.\n- If defect 2 reproduces: route paths through the layout / backend workspace path\n  (see LayoutFlavor in maw-core/src/model/layout.rs and how normal ws create\n  resolves paths); keep v2 behaviour for legacy layout. Regression test in\n  consolidated layout.\n- Kani harness (in whichever crate hosts validate_merge_id; move pure helpers to\n  maw-core if the root crate is too heavy): for any id up to ~8 bytes over an\n  alphabet including '.', '/', '-', 'a', '0': validate_merge_id(id).is_ok() implies\n  state_dir(base, id) has exactly one Normal component beyond base, name round trips\n  via merge_id_from_name, and the name passes WorkspaceId validation. Mutation-check\n  (drop the '/' rejection -> red).\n\nACCEPTANCE\n- `maw merge abandon ../x` rejected with actionable error, no fs access.\n- Defect 2 either fixed with consolidated-layout regression test, or documented as\n  not reproducing with evidence.\n- Kani harness green, shown red under mutation. `just check` green.\n","kind":"bug","labels":["verification","security","merge"],"parent":"bn-2ws4","size":"s","title":"Bug: quarantine merge_id unvalidated (path traversal in abandon/promote) + quarantine hardcodes legacy ws/ layout"}	blake3:l-K7sbQEJ9V00uKH41g5pxmkB-Bk88wvobq7KZrblGQ
1790464378149358	maw-lsz75n	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-2wav	{"description":"OBJECTIVE\nProve the lexical path-safety predicates that guard filesystem writes/reads are\ncorrect over all small inputs. This is the recovery --restore-file symlink-escape\nclass (fixed in pre.14) — prove the lexical half so it cannot regress.\n\nTARGETS\n- crates/maw-cli/src/workspace/recover.rs:1407 `checked_restore_destination`\n- crates/maw-cli/src/workspace/recover.rs:1278 `validate_show_path`\n- crates/maw-cli/src/workspace/undo.rs:171 `ensure_safe_relative_path`\n- crates/maw-cli/src/workspace/capture.rs:891 `path_is_under_excluded`\n  (must be component-wise: `a` excludes `a/x` but not `ab`)\n- NOT workspace/mod.rs:2276 path_is_within (canonicalises via the OS; out of scope,\n  mention in comment).\n\nAPPROACH\n- Read each function. Separate the pure lexical part (component inspection) from any\n  filesystem part (symlink_metadata, canonicalize). Extract the lexical part as a\n  pure fn in maw-core (suggest crates/maw-core/src/model/path_safety.rs or similar;\n  reuse one shared predicate if the three validators duplicate logic — deduplicate\n  only if semantics truly match). Callers keep the fs checks.\n- Kani harnesses (cfg(kani) module in maw-core; add `cfg(kani)` to check-cfg lints\n  for that crate if needed): paths built from <= 4 components over\n  {\"a\", \"ab\", \".\", \"..\", \"\", \"/\"-rooted, \"a/b\"}. Properties:\n    * accepted relative path => every component is Normal => base.join(p) starts\n      with base (lexically) and has no `..`\n    * rejects absolute, empty, `..`-containing inputs\n    * path_is_under_excluded(p, ex) <=> ex's components are a prefix of p's\n  If Path/PathBuf is too heavy for CBMC, model paths as Vec<Comp> and have the\n  production code operate over `Path::components()` with a thin adapter proven\n  separately by unit tests — but the harness must call production code.\n- If Kani proves impractical for Path, fall back to exhaustive enumeration in a\n  normal #[test] (the domain is small: 7^4 inputs) — that IS a proof for the bound.\n  Record which approach and why.\n- Mutation-check each harness.\n\nACCEPTANCE\n- Harnesses green, each shown red under a recorded mutation.\n- Any real bug found gets a regression test + fix (file a separate bug bone if large).\n- `just check` green.\n","kind":"task","labels":["verification","security"],"parent":"bn-2ws4","size":"m","title":"Kani: path containment predicates (recover --show/--restore-file, undo, capture exclusion)"}	blake3:EBid3DY5XTIu9gu9StUeWm0koHnrEt1z5CvCw6w-0uE
1790464378297324	maw-lsz75n	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-27n7	{"description":"OBJECTIVE\nThe FF-absorb / sibling-reconcile path has produced four data-loss defects\n(bn-p3m9 materialization, bn-286g ref faithfulness, bn-mq3b multi-epoch stale dirty,\nthe pre.14 dir/file prefix collision). Its decision logic is inline and mixed with\nI/O. Extract it as a pure function and prove the safety rules over every input.\n\nCODE\ncrates/maw-cli/src/workspace/merge.rs:\n  - `reconcile_epoch_with_branch` (~:3632): InSync / diverged error / ff_paths /\n    evaluate_ff_safety / per-sibling classification (~:3740-3858) / block-before-\n    mutation / replay / write_epoch_current (~:3971, plain write, relies on epoch lock)\n    / FF sibling refs + materialize.\n  - `ff_dirty_stale_conflict` (~:4527)\n  - SiblingPlan enum (FastForward, Replay, SkipStaleDirty, skip, block)\ncrates/maw-cli/src/workspace/ff_absorb.rs:\n  - `evaluate_ff_safety` (:61, already pure), `paths_conflict` (:94, already pure)\n\nAPPROACH\n1. Define in maw-core (e.g. crates/maw-core/src/merge/ff_plan.rs) a pure\n   `classify_sibling(input: SiblingFacts) -> SiblingDecision` where SiblingFacts holds\n   booleans/relations (base==branch, head==base, head ahead, dirty, dirty∩own-delta\n   nonempty, head/tree readable) and `stale_dirty_filter(dirty, own_delta) -> set`\n   using a component-prefix `paths_conflict`. Move paths_conflict there too.\n   reconcile_epoch_with_branch computes the facts via I/O and calls these. Behaviour\n   must be byte-identical: run the existing FF-absorb regression tests (grep tests/\n   and crates/maw-cli/tests for bn-mq3b, bn-p3m9, bn-2fto, ff_absorb, prefix) before\n   and after.\n2. Kani harnesses (exhaustive over the finite fact space):\n   - never FastForward a sibling whose HEAD != base (committed work ahead)\n   - never FastForward when dirty ∩ own-delta (stale dirty) is nonempty\n   - unreadable HEAD/tree => fail closed (Skip or Block, never FastForward)\n   - any Block => no mutation plan emitted for any sibling (model the batch fn)\n   - classification total (no panic)\n   paths_conflict over <= 3-component paths from a tiny alphabet: symmetric,\n   reflexive, equals \"one is a component prefix of the other\" (note: leading `./`\n   stays a CurDir component so `./a` vs `a` do not conflict — decide whether inputs\n   are normalised upstream and either assert that precondition or normalise).\n   stale_dirty_filter: result ⊆ dirty, and result empty <=> no (d, s) conflict.\n3. Mutation-check every property (e.g. drop the HEAD!=base check -> red).\n\nACCEPTANCE\n- Pure fns extracted; all existing FF-absorb tests green unchanged.\n- Kani harnesses green, each shown red under a recorded mutation.\n- `just kani-fast` includes the new maw-core harnesses (update Justfile recipe to\n  run `cargo kani -p maw-core` too if needed).\n- `just check` green.\n","kind":"task","labels":["verification","merge","data-integrity"],"parent":"bn-2ws4","size":"l","title":"Extract FF-absorb sibling classifier as a pure function and verify it exhaustively with Kani"}	blake3:mxm1Szoh74b8wDRM-6WeOGUjWJRCV29jS-G7FVEs_5k
1790464378457122	maw-lsz75n	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-z9t3	{"description":"OBJECTIVE\nProve the LFS pointer parser/writer/sniffer agree. Pre.14 fixed false-positive LFS\nsmudging of non-pointer files; lock that class down.\n\nCODE\ncrates/maw-lfs/src/pointer.rs: `parse` (:68), `write` (:161), `looks_like_pointer`\n(:223), `hex_digit`/`hex_char` (:202/:211). Duplicated nibble codecs at\ncrates/maw-lfs/src/store.rs:52/61, crates/maw-lfs/src/batch.rs:363/374,\ncrates/maw-git/src/types.rs:103.\n\nKNOWN GAPS (from reading; confirm)\n- `size +5` accepted (u64::from_str accepts leading '+') — non-canonical.\n- Doc says keys sorted / lowercased, code does not enforce.\n- write() accepts extension keys named oid/size/version, keys with spaces, values\n  with '\\n' -> parse(write(p)) != p.\nCheck the git-lfs spec (https://github.com/git-lfs/git-lfs/blob/main/docs/spec.md)\nbefore deciding what parse must reject. Be conservative about REJECTING things real\ngit-lfs writes — a stricter parser can reclassify real pointers as non-pointers.\nPrefer: parse stays compatible with git-lfs; add `is_canonical`/reject only what\ngit-lfs itself rejects; make write() refuse (Result) or be unreachable for\nmalformed Pointer values (validated constructor).\n\nPROPERTIES\n- parse(b).is_ok() => looks_like_pointer(b)   (sniffer never under-approximates\n  what parse accepts; the reverse direction is allowed to fail)\n- for well-formed p: parse(write(p)) == p\n- hex nibble codec round trip over all 256 bytes / 16 nibbles (Kani, trivially\n  complete); consider deduplicating the 4 copies into one pub fn.\nKani for the hex codec and for parse/looks_like_pointer on small byte inputs\n(<= ~24 bytes symbolic, which covers the prefix logic); proptest for full-size\nround trips with generated valid pointers + mutated near-pointers.\n\nACCEPTANCE\n- Harnesses/proptests green, each shown red under a recorded mutation.\n- Any spec deviation fixed or documented in a bone comment with rationale.\n- `cargo test -p maw-lfs` + `just check` green (just check does not run maw-lfs\n  tests — run them explicitly).\n","kind":"task","labels":["verification","lfs"],"parent":"bn-2ws4","size":"m","title":"Kani + proptest: LFS pointer codec (false-positive pointer detection class)"}	blake3:Bj_G2Q3clg52qT3BVnmNgXjhD1pCPokdJmicL0fVIgw
1790464378612093	maw-lsz75n	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-2l63	{"description":"OBJECTIVE\nCheap exhaustive proofs over small finite maw-core structures.\n\nTARGETS (crates/maw-core/src)\n- merge_state.rs:62 `valid_transitions`, :81 `can_transition_to`, :612\n  `recovery_outcome_for_phase`. Prove: terminal phases have no successors; every\n  non-terminal phase reaches Complete and Aborted; recovery outcomes are consistent\n  with the table. QUESTION TO RESOLVE: `Commit -> Aborted` is allowed although Commit\n  is documented as the point of no return — find why (read commit.rs recovery /\n  bn-38vw notes). Either document the justification at the transition or remove it.\n- model/ordering.rs:147/157 `SequenceGenerator::next`: `last_wall_clock_ms + 1` and\n  `last_seq += 1` overflow at u64::MAX (panic in debug, wrap in release -> ordering\n  violation). Kani will flag it; fix with saturating/checked arithmetic and prove\n  strict monotonicity of successive keys. Also OrderingKey (:65-87): Eq and Ord\n  consistent.\n- model/patch.rs:62/87 `FileId::from_hex`/`to_hex`: round trip + injectivity.\n- model/types.rs:333/364 WorkspaceId validation accepts \"epoch-delta\", the synthetic\n  id used by partition for epoch-delta injection (bn-7phd). Check whether a real\n  workspace named epoch-delta can collide in partition/merge; if so reserve the name\n  (reject in validation with clear error) and prove the synthetic id is outside the\n  accepted set.\n- merge_state.rs:454 `write_atomic` fsyncs the tmp file but not the parent dir\n  (compare src/merge/commit.rs:264). Add the dir fsync (not a proof, just fix it\n  here).\n\nACCEPTANCE\n- Harnesses green, each mutation-checked; overflow fixed; epoch-delta decided.\n- `cargo test -p maw-core`, `just check` green.\n","kind":"task","labels":["verification"],"parent":"bn-2ws4","size":"s","title":"Kani: MergePhase transition table, SequenceGenerator overflow, FileId hex, reserved workspace ids"}	blake3:AHNoMKH94UW0qR_0qBWP1JZrAhMSe1rEIL9SZ8izwkg
1790464378756779	maw-lsz75n	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-3ppf	{"description":"OBJECTIVE\nMake crates/maw-assurance/src/model.rs a faithful model of the multi-process\nprotocol and run it automatically.\n\nCURRENT MODEL (read it first)\nSingle merge actor; u64 OIDs; phases Prepare/Build/Validate/CommitEpoch/\nCommitBranch/Cleanup; CaptureRecovery/Destroy/Abort/Crash/Recover. Properties G1 (no\nsilent loss, :427, initial ancestry hardcoded via reachable.insert(1)), G3 (:472),\nG4 destroy-after-capture (:483). Tests in crates/maw-assurance/tests/formal_model.rs\nare #[ignore]; `just formal-check` is local-only.\n\nDRIFT / GAPS\n- Model moves epoch then branch refs in two steps (:321-331); real code uses one\n  atomic 2-ref CAS (src/merge/commit.rs:166 refs::update_refs_atomic). Model is a\n  superset (conservative) — keep or tighten, but document which.\n- Workspace `dirty` is never set true, so G4 is never exercised with dirty work.\n- Missing: CommitStateFile vs MergeStateFile (two journals), bn-38vw epoch_after\n  written before CAS (crates/maw-cli/src/workspace/merge.rs ~:5780), branch-only\n  --into CAS path (~:5843), crash during recovery.\n- Missing actors: concurrent sync / destroy / gc / auto-sync / agent file edits.\n  Real locks: epoch flock (crates/maw-cli/src/workspace/epoch_lock.rs:213; order =\n  epoch lock then workspace locks, :30-40), per-ws rebase lock (sync/lock.rs:75),\n  create lock (create_lock.rs:98). Ref writers that take NO epoch lock: recover.rs,\n  capture.rs, quarantine.rs, epoch_drift.rs, ref_gc.rs (check whether gc always holds\n  it), changes/mod.rs:1529, working_copy.rs. FF-absorb's write_epoch_current (~:3971)\n  is a plain write relying solely on the epoch lock.\n\nAPPROACH (incremental; commit after each step with model check green)\n1. Set dirty nondeterministically; add agent-edit action. Confirm G4 still holds.\n2. Add a second actor (sync or destroy) with lock acquire/release actions matching\n   real lock order; add deadlock-freedom (no reachable state where all actors wait)\n   and no-lost-commit properties.\n3. Model FF-absorb sibling advance (plan -> replay -> advance epoch -> FF siblings)\n   with crashes between steps and a concurrent agent writing files — property:\n   a sibling's committed or dirty work is never orphaned/overwritten (bn-rah2 /\n   bn-mq3b classes). Keep state space bounded (2-3 workspaces, 2 epochs).\n4. Audit the unlocked ref writers: for each, either argue in a code comment why it\n   cannot race (refs it writes are not ones merge/sync CAS), or model it and see.\n   File bug bones for real races.\n5. Un-ignore a fast subset (< ~60s) so `cargo test -p maw-assurance --features\n   stateright` runs it; add that to `just check` (or the verify workflow from the\n   gate-restoration sibling bone). Keep deep configs #[ignore] + nightly.\n6. For every property added: break the model (e.g. allow destroy without capture)\n   and confirm the checker finds a counterexample.\n\nACCEPTANCE\n- Model covers steps 1-3 with properties shown to fail under mutation.\n- Fast model check runs in the gate; unlocked-writer audit recorded in bone comment.\n","kind":"task","labels":["verification","assurance"],"parent":"bn-2ws4","size":"l","title":"Stateright: bring protocol model in line with real commit/destroy/FF-absorb and run it in CI"}	blake3:pkDjbP_C-9bSvFfUbolvyPrpfLOpItc3tfYgSp0brwA
1790464378898927	maw-lsz75n	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-3bjx	{"description":"OBJECTIVE\nMeasure which checks in the data-integrity-critical modules no test exercises.\n\nSCOPE\ncrates/maw-core/src/merge/partition.rs, crates/maw-cli/src/workspace/ff_absorb.rs\n(+ the new pure ff_plan module once extracted), crates/maw-lfs/src/pointer.rs,\ncrates/maw-cli/src/workspace/capture.rs (hidden_divergent_paths, force_rehash_paths).\n\nAPPROACH\n- `cargo mutants -p <crate> -f <file> --timeout-multiplier 2` (run per file; the\n  whole workspace is too big). cargo-mutants is installed via mise.\n- Triage each surviving mutant: equivalent mutant (note and skip), or real gap\n  (add a targeted test). Note: cargo-mutants runs cargo test, not Kani — a mutant\n  surviving in a Kani-proved function means only that no TEST catches it.\n- Run after the extraction/fix bones in this goal have landed.\n\nACCEPTANCE\n- Table of surviving mutants per file with disposition in a bone comment.\n- Real gaps closed with tests; `just check` green.\n","kind":"task","labels":["verification","testing"],"parent":"bn-2ws4","size":"m","title":"cargo-mutants pass over verified/critical modules; close surviving-mutant gaps"}	blake3:iXEmr_GjfnQ6962XYR2dITyAN9ifxPAVXFA5seZfJxk
1790464379042874	maw-lsz75n	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-7p3r	{"description":"OBJECTIVE\ncrates/maw-core/src/model/join.rs documents join as a CRDT (commutative,\nassociative, idempotent). Proptests cover commutativity, idempotence and CLEAN\nassociativity only. Associativity with conflicts present is the one property in\nmaw that needs an unbounded inductive argument over maps — the only good Verus\ncandidate found in the 2026-09-26 survey.\n\nAPPROACH (when picked up)\n- First try proptest with conflict-heavy generators; if associativity with conflicts\n  fails, that is a bug/spec question before it is a proof question.\n- Only then prototype in Verus following ../bend-playground/verus-proto/ward-lattice\n  (lattice laws as trait proof obligations, executable bodies verbatim).\n- Don't adopt Verus into the build for a single proof; keep it a side crate unless\n  more candidates appear.\n","kind":"task","labels":["verification","research"],"parent":"bn-2ws4","size":"l","title":"(Deferred) Verus: PatchSet::join associativity/commutativity including conflicts","urgency":"punt"}	blake3:3r_fK0m3uSxdHDr3X6kl5V8z6eXoJCjA1zTpsXz6xpc
