1790465261484520	maw-lsz75n	itc:AQ		item.comment	bn-86hd	{"body":"bn-86hd evidence (commit 8192e861, workspace bn-86hd).\n\nNO-DEFAULT BUILD: cargo clippy --no-default-features --all-targets -D warnings clean. Fix: build_phase.rs resolve imports made unconditional; all_equal gated on ast-merge; PathMergeStrategy allow(dead_code) under cfg(kani); kani_proofs kani-slow-only imports and helpers gated.\n\nKANI: just kani-fast green. Root: Complete - 13 successfully verified harnesses, 0 failures, 13 total (about 17s wall, warm). maw-core and maw-lfs: No proof harnesses found, exit 0 (so the per-crate lines are safe before harnesses land). kani-slow tier still codegens (cargo kani --features kani-slow --only-codegen clean); full 49 min run not executed.\n\nMUTATION: classify_shared_path step 2 (has_delete) changed to return ResolvedDelete instead of ConflictModifyDelete. kani-fast went RED: exhaustive_2_entry_decision_table FAILED (assertion failed: kinds.iter().all(is_delete)); modify_delete_always_conflicts FAILED (Any mix of delete and non-delete must be ModifyDelete conflict); Complete - 11 successfully verified harnesses, 2 failures. Reverted; green again.\n\nPROPTESTS: cargo test --lib --features proptests: 284 passed, 4 ignored. Rot fixed: determinism_tests passed a Path to build_merge_commit (now GixRepo); pushout_tests match lacked FileDirectory arm (added a justification check). 4 pushout properties (embedding_conflict_sides_complete, embedding_all_paths_accounted, minimality_conflicts_justified, full_contract) FAIL on trunk and are ignored with reason: since bn-ztu6 (f4a6e6f9) recover_diff3_atoms_with_participants stops at the first conflicting fold step, so a later workspace editing the same line is omitted from the conflict record. Minimal case: x.rs with base, ws-00/ws-01/ws-02 each rewrite the only line differently; sides are ws-00, ws-01; ws-02 missing. Needs its own bone.\n\nGATES: just check now runs nodefault-check and proptests; green (3m44s). New .github/workflows/verify.yml (actionlint clean): nodefault-check, proptests, formal-check, kani-fast (kani-verifier 0.68.0 pinned, ~/.kani cached). formal-check local-only marker removed (now wired); ci_lane_wiring test passes. NOTE formal-check runs 2 Stateright tests in 0.00s; model drift is a separate bone."}	blake3:T7tw3V5ALeRLDDe3WJKtqt0rrbylXIhGYHfOU5Gvdps
1790465345680799	maw-lsz75n	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-1lwk	{"description":"SUMMARY\nFound by the revived pushout proptests (bn-86hd). Shipped since v1.0.0-pre.10\n(bn-ztu6, commit f4a6e6f9). When 3+ workspaces edit the same region of a file, the\nconflict record lists only the first two; later workspaces are omitted entirely.\nTheir committed edit is invisible AND unselectable, so every available resolution\nsilently discards it. Prime Invariant class.\n\nEND-TO-END REPRO (confirmed 2026-09-26 with installed maw pre.15)\n  git init; printf 'line one\\n' > x.rs; commit; maw init\n  maw ws create wa|wb|wc --from main; each writes \"line <ws>\\n\" to x.rs and commits\n  maw ws merge wa wb wc --into default --message m3\n    -> cf-XXXX x.rs  Workspaces: wa, wb    (wc missing; sides/json also wa, wb only)\n  maw ws merge ... --resolve cf-XXXX=wc\n    -> Error: Workspace 'wc' is not a side in this conflict. Available: wa, wb\nScratch repo: /tmp/claude-1000/-home-bob-src-maw/1f1f33cd-6dfd-4115-ace2-f32551f65e2d/scratchpad/r3way-3082186\n\nROOT CAUSE\nsrc/merge/resolve.rs:1211 recover_diff3_atoms_with_participants folds variants\nleft-to-right and RETURNS at the first Diff3Outcome::Conflict (~:1250-1269) with\nparticipants = probe_folded_participants(ours_members) + theirs. Entries after that\nstep are never examined. bn-ztu6's intent (list only region-overlapping participants)\nis right for NON-overlapping workspaces; it must not drop overlapping ones.\n\nSECOND DEFECT, SAME FUNCTION (verify)\n`variants` is built with filter_map over e.content (skips None, e.g. deletions),\nbut the loop indexes entries[i + 1] as though variants and entries are aligned.\nAny content-less entry before the conflict shifts workspace attribution.\nCheck what callers pass (can deletions reach here? modify/delete conflicts are\nclassified earlier) and fix alignment regardless (zip entries with content).\n\nFIX DIRECTION\n- Continue past the first conflict: every remaining entry must be tested for\n  overlap against the conflicting region(s) (pairwise vs base, like the exclusion\n  probe) and included as a participant/side if it overlaps. Non-overlapping later\n  workspaces that merge cleanly should still be excluded (preserve bn-ztu6 tests).\n- Sides passed to conflict records, --resolve validation, `maw ws conflicts` JSON,\n  last-conflict, and markers materialized in the file must all include every\n  overlapping workspace.\n- Check other k-way sites for the same early-return pattern (grep resolve.rs for\n  Diff3Outcome::Conflict and `return (` in folds; also ast_merge.rs).\n\nACCEPTANCE\n- Red-first regression: unit test in resolve.rs (3 workspaces same line) + a\n  maw-cli integration test mirroring the repro that asserts wc is a listed side and\n  `--resolve cf=wc` succeeds with \"line wc\".\n- Un-ignore the 4 pushout proptests ignored by bn-86hd\n  (pushout_embedding_all_paths_accounted, pushout_embedding_conflict_sides_complete,\n  pushout_minimality_conflicts_justified, pushout_full_contract) — they must pass\n  with `cargo test --lib --features proptests`, several runs.\n- All existing bn-ztu6 participant tests still pass.\n- `just check` green. CHANGELOG note flagged for next release.\n","kind":"bug","labels":["verification","merge","data-integrity","prime-invariant"],"parent":"bn-2ws4","size":"m","title":"URGENT bug: k-way conflict omits workspaces after the first conflicting fold step — third side cannot be seen or chosen","urgency":"urgent"}	blake3:jGOcRg7ZkMFJKdUHRkhJ-Qo9fW9lnpgNXC6hByCWF3U
1790465363461838	maw-lsz75n	itc:AQ		item.move	bn-86hd	{"state":"done"}	blake3:vuuJQPtLswQ0twVdDyYtL7FW04O2MTsBKPJ7Ne51hvQ
