1790465373908259	maw-lsz75n	itc:AQ		item.assign	bn-1lwk	{"action":"assign","agent":"maw-lsz75n"}	blake3:Tnewes3gIaN3wxNRxwIfLe1Q5q15gngDVXkgiCrI1qg
1790465982307242	maw-lsz75n	itc:AQ		item.comment	bn-3ppf	{"body":"bn-3ppf MUTATION EVIDENCE (all kept as permanent gate tests in crates/maw-assurance/tests/formal_model.rs; each asserts the checker FINDS a counterexample, so a vacuous property turns the test red):\n- DestroyWithoutCapture -> \"no lost work (G1+G4)\" RED, 4 steps (destroy --force of a dirty ws).\n- NoStaleDirtyGuard (bn-mq3b) -> \"workspace coherence\" RED 13 steps and \"no silent revert\" RED 13 steps (agent commit after FF of a stale-dirty sibling drops the epoch atom).\n- RawMoveInsteadOfReplay (bn-rah2) -> \"no lost work\" RED, 6 steps.\n- GlobalFfPathsOnly (bn-p3m9) -> \"workspace coherence\" RED, 10 steps.\n- SplitCommitCas (old model shape) -> \"commit atomicity (G3)\" RED, 11 steps.\n- EpochAfterAfterCas (pre-bn-38vw) -> \"journal: refs moved => epoch_after recorded\" RED, 8 steps.\n- ReversedLockOrder (sync ws-lock-then-epoch, merge blocking ws lock) -> \"no deadlock (wait-for acyclic)\" RED, 11 steps.\n- AutoSyncNoHeadCas (pre-bn-29z8) -> \"no lost work\" RED, 5 steps; control fast_concurrent_actors_agents_anytime (faithful, agents act anytime) is GREEN.\n- SyncIgnoresDirty -> \"no lost work\" RED, 3 steps.\n- epoch monotone: residual_doctor_repair_unlocked_regresses_epoch RED (18 steps); locked control GREEN.\nSometimes-properties (merge committed, FF-absorbed, sibling FF, sibling replayed, stale-dirty skip, auto-rebase, sync, auto-sync, destroy, dirty destroy, crash recovered pre/post CAS, agent commit, doctor advance) are asserted reachable in the green configs (non-vacuity).\nProduction call: crash recovery dispatches through maw_core recovery_outcome_for_phase. Mutating it (Commit -> Terminal) did NOT turn anything red: journal clearing is data-safe in the model (refs are authoritative), so that call is fidelity only, not load-bearing. Reverted."}	blake3:aw9OL6Kc8tsLqmhowKS_g_yofOyaEfhU3LQWIxvsJqQ
1790465982340403	maw-lsz75n	itc:AQ		item.comment	bn-3ppf	{"body":"bn-3ppf UNLOCKED REF WRITER AUDIT (comments added at each site in commit 397b9319):\nSAFE: capture.rs recovery refs (create-only unique timestamped names, nobody CASes them; deleters hold the epoch lock or keep newest). recover.rs populate_from_snapshot (fresh workspace only). recover.rs cleanup_dangling_snapshots (deletes recovery refs only). working_copy.rs snapshot ref (fixed name, but both callers hold the epoch lock). ref_gc.rs (all deleting callers hold the epoch lock; dry-run read-only). changes/mod.rs update_ref_cas (true CAS vs merge --into's CAS).\nRACES:\n1. doctor --repair (epoch_drift::auto_advance_if_safe): plain write_epoch_current with NO epoch lock after re-reading the branch. A merge that FF-absorbs+commits between the re-read and the write gets undone from the epoch (epoch regresses, branch stays at the merge). Modelled: residual_doctor_repair_unlocked_regresses_epoch. Fix: take EpochLock in try_repair_epoch_drift (fast_doctor_repair_locked_is_safe shows it closes the race).\n2. FF-absorb FastForward loop (merge.rs reconcile_epoch_with_branch): holds epoch lock but not the sibling ws lock and uses the classification-time dirty snapshot; an agent edit to an FF path (or a commit) after classification is overwritten / HEAD moved off it. Modelled: residual_ff_absorb_races_concurrent_agent (7 steps).\n3. FF-absorb writes the sibling epoch ref BEFORE materialize + set_head. A crash in between (or the early-return warn paths in sync_ff_paths_in_worktree, e.g. set_head failure) leaves the epoch ref AHEAD of HEAD; status calls it current, and the next merge of that sibling diffs its stale tree against the new base and silently reverts the absorbed hunks. Modelled: residual_ff_absorb_crash_leaves_leading_epoch_ref, residual_ff_absorb_crash_then_merge_reverts (11 steps, no silent revert RED). Fix idea: write the ws epoch ref last (as sync does).\n4. bn-38vw residual: advance_merge_state(Commit) and record_epoch_after are two atomic writes; crash between leaves phase=commit, epoch_after=None (Oracle B shape). Data-safe. Modelled: residual_oracle_b_commit_phase_without_epoch_after.\n5. quarantine promote (src/merge/quarantine.rs): no epoch lock, split epoch/branch CAS; can leave refs split and can be overwritten by a concurrent FF-absorb plain epoch write. Content survives in the quarantine ws. Not modelled beyond the SplitCommitCas mutation.\n6. changes close delete_change_branch_if_requested: ancestry check then non-CAS delete; a concurrent ws merge --into the change in between is unreferenced from the branch. Narrow.\nSide finding (not a race): gc --recovery-snapshots ages recovery refs by the pinned COMMIT timestamp, so a pin made today of an old HEAD (capture.rs pin_head_only, destroy --force of a clean ws with old commits) is deleted by the next sweep."}	blake3:V2WO9DzYykFxVmmOjSF51274VH7LHkQPtTdzJfBVSkg
1790466102983626	maw-lsz75n	itc:AQ		item.move	bn-3ppf	{"state":"done"}	blake3:1y7flnPaa5L66q60JEE9Vd8IZw0fvxmjoCAt2oi09eE
1790466146008721	maw-lsz75n	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-32g8	{"description":"FOUND BY: bn-3ppf Stateright model (pinned as a residual_* test in\ncrates/maw-assurance/tests/formal_model.rs / src/model.rs — see bn-3ppf comments).\nConfirmed by reading 2026-09-26.\n\nDEFECT\ncrates/maw-cli/src/workspace/epoch_drift.rs:286 auto_advance_if_safe (called from\ncrates/maw-cli/src/doctor.rs:234 for `maw doctor --repair`) re-reads refs/heads/<branch>\nthen calls manifold_refs::write_epoch_current (plain write, :322) and write_ref for the\ndefault ws epoch ref. No epoch lock is taken by it or its caller. A `maw ws merge`\nthat commits (atomic epoch+branch CAS) between the branch re-read and the write gets\nits epoch advance overwritten with the older branch value -> epoch regresses behind\nthe branch; subsequent operations see the merge as drift.\n\nFIX\nTake the epoch lock (crates/maw-cli/src/workspace/epoch_lock.rs, same acquisition as\n`maw epoch sync` in crates/maw-cli/src/epoch.rs) around classify + re-read + write,\nand/or make the write a CAS from the classified old epoch. Re-classify under the lock.\n\nACCEPTANCE\n- The model's residual test for this race flips: model the fixed behaviour, assert\n  the property now HOLDS (and keep a mutation test showing the old behaviour fails).\n- Unit/integration test where possible (failpoint between re-read and write, if the\n  failpoints feature has a suitable hook — crates/maw-core/src/failpoints.rs).\n- just check green.\n","kind":"bug","labels":["verification","data-integrity","concurrency"],"parent":"bn-2ws4","size":"s","title":"Bug: doctor --repair auto-advance can regress the epoch (plain write, no epoch lock)"}	blake3:SDTdYxMfiiYgojbKg2j2IrhyZPMFLzyt_5Z15jobVHE
1790466146153322	maw-lsz75n	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-302v	{"description":"FOUND BY: bn-3ppf Stateright model (11-step counterexample; residual_* tests pinned\nin crates/maw-assurance). Ordering confirmed by reading 2026-09-26.\n\nDEFECT A (ordering) — crates/maw-cli/src/workspace/merge.rs ~:4017-4030, in\nreconcile_epoch_with_branch's sibling FastForward loop:\n  write_ref(workspace_epoch_ref(sibling), branch_oid)   // FIRST, failure only warned\n  sync_ff_paths_in_worktree(...)                         // THEN files + HEAD\nThe workspace epoch ref is the snapshot diff base\n(crates/maw-core/src/backend/git.rs:192 workspace_baseline_opt, and ~:613 status).\nIf the process crashes between the two, or sync_ff_paths_in_worktree takes an\nearly-return/warn path (e.g. set_head failure), the ref claims the new epoch while\nHEAD/worktree are old. The next snapshot/merge of that sibling diffs new-epoch ->\nold worktree = a revert of the absorbed epoch, which merges cleanly and silently\nreverts other workspaces' merged work. Same class as bn-rah2 / bn-mq3b.\nFix direction: write the epoch ref LAST, only after HEAD + materialization succeeded\n(as `maw ws sync` does); on any failure leave the ref at the old base so the sibling\nis merely stale (safe). Propagate failure as a warning naming the sibling + recovery\ncommand.\n\nDEFECT B (TOCTOU with agents) — the FF loop holds no per-workspace lock and uses\ndirty_paths computed at classification time. An agent edit to an absorbed path after\nclassification is overwritten by materialization; an agent commit landing in the\nwindow has HEAD moved off it. Fix direction: take the sibling's rebase lock\n(crates/maw-cli/src/workspace/sync/lock.rs, try-lock; on contention skip the sibling\nlike auto-rebase SkippedInUse), then re-check HEAD == expected and re-compute dirty\n∩ paths-to-write immediately before writing; skip (leave stale) on any change.\nAgents do not take locks, so a residual window remains — make it as small as\npossible and document it.\n\nDEPENDS ON bn-27n7 (extracts the FF-absorb classifier from this exact region) —\nstart after it merges to avoid conflicts, and reuse its pure classifier for the\nre-check.\n\nACCEPTANCE\n- Model residual tests for both races flip to must-hold; mutation tests retain the\n  old orderings as must-fail.\n- Failpoint integration test: crash/fail between ref write and HEAD move no longer\n  produces a revert on the next merge (crates/maw-cli tests with --features\n  failpoints; see Justfile failpoints recipes).\n- Existing FF-absorb regression tests (bn-p3m9, bn-mq3b, bn-2fto, bn-3gba) green.\n- just check green.\n","kind":"bug","labels":["verification","merge","data-integrity","prime-invariant","concurrency"],"parent":"bn-2ws4","size":"m","title":"Bug: FF-absorb sibling advance writes epoch ref before HEAD/files (crash or warn-path => silent revert) and races concurrent agent edits","urgency":"urgent"}	blake3:YrJACJKLR9Vo7Lq7hc7DUKOZyYkeMgXqeopRosm3CiY
1790466146303250	maw-lsz75n	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-3maj	{"description":"FOUND BY: bn-3ppf audit. Confirmed by reading 2026-09-26.\n\nDEFECT\ncrates/maw-cli/src/ref_gc.rs:241 run() computes age from get_commit_timestamp (:374,\ncommitter_time) of the commit a refs/manifold/recovery/* ref points at. For a\n`destroy --force` of a CLEAN workspace (or any pin that points at an existing\ncommit rather than a fresh snapshot commit), that commit can be months old, so the\nnext `maw gc --recovery-snapshots` deletes a recovery point created minutes ago.\nViolates the spirit of \"every destroyed workspace gets a recoverable record\".\n\nFIX\nAge by pin creation time: recovery ref names embed an ISO timestamp\n(refs/manifold/recovery/<ws>/<timestamp>, see capture.rs:48 recovery_ref and\nrecover.rs:622 parse_recovery_ref_name) and destroy records have their own timestamp\n(destroy_record.rs). Use the ref-name timestamp (fallback: record timestamp; last\nresort commit time, keep conservatively if unparseable). Update docs (module doc :16).\n\nACCEPTANCE\n- Regression test: pin a 60-day-old commit now; gc with 30-day threshold keeps it.\n- Existing gc tests green; just check green.\n","kind":"bug","labels":["data-integrity","recovery"],"parent":"bn-2ws4","size":"s","title":"Bug: gc --recovery-snapshots ages pins by the pinned commit's time, so a fresh destroy of old work is collected"}	blake3:hV7v0BnwD6yZBXhog0Y4rhe_Sx8iBI7vQFisMRMnJqc
1790466146454281	maw-lsz75n	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-3w2b	{"description":"Lower-severity findings from the bn-3ppf Stateright audit (see bn-3ppf comments for\nthe full write-up and the residual_* model tests).\n\n1. Quarantine promote (src/merge/quarantine.rs promote_quarantine) takes no epoch\n   lock and moves epoch and branch refs with two separate CAS steps. Take the epoch\n   lock and use refs::update_refs_atomic like src/merge/commit.rs:166.\n   (Coordinate with bn-1cth which is changing quarantine.rs — start after it merges.)\n2. `maw changes close` (crates/maw-cli/src/changes/mod.rs ~:1529) deletes the change\n   branch after its safety check without a CAS — use a CAS delete against the checked\n   OID.\n3. bn-38vw gap: a crash between the Commit-phase journal write and the epoch_after\n   write produces the journal shape Oracle B flags (no data loss). Either write\n   epoch_after in the same atomic journal write as the Commit phase, or teach\n   recovery/Oracle B that this shape is benign. Check crates/maw-cli/src/workspace/\n   merge.rs ~:5780 and src/merge/commit.rs.\nModel quarantine promote as a Stateright actor if cheap.\n\nACCEPTANCE: each item fixed or explicitly documented as accepted; model/residual\ntests updated; just check green.\n","kind":"task","labels":["concurrency","hardening"],"parent":"bn-2ws4","size":"s","title":"Hardening: quarantine promote epoch lock + single CAS, changes-close CAS, bn-38vw journal gap"}	blake3:-9aYK-Svd_yFjXsBC7dBftNhdLTD02lnlxHUznXrfcQ
