1790466658962521	maw-lsz75n	itc:AQ		item.comment	bn-3maj	{"body":"bn-3maj fix in workspace bn-3maj. ref_gc::run now ages recovery pins by pin creation time: ref-name timestamp (pin_created_at_from_ref_name, handles clean-/materialize-/invariant- prefixes), else latest destroy record claiming the ref, else commit time (legacy names), else keep.\nRED FIRST: with a stub returning None, 5 new tests failed (fresh_pin_of_old_commit_is_kept, fresh_prefixed_pins_of_old_commit_are_kept, old_pin_name_is_swept_even_if_commit_is_fresh, unparseable_pin_name_falls_back_to_destroy_record_time, pin_created_at_parses_known_shapes).\nMUTATIONS (all reverted): M1 commit-time-first ordering -> 4 tests FAILED incl fresh_pin_of_old_commit_is_kept. M2 drop destroy-record fallback -> unparseable_pin_name_falls_back_to_destroy_record_time FAILED. M3 parser ignores kind prefix -> fresh_prefixed_pins_of_old_commit_are_kept and pin_created_at_parses_known_shapes FAILED.\nGATES: cargo build --release -p maw-cli ok; just check exit 0, no test result FAILED."}	blake3:7zTXSzCGEKHGxR2fEcHxk64xpTauprE4CnVQ6aJKi7s
1790466692995304	maw-lsz75n	itc:AQ		item.comment	bn-1lwk	{"body":"FIXED in workspace bn-1lwk, commit ad46801c (rebased on 3631a289).\n\nFix: new kway_conflict_participants in src/merge/resolve.rs - participant iff the workspace's ORIGINAL content pairwise-conflicts (diff3 vs base) with at least one other workspace (distinct contents probed once; probe error = keep both; no conflicting pair = all members). Used by both recover_diff3_atoms_with_participants (plain path) and resolve_shared_path_with_ast (AST path, computed lazily after AST merge fails). New kway_conflict_atoms: atoms carry an edit for every participant (pairwise p0/pk atoms merged when base regions align, else one WholeFile atom with each side's full content). Alignment defect fixed: members are (workspace_id, content) pairs built together; content-less entries kept as participants and never shift attribution (unreachable from production callers today - ModifyDelete/MissingContent classify first - but fixed anyway).\n\nTests changed: bn_ztu6_three_overlapping_all_listed asserted m3 ABSENT (pinned the bug) - flipped to require [m1,m2,m3]. bn_ztu6_two_region fixture's 'disjoint' m3 edited line 7, directly ADJACENT to region b; git merge-file conflicts on that pairwise, so it was a genuine participant only hidden by the truncated fold - fixture moved to line 9 (clear context), intent kept.\n\nRed-first: 5 new unit tests in resolve.rs mod bn_1lwk_tests (4 red on trunk: three_workspaces_same_line_all_listed, interleaved_second_region_pair_all_listed, late_overlapping_listed_disjoint_excluded, content_less_entry_does_not_shift_attribution; participants_order_independent passes on trunk and is a guard). Plus ast_items_three_way_same_fn_all_listed. Tests run plain, ast all_languages, ast default config. New CLI test tests/kway_conflict_sides_bn_1lwk.rs: snapshot sides, ws conflicts JSON sides + every atom has wc, --resolve cf=wc publishes 'line wc'.\n\nMutation evidence (all reverted, file restored from saved copy, grep MUTANT = 0):\nM1 early-return in pairwise loop after first conflicting pair (mimics old fold): 4 bn_1lwk unit tests FAILED; CLI test FAILED 'left: [wa, wb] right: [wa, wb, wc]'; pushout_embedding_conflict_sides_complete FAILED 'Conflict on a.rs: sides {ws-00} != expected {ws-00, ws-01}'.\nM2 reintroduce misalignment (zip entries with filter_map'd contents): content_less_entry_does_not_shift_attribution FAILED 'd must be a participant; got [a-del, b, c]'.\nM3 minimality removed (always return all members): 7 FAILED incl. bn_ztu6 disjoint-exclusion tests (plain + AST) and participants_order_independent.\n\nGates: cargo test --lib --features proptests pushout x3 (16 passed each, ~110s); just check exit 0 (fmt, clippy, nodefault-check, test, proptests, dst-fast, contract-drift; no FAILED); cargo test --lib --no-default-features bn_1lwk/bn_ztu6 10 passed.\n\nOut of scope, pre-existing (confirmed with installed pre.15, 2-way): atom-level resolve drops the newline at the end of a line atom - base l1/l2/l3, wa and wb edit l2, --resolve cf-X.0=wb yields 'l1\\nwbl3\\n'. parse_diff3_atoms joins lines with no trailing newline while resolve_atoms replaces a newline-inclusive byte range. Silent content corruption; needs its own bone."}	blake3:8-KP51SdwTE9dhbvKgG9o_IO8foIKv2dbidFwFAyWGs
1790466734372752	maw-lsz75n	itc:AQ		item.move	bn-3maj	{"state":"done"}	blake3:f24GI0XellOzUpO6skocoKhdJG1e7Q2VfRa46qnaFvo
1790466753108928	maw-lsz75n	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-34zv	{"description":"FOUND BY: bn-1lwk worker; reproduced by lead 2026-09-26 with installed maw pre.15.\n\nREPRO\n  base f.txt = \"l1\\nl2\\nl3\\n\"; ws wa writes \"l1\\nwal2\\nl3\\n\", ws wb \"l1\\nwbl2\\nl3\\n\"\n  maw ws merge wa wb --into default --message m      -> cf-XXXX (atom cf-XXXX.0)\n  maw ws merge wa wb --into default --message m --resolve cf-XXXX.0=wb\n  -> [OK] merged; f.txt = \"l1\\nwbl2l3\\n\"   (expected \"l1\\nwbl2\\nl3\\n\")\nWhole-file resolution (cf-XXXX=wb) is NOT affected.\nScratch repro dir: /tmp/claude-1000/-home-bob-src-maw/1f1f33cd-6dfd-4115-ace2-f32551f65e2d/scratchpad/atomnl-*\n\nROOT CAUSE (per worker; verify)\nparse_diff3_atoms (src/merge/resolve.rs) stores each side's edit text without its\nfinal newline; resolve_atoms (grep for it — atom resolution splice) replaces a line\nrange that includes the newline with that text.\n\nFIX / VERIFY\n- Red-first unit test on the splice + CLI integration test mirroring the repro.\n- Property test (proptest, in the style of src/merge/pushout_tests.rs or resolve.rs\n  tests): for random base/two-side line edits producing one conflict, resolving\n  every atom to side S yields exactly S's file content, for both sides — the\n  invariant that would have caught this. Include files without trailing newline,\n  CRLF lines, empty regions (pure deletions) and multi-atom files.\n- Check other consumers of atom edit text (maw ws resolve --keep on atoms,\n  resolve_structured.rs, conflicts JSON `atoms[].edits`) for the same assumption.\n- Mutation-check the property. CHANGELOG Unreleased note.\n- Coordinate: bn-1lwk (k-way participants, touches parse_diff3_atoms callers and adds\n  kway_conflict_atoms) is merging just before this starts; base on trunk after it.\n","kind":"bug","labels":["merge","data-integrity","conflicts"],"parent":"bn-2ws4","size":"s","title":"URGENT bug: atom-level --resolve cf-X.N=<ws> drops the region's trailing newline, silently joining lines","urgency":"urgent"}	blake3:7feIVSj0i6rilqSCw_LXQgS3mRZO1uQKMnBg_U2PW5Q
1790466793880109	maw-lsz75n	itc:AQ		item.move	bn-1lwk	{"state":"done"}	blake3:VhMjfIMHbsBXQTRM1f3ICsV380Qq6B2I-hwWJc4-iE0
1790466882579891	maw-lsz75n	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-28os	{"description":"FOUND BY: lead while reviewing bn-1lwk, 2026-09-26. Reproduces on shipped pre.15\nAND on trunk after bn-1lwk (c0b8b9bf). Present since bn-ztu6 (pre.10), which made\nconflict records list only region-overlapping participants.\n\nREPRO\n  base f.txt = l1..l7 (one per line)\n  wa: line1 -> A1      wb: line1 -> B1      wc: line7 -> C7 (disjoint)\n  maw ws merge wa wb wc --into default --message m\n    -> cf-XXXX f.txt  Workspaces: wa, wb   (wc correctly NOT a participant)\n  maw ws merge wa wb wc --into default --message m --resolve cf-XXXX=wa\n    -> [OK] merged wa, wb, wc ; f.txt = A1 l2 l3 l4 l5 l6 l7   <- C7 LOST\nThe output claims wc was merged; wc's committed edit is silently absent. wc was\nnever shown to the user as involved in the conflict, so there was no informed\nchoice. Scratch repros: scratchpad/disj-*, disj2-*.\n\nEXPECTED\nChoosing side S for a conflict must yield: S's resolution of the conflicting\nregions, PLUS every non-participant workspace's clean edits to that file. I.e.\nresolution content = clean diff3 fold of S's content with each non-participant's\ncontent (non-participants are pairwise-clean with everyone by definition, but the\nfold can still conflict; if it does, fall back to treating them as participants,\nnever to dropping them).\nAlso consider atom-level resolution (cf-X.N=S) and --resolve-all=S, `maw ws resolve\n--keep`, and `ID=content:PATH` (user-supplied content: arguably user's\nresponsibility, but warn if non-participant hunks are absent).\n\nALSO IN SCOPE (same code area, do sequentially in the same workspace)\nbn-34zv atom-level resolve drops trailing newline — take both bones in one\nworkspace to avoid conflicting edits to src/merge/resolve.rs; commit separately.\n\nVERIFY\n- Red-first CLI regression mirroring the repro (tests/, like\n  tests/kway_conflict_sides_bn_1lwk.rs from bn-1lwk).\n- Property (proptest): for random k-way (k<=4) line edits over a small base, for\n  every conflict and every chosen participant S, the resolved file contains every\n  non-participant's edited lines, and equals diff3-fold(S, non-participants...)\n  when that fold is clean. Pair it with the existing pushout proptests\n  (src/merge/pushout_tests.rs) — consider adding an \"embedding after resolution\"\n  property there, which is the invariant both this and bn-34zv violate.\n- Mutation-check. CHANGELOG Unreleased entry.\n","kind":"bug","labels":["merge","data-integrity","prime-invariant","conflicts"],"parent":"bn-2ws4","size":"m","title":"URGENT bug: whole-file --resolve cf-X=<ws> discards a non-participant workspace's disjoint edit to the same file","urgency":"urgent"}	blake3:AUHHxfUIGkjl4W0bpxEpky13HiXg3SJnjFAI5UmIKP8
