1790466934396349	maw-lsz75n	itc:AQ		item.comment	bn-32g8	{"body":"bn-32g8 FIX (workspace bn-32g8, commit 7bd8b3d3). auto_advance_if_safe (epoch_drift.rs) now: takes EpochLock (label \"doctor --repair\", configured wait policy) around classify+write; classifies via classify_drift_with_oids so the write uses the exact epoch/branch OIDs the FF-safety predicate judged (no branch re-read); writes the epoch with advance_epoch CAS (classified epoch -> classified branch). CasMismatch -> error \"epoch moved concurrently ... nothing written\", doctor shows it as a warn row. Default-ws epoch ref write stays plain but is now under the lock. New failpoint FP_DOCTOR_ADVANCE_BEFORE_WRITE between classify and write.\nTESTS + MUTATION EVIDENCE:\n1. auto_advance_takes_epoch_lock_and_writes_nothing_when_busy (default build): test holds the epoch lock, repair with no-wait must return EpochLockBusy and leave epoch untouched. Mutation: lock acquisition disabled -> RED: \"repair must not proceed while the epoch lock is held: Advanced { ... }\". Reverted.\n2. auto_advance_never_regresses_epoch_past_concurrent_merge (--features failpoints, runs in just sg1-faithful-test): callback on the failpoint lands a merge commit M (branch+epoch) between classify and write; epoch must stay at M. Mutation: CAS replaced by plain write_epoch_current -> RED: \"repair must detect the concurrent epoch move: Advanced { ... }\". Reverted.\n3. Stateright model: ProcSpec::DoctorRepair is now the fixed protocol (lock + CAS from classified epoch). fast_doctor_repair_vs_merge GREEN incl. sometimes merge committed / FF-absorbed / doctor advanced. Old behaviour is Mutation::DoctorRepairUnlocked; mutation_pre_bn_32g8_doctor_repair_unlocked_regresses_epoch finds \"epoch monotone\" counterexample (18 steps). Replaces residual_doctor_repair_unlocked_regresses_epoch / fast_doctor_repair_locked_is_safe.\nSide note: in the model, CAS alone (lock removed) also keeps epoch monotone green; the lock additionally makes classification consistent with the write.\nGATES: just check exit 0 (99 test-result ok lines, no FAILED); cargo clippy -p maw-cli --features failpoints --all-targets -D warnings clean; cargo clippy -p maw-assurance --features stateright --all-targets -D warnings clean; maw-assurance lib+formal_model green."}	blake3:MzE2Outq9ck_rw3_j0fC1Uz4O92I-l_S1aUK66fTFB8
