1790467842970321	maw-lsz75n	itc:AQ		item.comment	bn-2jml	{"body":"bn-2jml worker report (workspace bn-2jml, commit 67533833).\n\nEND-TO-END EFFECT BEFORE FIX (reproduced with installed maw pre.15): w1+w2 add file a, w3+w4 add a/b. maw ws merge exits 0 with OK, 2 shared paths, 2 resolved. main advances to a commit whose root tree holds BOTH \"100644 blob a\" and \"040000 tree a\". git fsck --strict: duplicateEntries. Default-workspace checkout fails (IO error while changing filetype), leaving root HEAD on the old epoch while main moved. The invariant check still reports OK. Verdict: a bad tree committed to the branch, not a build failure and not a silent drop.\nAFTER FIX: the merge refuses with 1 D/F conflict naming w1..w4, and main does not move. --resolve-all=w1 lands a valid tree containing only file a.\n\nFIX: partition.rs detect_df_clashes does one sorted scan over all non-deletion entries, unique and shared, using component-normalised byte keys. It emits every (file, dir-child) pair. resolve.rs FileDirectory conflict sides now list all file-side and dir-side workspaces.\n\nMUTATION EVIDENCE (each reverted afterwards):\nM0 is the real pre-fix detector spliced back in. partition_df_clash_shared_file_vs_shared_dir_child goes RED (left [] right [(a, a/b)]). The prop_df_clash_iff_component_prefix proptest goes RED. The CLI test merge_refuses_shared_file_vs_shared_dir_child_clash goes RED (merge must refuse). The root pushout_resolved_upserts_are_tree_shaped proptest goes RED (resolved upserts src and src/lib.rs cannot coexist in one tree).\nM1 drops the shared rows from detection. The partition prop goes RED (left {} right {(a, a/a)}). The root tree-shape prop goes RED (src vs src/src).\nM2 drops the slash from the dir prefix. The partition prop goes RED (left {(a, a)}).\nM3 drops the deletion filter. The partition prop goes RED (left {(b, b/a)} right {}).\n\nKANI: tried 2 bounded harnesses, one on partition_by_path with 3 changes and one on detect_df_clashes with 2 paths and at most 2 entries. Both hit the 580s timeout (PathBuf component parsing, sort and BTreeMap are not CBMC-friendly). Dropped, nothing committed.\n\nOUT-OF-SCOPE DEFECT FOUND: resolve.rs recover_diff3_atoms_with_participants (bn-ztu6) stops at the first pairwise conflict. So in a k>=3 diff3 conflict, later workspaces that overlap the same region are dropped from sides. Repro: base l1/l2/l3, and 3 workspaces rewrite line 1 to A, B and C; sides come out as [ws-a, ws-b]. The pushout oracles have a narrow labelled carve-out, known_k_way_diff3_sides_gap, to remove once that is fixed."}	blake3:0Q8oP8FTl8qAW_f9H9vv5gsIY9lBbHX8wGS_xZGXvSQ
1790468270416603	maw-lsz75n	itc:AQ		item.comment	bn-27n7	{"body":"bn-27n7 evidence (workspace bn-27n7, commit 4b1a7ad9).\n\nExtracted to crates/maw-core/src/merge/ff_plan.rs: paths_conflict (now a component-prefix walk, component_prefix_either), stale_dirty_filter(_by), split_own_delta(_by), classify_sibling (lazy probe + stale closures), absorb_verdict. merge.rs reconcile_epoch_with_branch, ff_dirty_stale_conflict and sync_ff_paths_in_worktree call them. ff_absorb::paths_conflict is a re-export.\n\nKani harnesses (crates/maw-core/src/merge/ff_plan_kani.rs), all SUCCESSFUL, cargo kani -p maw-core total ~100s:\n1 component_prefix_either_matches_prefix_spec_le_3_comps\n2 stale_dirty_filter_known_delta_any_relation_le_3_delta_le_2_dirty\n3 stale_dirty_filter_unknown_delta_fails_closed_le_2_dirty\n4 split_own_delta_partitions_any_relation_le_3_delta_le_2_dirty\n5 classify_sibling_safety_exhaustive\n6 classify_unreadable_dirty_never_fast_forwards_le_2_dirty\n7 absorb_verdict_blocks_all_or_nothing_le_3_siblings\n\nMutations (each applied, harness went RED, reverted; restore verified):\nM1 Ahead arm disabled (Ahead treated as FF) -> 5 RED: assertion failed: !matches!(head, SiblingHead::Ahead)\nM2 stale result ignored -> 5 RED: assertion failed: !(dirty && stale)\nM3 None delta returns empty (fail open) -> 3 RED: got.as_slice() == dirty ; and 6 RED: d == Ok(SiblingDecision::SkipStaleDirty)\nM4 stale filter any->all -> 2 RED: got == expected\nM5 component prefix -> exact equality only (the pre.14 dir/file bug) -> 1 RED: got == a.starts_with(b) || b.starts_with(a)\nM6 split refreshes dirty-conflicting paths -> 4 RED: refresh == exp_refresh\nM7 verdict proceeds with a single blocker -> 7 RED: blockers == 0\nM8 probe run before base==branch check -> 5 RED: probe_calls.get() == u8::from(!base_is_branch)\nPath layer: paths_conflict mutated to left == right -> unit test paths_conflict_exhaustive_le_3_comps_matches_legacy_and_spec RED (a vs a/a).\n\nWhy the path harnesses use generic cores: Kani over std Path parsing with symbolic bytes did not finish in 300-580s even for a 6-entry table (a concrete pair takes 5s). So the Kani harnesses verify the *_by cores and component_prefix_either (which the PathBuf wrappers call) for every conflict relation over ids 0..3, and an exhaustive unit test covers all 24336 path pairs of <=3 components over {a,b,ab} in plain, doubled-slash, trailing-slash and leading ./ spellings, checking equality with the legacy expression (all spellings) and with the component-prefix spec (git-normalised spellings). Leading ./ is NOT normalised (./a vs a do not conflict); documented as a precondition, inputs come from maw-git tree diffs and status.\n\nDeviation from bone text: the stale filter returns delta paths (result is a subset of own-delta, not of dirty), matching production. A CLEAN sibling with unreadable HEAD is still FastForward (historic behaviour kept for byte-identity); see final report."}	blake3:FlgsyVM_7ALXyDELnjv-ntnzcqAFlmlB5ltNq4Zzias
1790468586955388	maw-lsz75n	itc:AQ		item.comment	bn-2jml	{"body":"Follow-up commit 994a29df. The workspace is synced onto trunk; the only conflict was the proptest seed file, kept as the union in 13110df9. The known_k_way_diff3_sides_gap tolerance is removed and the pushout checks pass at full strength on top of bn-1lwk. Trunk's weaker duplicate FileDirectory arm is removed, and D/F sides must now be a superset of the workspaces touching the file path. New build_tree guard: FileDirectoryClash plus DuplicateTreeEntry. Mutation A disabled the shape check: the tests went RED (expected FileDirectoryClash, got DuplicateTreeEntry, so the second layer still refused). Mutation B disabled both checks: RED, because build returned a commit OID for a tree holding both a and a/b. For the resolve-all fix, the mutation that restored the old suggestion list went RED (Try: w1, w2, w4 or content:PATH). All three mutations were reverted."}	blake3:BNYQ9Ji5vxnCkWAdck213JizE0X5E_dEzk7C3C1lyAw
1790468611730350	maw-lsz75n	itc:AQ		item.comment	bn-3w2b	{"body":"bn-3w2b DONE in workspace bn-3w2b, commit fce6d130.\n1. quarantine promote: maw merge promote holds EpochLock for the whole promote; promote_quarantine refuses (QuarantineError::MergeInProgress) while a non-terminal merge-state.json exists; epoch+branch move in ONE refs::update_refs_atomic CAS.\n2. changes close: new GitRepo::delete_ref_cas (gix Change::Delete MustExistAndMatch); delete_change_branch_if_requested CAS-deletes against the checked branch_oid; DeleteReferenceMustExist now classified as RefConflict.\n3. bn-38vw gap: MergeStateFile::advance_to_commit sets phase=Commit and epoch_after in one mutation; merge.rs enter_commit_phase persists it with a single write_atomic (replaces advance_merge_state(Commit)+record_epoch_after).\nMODEL: new ProcSpec::QuarantinePromote actor; P_COMMIT_ATOMIC extended to the quarantine candidate; residual_oracle_b_commit_phase_without_epoch_after became green fast_oracle_b_strict; new green fast_quarantine_promote_vs_merge.\nMUTATION EVIDENCE (all reverted except the permanent must-fail tests):\n- Model Mutation::SplitCommitJournal (pre-fix two journal writes) -> mutation_pre_bn_3w2b_split_commit_journal_breaks_oracle_b finds Oracle B counterexample (permanent test).\n- Model Mutation::QuarantinePromoteUnlockedSplitCas -> P_COMMIT_ATOMIC and P_EPOCH_MONOTONE counterexamples (two permanent tests).\n- Model: dropping the promote merge-state refusal -> fast_quarantine_promote_vs_merge RED: Unexpected crash recovery converges counterexample, 10 steps (merge crashes in COMMIT pre-CAS, promote advances epoch, --abort refuses). This is how the refusal was discovered.\n- Model: dropping only the promote epoch lock (keeping atomic CAS) -> stays GREEN; the lock is defense-in-depth in the model because the model check+CAS step is atomic; in real code the lock is what makes the merge-state check and FF-absorb plain epoch write safe.\n- Prod: promote_quarantine reverted to advance_epoch + write_ref_cas and merge-state check disabled -> promote_branch_moved_leaves_both_refs_untouched RED (epoch must NOT advance when the branch CAS cannot succeed) and promote_refuses_while_merge_state_in_progress RED.\n- Prod: delete_ref_cas replaced by plain delete_ref -> delete_ref_cas_only_deletes_expected_value RED.\n- Prod: advance_to_commit without setting epoch_after -> advance_to_commit_records_epoch_after_atomically RED.\nGATES: cargo build --release -p maw-cli OK; just check exit 0 (incl formal-fast); cargo test -p maw-git -p maw-assurance exit 0."}	blake3:onleQYFdBgTIvd_2HFKUdAzgOGhbyelhg-2C1PZuZAE
