1790468642960291	maw-lsz75n	itc:AQ		item.comment	bn-2wav	{"body":"bn-2wav evidence (workspace bn-2wav, commit 864d19b1).\nApproach: lexical cores extracted to maw_core::model::path_safety. Kani proves them over a component-kind enum (LexComp) and byte slices (fast: 1-30s each, under 1GB). Real std::path::Path production functions are proven by exhaustive enumeration in unit tests over every path of <= 4 segments from {a, ab, ., .., empty}, rooted or not (complete proof for that bound). Kani over std Path was not attempted given the bn-1cth experience.\nHarnesses (all green): Kani contained_relative_is_strictly_inside_le_6_comps, show_path_accepts_iff_no_traversal_le_7_bytes, path_under_is_segment_prefix_le_6_bytes. Exhaustive tests: maw-core path_safety tests (3), maw-cli recover exhaustive_restore_destination_le_4_segments and exhaustive_validate_show_path_le_4_segments, undo exhaustive_ensure_safe_relative_path_le_4_segments plus regression remove_added_paths_refuses_workspace_root, capture exhaustive_path_is_under_excluded_le_3_segments.\nMutations (each reverted after, tree verified identical):\nM1 is_contained_relative returns true instead of saw_normal: Kani FAILED (assertion failed: depth >= 1); maw-core exhaustive FAILED; maw-cli restore, undo exhaustive and undo regression FAILED.\nM2 ParentDir treated like CurDir: Kani FAILED (assertion failed: !escaped, depth >= 1, !has_bad).\nM3 traversal check length 2 changed to 3: Kani FAILED (validate_show_path_bytes(b).is_ok() == spec); maw-core exhaustive_show_path FAILED.\nM4 path_bytes_under segment length check relaxed to prefix match (the a vs ab bug): Kani FAILED (path_bytes_under(p, d) == spec); maw-core exhaustive FAILED.\nM5 undo reverted to old predicate (reject only ParentDir/RootDir): undo exhaustive + regression FAILED.\nM6 capture reverted to plain string starts_with: capture exhaustive FAILED.\nM7 restore lexical check replaced by empty-only check: recover exhaustive_restore_destination FAILED.\nFindings: undo ensure_safe_relative_path accepted empty, dot and ./ paths which join to the workspace root; remove_added_paths would remove_dir_all the whole workspace. Latent (git diff never emits such paths); fixed and regression-tested. capture path_is_under_excluded made segment-wise (old string version was only correct for canonical paths without repeated slashes). No bug in the restore/show validators.\nOut of scope: workspace::path_is_within canonicalises via the OS."}	blake3:Cue2w6GsI1zJanlT5BsFOLT6kninsWy1QstefB6hXOY
1790468706834873	maw-lsz75n	itc:AQ		item.move	bn-27n7	{"state":"done"}	blake3:t4BgBmW5jRDFEE5LsOOh7iSWd54qGYCtIDYusvlzZRM
1790468790983362	maw-lsz75n	itc:AQ		item.comment	bn-34zv	{"body":"FIXED in workspace bn-28os, commit 597671c9 (not merged).\n\nRoot cause wider than reported: the CLI atom splice (crates/maw-cli/src/workspace/merge.rs resolve_atoms) rebuilt the file from the BASE: (1) region text from parse_diff3_atoms lacked its trailing newline -> lines joined; (2) the base line number was counted from merged-output context lines, so it was wrong whenever a clean edit earlier in the file changed the line count -> text spliced at the wrong place; (3) every clean edit outside the atoms (from either participant) was reverted to base.\n\nFix: new src/merge/apply_resolution.rs resolve_record_atoms. It re-runs the detecting diff3(base, p0, pk) merges and replaces each conflict block with the chosen side's section, byte-exact (EOF-without-newline and CRLF handled by stripping git's synthetic EOL on an EOF block). k-way per-pair results are folded with diff3; residual conflict = refused (FoldConflict), never dropped. AST byte-range atoms keep the old splice (AST merge is off by default; clean edits outside AST atoms are still not re-applied - known limitation). parse_diff3_atoms display text is unchanged (display only now; its line numbers are still approximate).\n\nTests: red-first CLI tests/atom_resolve_newline_bn_34zv.rs (3 tests: trailing newline both sides; clean edits + line-shift outside region; mixed per-atom choices with missing final EOL) - all 3 RED before fix (e.g. left l1 wbl2l3, right l1 wbl2 l3). Property tests src/merge/resolution_choice_tests.rs (wired into just proptests): random line edits, CRLF, missing final newline, deletions, inserts, k=2..4, both plain and AST-config merge paths; oracle = git merge-file -p --ours/--theirs (exact, 2 participants) plus absorption (re-merge with --ours is a no-op).\n\nMutations (each reverted): (a) drop strip_synthetic_eol calls -> RED: all atoms -> ws-0 must equal git merge-file --ours, left b0 w0r1 b2 with EOL, right without. (b) pop trailing newline from chosen block text (the original bug) -> RED: left w0r0b1, right w0r0 newline b1.\n\nGates: cargo build --release -p maw-cli OK; just check EXIT 0, no test result FAILED."}	blake3:hX3scGJn9OJcKo0vYWUgEQN3YkXxKuKupjAbYfjmQck
1790468791022616	maw-lsz75n	itc:AQ		item.comment	bn-28os	{"body":"FIXED in workspace bn-28os, commit 40985bba (on top of bn-34zv 597671c9; not merged).\n\nFix: ConflictRecord gains bystanders: Vec of ConflictSide (content-bearing workspaces that changed the path but are not participants). Populated by conflict_record_with_bystanders on the plain diff3 path, the AST-conflict path and the AST diff3 fallback. Every workspace-choice resolution folds bystanders back in with diff3: file-level and --resolve-all via apply_resolution::resolve_record_to_side, atom-level via resolve_record_atoms (fold_bystanders tail). A residual fold conflict is refused (merge aborted), never dropped. Engine side: resolvable_participants widens kway_conflict_participants - a bystander that cannot be folded into some participant's content is promoted to a participant (fixpoint). content:PATH: WARNING on stderr naming bystanders whose edit the user content omits (bystanders_missing_from).\n\nTests: red-first CLI tests/resolve_keeps_bystander_edits_bn_28os.rs - file-level (both sides), atom-level, --resolve-all all RED before fix (left A1..l7, right A1..C7); plus content: warning test. Unit merge::resolve::tests::unfoldable_bystander_is_promoted_to_participant uses a case found by random search (repetitive lines a/b/a/b/a/c: s, t conflict; n1, n2 pairwise clean with all, but s+n1+n2 fold conflicts). Property tests in merge::resolution_choice_tests now also assert: every changed workspace is exactly one of side/bystander; file-level and atom-level resolution to every side absorbs every bystander; file-level with no bystanders equals the side exactly.\n\nMutations (each reverted): (a) fold_bystanders returns chosen unchanged -> proptest RED: file-level resolve to ws-0 dropped bystander ws-2 (left w2r0 b1 w0r2, right b0 b1 w0r2). (b) disable the widening loop -> unit test RED: a bystander must be promoted: [ws-s, ws-t]. Note: the proptest generator alone does NOT hit the widening case (mutation (b) stayed green there), hence the searched unit case.\n\nGates: cargo build --release -p maw-cli OK; just check EXIT 0, 102 test-result-ok lines, no FAILED."}	blake3:JW1S-pYRQzMsroBhUEmTzb7VfQGkswwkO69-VwCkXGQ
1790469131004193	maw-lsz75n	itc:AQ		item.move	bn-2jml	{"state":"done"}	blake3:kMvjXrx3m8jUueUd_-2kviiN7nsnRL1VSc3TGDr59rY
1790469143812642	maw-lsz75n	itc:AQ		item.comment	bn-z9t3	{"body":"bn-z9t3 evidence (workspace bn-z9t3, commit 7a8c3dfa)\n\nSPEC DECISION. Oracle used: git-lfs 3.8.0 'git lfs pointer --check [--strict]' on hand-built inputs, plus the spec. Policy: maw accept set must be a SUBSET of git-lfs --check (no false positives vs git-lfs) and a SUPERSET of what git-lfs writes. Findings from git-lfs itself:\n- git-lfs --check ACCEPTS but --strict rejects: size +5, size 05, size -0, trailing space after size, empty lines, missing final LF, CRLF, ext line after oid, unsorted ext lines, hawser version URL, size 0 (strict only). maw rejects all of these except size 0 (kept: --check accepts it and maw wrote it before).\n- git-lfs REJECTS but old maw ACCEPTED (real false-positive gaps, now fixed): size before oid, any non-extension unknown key (e.g. 'extra value-x'), extension value that is not sha256:<hex>, duplicate extension priority, any line after size, size above i64::MAX (git-lfs uses int64; old maw accepted u64::MAX).\n- Extension keys: ext-<digit>-<name>, name starts with [A-Za-z0-9_] then [A-Za-z0-9_.-]; git-lfs --strict accepts ext-0-Foo_x so uppercase/underscore are allowed.\nResult: parse/write is a bijection on the accept set. write() now returns Result and refuses pointers with no canonical encoding (size above i64::MAX, bad/out-of-order extension keys, keys oid/size/version or containing space/newline in extensions, over 1024 bytes).\n\nHEX DEDUP. pointer.rs, store.rs, batch.rs nibble codecs replaced by crate::hex (nibble_value, nibble_char, encode_oid, decode_oid with HexCase). Side fix: batch hex_to_oid used str slicing and u8::from_str_radix, so a server oid with multibyte UTF-8 panicked and '+f' was accepted. maw-git types.rs hex_digit left alone (git SHA-1 oids, deliberately case-lenient, and maw-git only optionally depends on maw-lfs).\n\nRELATED FIX (same false-positive class). maw-git lfs_clean.rs used looks_like_pointer (prefix sniff) to decide content is already a pointer and store it raw. git-lfs clean only passes through content that decodes as a pointer. Now uses Pointer::parse. Regression test near_pointer_content_is_cleaned_not_passed_through: RED with the old sniff (assertion left != right failed: near-pointer content was stored raw), green with the fix.\n\nKANI (cargo kani -p maw-lfs, 6 harnesses, all SUCCESSFUL, about 95s total). Each mutated, RED, reverted:\n- hex_nibble_char_then_value_all_256_bytes: mutation nibble_char letters b'a'+n-9 -> FAILED: nibble_value(c, HexCase::LowerOnly) == Some(n & 0x0f)\n- hex_nibble_value_exact_domain_all_256_bytes: mutation LowerOnly accepts A-F -> FAILED: lower_or_digit || (upper && case == HexCase::AnyCase)\n- envelope_ok_implies_sniffer_le_48_bytes: mutation sniffer requires len > version line -> FAILED: looks_like_pointer(bytes); mutation parse version check relaxed to starts_with https:// -> FAILED: looks_like_pointer(bytes)\n- size_parse_then_format_identity_le_6_bytes: mutation accept leading + -> FAILED: out.as_slice() == value; mutation accept leading zeros -> same failure\n- size_format_then_parse_identity_lt_1e6: mutation push_decimal pads to 2 digits -> FAILED: parse_size(&out) == Some(n)\n- size_format_then_parse_near_i64_max: mutation drop i64::MAX cap -> FAILED: parse_size(&out) == expected\nAll harnesses have kani::cover checks where relevant (SATISFIED).\nBounds and what did not scale: whole Pointer::parse on a symbolic 44-byte version line plus concrete oid/size tail did not finish in 7.5 min; full-u64 symbolic push_decimal did not finish in 10 min. So Kani proves the envelope (version line/size/ASCII/LF checks, which parse calls first) and the size field; whole-pointer properties are proptests. To make the envelope tractable: ParseError::UnsupportedVersion.found is now Vec<u8> (String collect on symbolic bytes blew up symex from 5s to over 250s), and is_ascii/contains replaced by one byte loop.\n\nPROPTEST (crates/maw-lfs/tests/pointer_proptest.rs, 7 tests, about 2s):\n- write_then_parse_is_identity (2048 cases), parse_accepts_only_canonical_and_sniffer_agrees (near-pointers: canonical pointers with 1-3 byte/line edits; asserts sniffer, spec line-structure oracle, and write(parse(b)) == b), parse_never_panics_on_arbitrary_bytes, differential_maw_accepts_subset_of_git_lfs and differential_maw_writes_git_lfs_strict_pointers (skip if git-lfs missing), git_lfs_lenient_forms_maw_rejects (documents the deliberate gap, asserts git-lfs --check accepts and --strict rejects each), near_pointer_generator_is_not_vacuous (2000 samples: 55 accepted, 1945 rejected).\nMutations (each RED then reverted): size accepts + -> canonical property and lenient-forms test FAILED; leading zeros -> same; empty lines skipped -> canonical property FAILED; any key accepted as extension -> canonical property FAILED via spec oracle; sniffer len < 200 -> write_then_parse and canonical FAILED; version check relaxed -> canonical, differential and lenient-forms FAILED; write emits 'oid  ' -> write_then_parse, canonical, differential-strict FAILED; LowerOnly accepts uppercase -> canonical FAILED.\nEquivalent mutant found: the explicit 'nothing after size' check was unreachable (after size, oid is set so ext lines are rejected and oid/size/version are duplicates). Removed it and documented why.\n\nGATES: cargo test -p maw-lfs green; cargo test -p maw-git green; cargo clippy -p maw-lfs -p maw-git --all-targets --all-features -D warnings clean; cargo build --release -p maw-cli ok; just check green (exit 0, no FAILED)."}	blake3:JWOul-PXnj92accC-9qhcdi_aLhFfGOS4ueRSrLNNU0
1790469499457336	maw-lsz75n	itc:AQ		item.move	bn-2wav	{"state":"done"}	blake3:t0OlgNzBw3Oar4P8NfjcFwlnXedibFZEcI_lfkJH7oc
1790469910314180	maw-lsz75n	itc:AQ		item.move	bn-z9t3	{"state":"done"}	blake3:Jhtnw2-jo5Ot1wKVHN856SG3mV2XWRTeYcXSZl6rBJM
1790470304584037	maw-lsz75n	itc:AQ		item.comment	bn-ila3	{"body":"bn-ila3 DONE in workspace bn-3w2b (commits d2f787c9, 4f9718de on top of trunk 402a05a2). All three items verified as real before fixing.\n1. validate-tmp: VERIFIED (hardcoded root/.manifold/validate-tmp). Now validate_worktree_dir() = LayoutFlavor::manifold_dir()/validate-tmp. Test validate_phase_consolidated_layout_creates_no_root_manifold_dir; mutation (restore hardcoded path) RED: left .manifold/validate-tmp vs right .maw/manifold/validate-tmp.\n2. [merge.validation] in .maw.toml: VERIFIED silently ignored (MawConfig has no validation field, no deny_unknown_fields). Precedence chosen: explicit [merge.validation] in the manifold config.toml wins (long-standing location, compat); else .maw.toml; else defaults. ManifoldConfig::load_layered warns on a shadowed .maw.toml [merge.validation] and on any other .maw.toml [merge] key maw ignores (drivers, append_only, ...). Wired into ws merge VALIDATE, --plan/--check config, and merge promote. Unit tests layered_* in maw-core config.rs; e2e maw_toml_validation_is_honored_without_stray_root_manifold_dir. Mutation (VALIDATE call site back to ManifoldConfig::load) RED: .maw.toml [merge.validation] must run and block the merge.\n3. quarantine as sibling: VERIFIED both paths. Auto-rebase ran on it (rebased clean 0 commits + bogus Fix: maw ws sync merge-quarantine-... hint); FF-absorb REPLAYED it (HEAD moved off the candidate, epoch ref written). Fix: auto-rebase skips merge-quarantine-* (SiblingResult::SkippedQuarantine, JSON skipped_quarantine); reconcile_epoch_with_branch and classify_post_prepare_divergence skip quarantines (bn-27n7 had merged, so the region was free). Tests unrelated_merge_leaves_quarantine_candidate_untouched and ff_absorb_does_not_replay_quarantine_sibling. Mutations: disable auto-rebase skip -> RED (auto-rebase must skip the quarantine); FF test RED before the merge.rs fix (FF-absorb moved the quarantine candidate).\nNOTE on the bone's expectation 'promote must still work after an unrelated merge': by design it cannot. The quarantine candidate is built on epoch_before and promote CASes from it; any later merge moves the epoch, so promote now refuses with both refs untouched and the quarantine intact (asserted in the test). Rebasing a quarantine onto a newer epoch would be a new feature.\nGATES: cargo build --release -p maw-cli OK; just check exit 0; cargo test -p maw-core -p maw-git -p maw-assurance --features maw-assurance/stateright exit 0."}	blake3:okmA9YJmfq9W-vNIbE2VXeoHS9cNQIVzIQVqO8jngiQ
