1790472426649937	maw-lsz75n	itc:AQ		item.comment	bn-2l63	{"body":"bn-2l63 Kani evidence (workspace bn-2l63, commits 11bde97c + 67528dc3). cargo kani -p maw-core: 11/11 harnesses verified (10 new + bn-1cth), 112s total.\n\nMutation checks (each applied, harness went RED, then reverted from backup):\nm1 merge_state.rs Complete gets edge to Aborted -> merge_phase_table_terminal_sinks_forward_edges_all_pairs FAILED: assertion failed: p.valid_transitions().is_empty()\nm2 Cleanup => [Aborted] only -> merge_phase_every_live_phase_reaches_complete_and_aborted FAILED: assertion failed: reach[rank(Complete)]\nm3 Commit => [Cleanup] only (drop Commit->Aborted) -> recovery_outcome_consistent_with_transition_table_all_phases FAILED: assertion failed: p.can_transition_to(Aborted) (CheckCommit arm)\nm4 abort() terminal guard narrowed to Complete only -> merge_state_advance_and_abort_follow_table_all_pairs FAILED: assertion failed: ab.is_ok() == p.can_transition_to(Aborted)\nm5 reserved compare against b\"epoch-delt\" -> create_rejects_exactly_epoch_delta_names_le_12_bytes FAILED: assertion failed: !create_ok\nm6 seq = last_seq + 1 (original code) -> seq_gen_successive_seqs_strictly_increase_any_state FAILED: next_with_clock attempt to add with overflow\nm6b seq = last_seq.saturating_add(1) -> same harness FAILED: assertion failed: s1 > last_seq\nm7 Ord compares seq reversed -> seq_gen_successive_keys_strictly_increase_fixed_ids FAILED: assertion failed: k1 < k2\nm8 PartialEq also compares wall_clock_ms -> ordering_key_eq_ord_consistent_4_id_shapes FAILED: assertion failed: a == b == (ord == Equal)\nm9 hex DIGITS ends ee instead of ef -> file_id_hex_round_trip_all_u128 FAILED: decode(encode(n)) == Ok(n)\nm10 decode also accepts A-F -> file_id_decode_accepts_only_canonical_hex_le_33_bytes FAILED: encode(n) == b\n\nCommit->Aborted decision: KEPT and documented at the transition. Phase is persisted as commit BEFORE the ref CAS; all aborts from Commit (branch-divergence preflight, failed CAS, recover_partial_commit NotCommitted) happen while refs are provably not at the candidate, and crash recovery CheckCommit needs exactly this edge (m3 proves the dependency). Point of no return = successful CAS; after that abort_merge_state refuses (Prime-Invariant gate).\n\nepoch-delta decision: collision was real (duplicate side ids in partition/resolve, --resolve path=epoch-delta ambiguous, real ws shown as epoch (previous merge)). Reserved at creation (WorkspaceId::new_for_create, used by ws create and ws attach); new/FromStr/serde still parse it because the synthetic side, AST edit attribution and --resolve targets round-trip through them. BUILD refuses with BuildPhaseError::ReservedWorkspaceId if a legacy source named epoch-delta is merged while the synthetic side is injected (regression test stale_merge_refuses_source_named_epoch_delta)."}	blake3:NjvDxIXoGTmL9GQ4GlU_b2NsZeXimHwOXkr02v9x9Ks
1790473118330089	maw-lsz75n	itc:AQ		item.move	bn-2l63	{"state":"done"}	blake3:VKEgIncrN_vBoZvhlNQ2J5BOCWJHG8sWSSaYQuju-OU
1790473139272314	maw-lsz75n	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-1u93	{"description":"OBSERVED 2026-09-26 by lead: tests/concurrent_create.rs\nconcurrent_different_name_creates_all_succeed_in_parallel failed once under heavy\nmachine load (passes 12/12 in isolation, on trunk and branch):\n  Error: Failed to create workspace: `worktree add` failed: git backend error: failed\n  to acquire git index lock for worktree 'c': No such file or directory (os error 2)\n  at path \".../.git/worktrees/c/index.lock\"\nReal user-facing race: parallel agents creating distinct workspaces (the normal\nmulti-agent startup pattern) can fail spuriously.\n\nLIKELY CAUSE (verify)\ncrates/maw-git/src/worktree_impl.rs index-lock acquisition (~:44, bn-2mio retry with\nexponential backoff) only retries typed AcquireLock contention; ENOENT on the\nper-worktree admin dir means the lock is attempted before .git/worktrees/<name>/\nexists, or the dir was pruned/raced by a concurrent `git worktree prune`/create\n(check whether another create's prune step removes in-progress admin dirs — maw calls\n`worktree prune`; a prune racing a half-created worktree would delete its admin dir).\n\nFIX\nFind the real ordering bug first (a prune racing create would be a correctness bug,\nnot just a retry issue). Make create robust: create the admin dir before locking, or\nnever prune while holding/without the create lock, and retry ENOENT on the lock path\na bounded number of times. Stress test: N=16 parallel distinct creates x 20\niterations, all succeed.\n","kind":"bug","labels":["concurrency","workspace"],"parent":"bn-2ws4","size":"s","title":"Bug: concurrent maw ws create can fail with ENOENT on .git/worktrees/<name>/index.lock (no retry)"}	blake3:vjplRHAwsH9lk9jWpFsQJ0L21i5bNcF6mv7Mn5FutOg
1790473139520517	maw-lsz75n	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-2xqt	{"description":"OBSERVED 2026-09-26 during a loaded `just check`: src/merge/validate.rs:1003 panicked\n\"validation descendant remained live after parent exit: Some('R')\". Test added by\nbn-15tj (commit 2482d0b9). It reads /proc/<pid>/stat immediately after validation\nreturns and requires the descendant to be gone or zombie; on a loaded machine the\nSIGKILLed process can still be 'R' for a moment. Poll with a deadline (e.g. up to 2s,\n10ms steps) before asserting. Confirm the production code actually kills the process\ngroup (the property under test) — don't weaken it to \"eventually\" if production\nrelies on synchronous reaping.\n","kind":"bug","labels":["testing","flaky"],"parent":"bn-2ws4","size":"xs","title":"Flaky test: validate_success_does_not_wait_for_descendant_held_pipes asserts killed descendant already dead"}	blake3:mJgbumweFZnGqSyuSB2PT4kr5AzhwdGSWfbT4-TgNU8
1790473139779825	maw-lsz75n	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-s8ti	{"description":"From bn-2l63 (2026-09-26): crates/maw-core/src/merge_state.rs valid_transitions still\nallows Cleanup -> Aborted, but no code takes it; aborting after the ref CAS succeeded\nwould label committed work as aborted. Remove the edge, update the Kani harnesses\nadded by bn-2l63 (terminal/reachability/recovery consistency) and the Stateright model\nif it mirrors the table; mutation-check that re-adding it is caught by some check (add\nan explicit \"no transition to Aborted after the CAS phase\" harness).\n","kind":"task","labels":["verification","hardening"],"parent":"bn-2ws4","size":"xs","title":"MergePhase table: Cleanup -> Aborted edge is unused and unsafe (would mislabel committed work)"}	blake3:-gbUoAQvI18RQVX8Kzo84dFmx4GQE34FMQ8tdCwjNpc
