1790473155648088	maw-lsz75n	itc:AQ		item.assign	bn-s8ti	{"action":"assign","agent":"maw-lsz75n"}	blake3:QvQ0yQVZnbicxKGDapKtDFRR2GYP_EBA9rsOSmSdosU
1790473211602167	maw-lsz75n	itc:AQ		item.comment	bn-302v	{"body":"bn-302v evidence (workspace bn-302v, commit 2798d0a8; no file overlap with trunk's newer bn-2l63 commit).\n\nFIX\nA: FF sibling loop order is now lock+recheck -> materialize -> HEAD CAS -> epoch ref (last). Failure before the HEAD move leaves the ref at its old base and prints \"left stale (NOT fast-forwarded) ... run: maw ws sync <ws>\". Ref-write failure after the HEAD move warns (ref behind HEAD = safe direction).\nB: WorkspaceRebaseLock try-lock per FF sibling (held -> skip \"in use\"), classify_sibling re-run on fresh HEAD + dirty facts (stale delta = own HEAD..target delta plus ff_paths), fresh dirty set used for materialization, HEAD moved by new maw-git set_head_detached_cas (creates HEAD.lock O_EXCL, re-reads, writes lock, renames; a foreign HEAD.lock is never removed). Residual window documented in merge.rs: agent file write between re-check and a path's write, or a HEAD writer that bypasses HEAD.lock.\nC: classify_sibling: Unreadable HEAD -> new SiblingDecision::SkipUnreadableHead (clean or dirty); stale closure only for AtBase+dirty.\nD: auto_advance_if_safe refuses (AutoAdvanceSkip::MergeInProgress, doctor prints warn + maw ws merge --abort) while merge-state.json is non-terminal; unreadable journal = error (fail closed).\nD2 (found by the model, same class): reconcile_epoch_with_branch runs BEFORE PREPARE's journal check, so ws merge FF-absorbed a trunk commit under a crashed COMMIT journal and --abort then refused forever. Now refuses when the journal is in commit/cleanup phase.\n\nRED FIRST (old code + failpoint sites only, cargo test -p maw-cli --features failpoints --test ff_absorb_sibling_order_bn_302v): 5/5 FAILED, e.g.\n- crash_before_materialize...: \"epoch ref 1a2f9232 is not an ancestor of HEAD 658d4a4b (epoch ref ahead of HEAD: next merge would revert)\"\n- agent_edit_after_classification_is_never_overwritten: \"the agent's post-classification edit was overwritten by FF-absorb\"\n- held_sibling_rebase_lock_skips_ff_advance: \"FF-absorb moved HEAD of a sibling whose rebase lock is held\"\n- materialize_failure...: epoch ref != old base\nEnd-to-end manual repro on old binary (abort before materialize, then agent commit + merge of the sibling): main:f2.txt = f2-base, i.e. the trunk commit was silently reverted.\nff_absorb_refuses_under_crashed_commit_journal... RED before the D2 guard: \"Absorbed 1 upstream commit(s) into epoch\" then \"PREPARE: merge already in progress (phase: commit)\".\nAfter fix: 6/6 green.\n\nMUTATIONS (applied, RED, reverted)\nKani C: Unreadable folded back into the AtBase arm -> classify_sibling_safety_exhaustive FAILED (\"assertion failed: matches!(head, SiblingHead::AtBase)\", \"stale_calls.get() == u8::from(expect_stale_call)\"); classify_unreadable_head_or_tree_never_fast_forwards_le_2_dirty FAILED (\"d == Ok(SiblingDecision::SkipUnreadableHead)\"). Restored: cargo kani -p maw-core 11/11 SUCCESSFUL.\nDoctor unit test: guard disabled via .filter(|_| false) -> auto_advance_refuses_while_unfinished_merge_journal_exists FAILED (\"must refuse under an unfinished merge journal, got Advanced\").\nStateright (crates/maw-assurance/tests/formal_model.rs): residual_* flipped to fast_ff_absorb_agents_anytime / fast_ff_absorb_crash_in_loop / fast_ff_absorb_crash_then_merge_sibling (green) + fast_doctor_repair_vs_crashed_merge (green); old shapes kept as must-fail: mutation_pre_bn_302v_ff_no_sibling_lock_loses_agent_work (P_NO_LOST_WORK), mutation_pre_bn_302v_ff_ref_before_head_breaks_coherence (P_WS_COHERENT), ..._then_merge_reverts (P_NO_SILENT_REVERT), mutation_pre_bn_302v_doctor_ignores_merge_journal_strands_recovery and mutation_pre_bn_302v_ff_absorb_ignores_merge_journal_strands_recovery (P_RECOVERY_CONVERGES). Ad-hoc: re-check reading the classification dirty mask -> fast_ff_absorb_agents_anytime RED (no lost work, 6 steps). NoStaleDirtyGuard now also disables the re-check's stale part (same production classify_sibling), keeping the bn-mq3b mutations RED. 32 passed, 1 ignored.\nHonest gaps: removing only the HEAD CAS or only the sibling try-lock does NOT turn the model red (the model's loss property is content based and an orphaned agent commit's atoms stay in the worktree; no model actor holds the ws lock across the FF window). Those two are covered by maw-git unit tests (CAS refuses on moved HEAD, keeps a foreign HEAD.lock, real git commit refuses while HEAD.lock is held) and the held-lock CLI test.\n\nGATES\njust check (TMPDIR=/var/tmp/bn-302v): exit 0, 106 test-result ok lines, no FAILED.\nFF-absorb suites before/after: 187/187 both (merge_ff_absorb 40, epoch_sync_default_baseline 25, sync_ff_hidden_divergence_bn_154g 27, destroy_hidden_divergence_bn_2k9e 29, materialize_verify_bn_3gba root 27, trunk_dirty_preserve_bn_1xmk 28, ff_absorb_stale_sibling_cli 5, materialize_verify_stat_cache_bn_3gba 3, failpoints materialize_verify_bn_3gba 3).\nmaw-git 127 passed; maw-assurance --features stateright,oracles 152 passed; clippy -D warnings default + failpoints + assurance stateright clean.\njust sg1-faithful-test: integration all green; lib has a PRE-EXISTING parallel flake (sync_fp_auto_sync_before_checkout_aborts_cleanly arms the global FP_AUTO_SYNC_BEFORE_CHECKOUT with no serialization, racing sync_succeeds_for_clean_fast_forward / sync_proceeds_when_expected_head_matches); lib is 693/693 with --test-threads=1. Not touched here."}	blake3:RyVvWM0bKMYe9PTz3fK4DCgvwyYxs87u7qz-8sxwJbg
1790473664176254	maw-lsz75n	itc:AQ		item.move	bn-302v	{"state":"done"}	blake3:ZqsqPvV_-56DWn__sbvmDdObAioELXp6OACz-axTF1Y
1790473738988467	maw-lsz75n	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-1svi	{"description":"FOUND BY: bn-302v worker 2026-09-26. `just sg1-faithful-test` --lib fails 2 tests\nunder parallel runs, 693/693 with --test-threads=1. Cause (per worker; verify):\ncrates/maw-cli/src/workspace/sync/checks.rs test\nsync_fp_auto_sync_before_checkout_aborts_cleanly sets the process-global\nFP_AUTO_SYNC_BEFORE_CHECKOUT failpoint (registry: crates/maw-core/src/failpoints.rs,\nLazyLock<Mutex<HashMap>>) without serialization, so concurrently-running tests that\nreach that site hit it. Fix: scope failpoints to the test thread (bn-32g8 used a\nthread-checking callback for its failpoint) or serialize failpoint-using tests via a\nshared test mutex/guard; audit other lib tests that set failpoints the same way.\nAcceptance: sg1-faithful-test --lib passes 5 consecutive parallel runs.\n","kind":"bug","labels":["testing","flaky"],"parent":"bn-2ws4","size":"xs","title":"Flaky failpoints lib tests: sync_fp_auto_sync_before_checkout_aborts_cleanly sets a global failpoint without serialization"}	blake3:o2RPWxghmWkjPYje7oTW-_z_ww9lHWyqWPKESgkW_YM
1790473753493872	maw-lsz75n	itc:AQ		item.move	bn-2dyz	{"state":"doing"}	blake3:FwgjPDxc9zw2yRz3BFILGke5ajCdkH9xO3P8-ElSQ8A
1790473753504578	maw-lsz75n	itc:AQ		item.assign	bn-2dyz	{"action":"assign","agent":"maw-lsz75n"}	blake3:7wYLtae7oBKGmkAr00n4Ub1Wz_w2h5VOCMmdAxxcEoU
1790473753537098	maw-lsz75n	itc:AQ		item.move	bn-1svi	{"state":"doing"}	blake3:09q-C8le7o-r_H0wgq9_3bbnr2P2llxRRmCvuehcWNk
1790473753561342	maw-lsz75n	itc:AQ		item.assign	bn-1svi	{"action":"assign","agent":"maw-lsz75n"}	blake3:u11tM1jFXu3omLL2eaPHYCqVl0e_jarY6nj9YNI5fog
1790474615765075	maw-lsz75n	itc:AQ		item.comment	bn-1u93	{"body":"ROOT CAUSE (confirmed, commit 935f778a in ws bn-1u93): worktree_add wrote admin/gitdir (old step 4) before creating the worktree dir (step 5). Every maw ws create/destroy runs worktree_prune first; a prune landing in that window saw gitdir naming a non-existent .git whose worktree root also did not exist, judged the admin dir stale and deleted it; the create then failed writing admin/index -> ENOENT on index.lock. Not an index-lock contention issue, so a retry would not help (admin dir is gone for good). Second, smaller window found by mutation: fs::write truncates gitdir first, so prune could read an EMPTY path and also judge it stale.\nFIX: (1) admin/locked = 'initializing' written right after mkdir, removed by a Drop guard on every exit path; maw worktree_prune skips locked dirs (git worktree prune already does). (2) worktree dir + .git file created BEFORE gitdir; gitdir written tmp+rename; prune skips empty gitdir. (3) ENOENT message names the vanished admin dir.\nEVIDENCE: unit worktree_add_survives_concurrent_prune_stress (pruner thread vs 60 adds): pre-fix RED 32 of 60 failed with the exact field error. Mutation: prune ignores locked (reorder but non-atomic gitdir) -> RED 1 of 60 (torn read), which led to the atomic write; with atomic write, reorder alone also holds. prune_spares_locked_in_progress_admin_dir (maw prune + real git worktree prune) RED when locked check removed. worktree_add_removes_initializing_lock_on_success_and_failure RED when Drop guard does not remove. CLI tests/concurrent_create.rs concurrent_distinct_creates_stress_with_barrier (16 x 20, env MAW_CREATE_STRESS_N/ITERS): built maw with trunk worktree_impl.rs -> RED at iteration 0 with 'failed to acquire git index lock for worktree s0-2: No such file or directory'; green with fix. All mutations reverted."}	blake3:ctB8L8zoAKhtcVoA3kZSQVNgoYHkmW4Eg67R_v0RW80
1790474615800794	maw-lsz75n	itc:AQ		item.comment	bn-2xqt	{"body":"Commit 455bb59c. Production (kill_command_tree) sends SIGKILL to the whole process group via kill -KILL -- -pgid and returns; kill(2) is async and the orphaned descendant is reaped by init/subreaper, so no synchronous-death guarantee exists and none is relied on (pipe drain has its own 2s bound). Both descendant tests now poll /proc/pid/stat up to 2s (10ms steps) for gone-or-zombie. Mutation: commented out kill_command_tree in the success path -> RED 'validation descendant remained live after parent exit: Some(S)'; reverted."}	blake3:7rkbtxO0epK3n8tq-GIyAP4e3ReeJZXSzR6fptIotL0
1790474615832462	maw-lsz75n	itc:AQ		item.comment	bn-s8ti	{"body":"Commit d0c580df. Removed Cleanup -> Aborted from valid_transitions. Also found MergeStateFile::abort ignored the table (only checked is_terminal), so it would still have taken the edge; abort now refuses whenever Aborted is not a legal edge. All call sites of abort_merge in maw-cli merge.rs precede advance to Cleanup, so no behavior change. Kani: terminal-sinks harness now requires abort only for rank <= Commit; reachability harness asserts Aborted reachable iff start is pre-CAS; new harness no_transition_to_aborted_after_commit_phase_all_phases (table + abort() refusal leaves state untouched). Stateright model does not mirror the table (no Aborted journal phase; uses recovery_outcome_for_phase, unchanged) - no change needed. Mutation M1 re-add edge: new harness FAILED, reachability FAILED, unit cleanup_cannot_abort FAILED. Mutation M2 abort back to is_terminal check: new harness FAILED, merge_state_advance_and_abort_follow_table_all_pairs FAILED. Reverted. cargo kani -p maw-core: 22/22 verified. formal-fast green inside just check."}	blake3:45WSbb_b3WM5u_ZGIbJnlgccVfbtfP9BDnPSizEdbz8
1790474810574442	maw-lsz75n	itc:AQ		item.comment	bn-3bjx	{"body":"cargo-mutants 27.1.0 pass (workspace bn-3bjx, commit 870a7228). Runs used TMPDIR=/var/tmp/bn-3bjx (the first runs under /tmp/claude-1000 hit EDQUOT and were discarded), --timeout-multiplier 2 --jobs 4. Test scope per file: maw-core and maw-lfs full crate tests; root crate src/merge/apply_resolution.rs with --features proptests and lib tests filtered to merge::resolution_choice_tests, merge::resolve::, merge::apply_resolution (full root lib tests take 116 s per mutant); maw-cli capture.rs with lib tests filtered to workspace::capture::. path_safety.rs ran with -E kani_proofs (cfg(kani) code is not compiled under cargo test). Timeouts count as caught (the mutant made the loop infinite).\n\nBEFORE -> AFTER (missed / total)\npartition.rs 2/33 -> 1/33 | build.rs 13/39 -> 1/39 | path_safety.rs (excluding kani) 4/73 -> 0 | pointer.rs 22/116 -> 1/116 | hex.rs 1/48 -> 1/48 | apply_resolution.rs 19/88 -> 1/88 | capture.rs 16/76 -> 10/76 (all 10 triaged below)\n\nSURVIVORS AND DISPOSITIONS\npartition.rs:382 < to <= in detect_df_clashes (partition_point) | EQUIVALENT: path_key never ends in a slash, so no row key equals the probe P/ and the partition point does not change.\npartition.rs:394 && to || in detect_df_clashes | REAL GAP, closed: new test partition_df_clash_reports_first_differing_workspace_pair (the documented rule is first differing ws pair; the mutant let a later pair overwrite it).\nbuild.rs:173 Error::source -> None | REAL GAP (minor), closed: build_error_io_exposes_source.\nbuild.rs:349 == to != in walk_tree_recursive | REAL GAP, closed: build_preserves_nested_epoch_files_and_gitlinks. Every build test used a flat epoch, so dropping the path prefix of nested epoch files was never seen.\nbuild.rs:527 delete the 160000 arm in build_tree | REAL GAP, closed by the same test: a gitlink in the epoch was rewritten as a blob-mode entry.\nbuild.rs:419/420/424/431x3/439x3 git_tree_entry_cmp | NO END-TO-END EFFECT (maw-git write_tree sorts entries canonically again). Closed anyway with direct unit test git_tree_entry_cmp_matches_git_canonical_order.\nbuild.rs:494 || to && in build_tree dir collection | EQUIVALENT: it only lets duplicate dir paths into all_dirs. Rebuilding one dir gives the same tree OID in a HashMap, so the output tree is the same (performance only).\npath_safety.rs:91 Display -> Ok(default) | REAL GAP (message), closed: show_path_error_display_messages.\npath_safety.rs:134 path[start+1] to path[start*1] | REAL GAP, closed: exhaustive alphabet now includes .a. The mutant rejected the segment .x as traversal.\npath_safety.rs:188 < to == / > in path_bytes_under | REAL GAP, closed: exhaustive alphabet now includes b (same length as a). The mutant skipped the byte compare, so path_is_under(b/x, a) returned true.\npointer.rs:133 delete the version arm in the duplicate check | REAL GAP (error variant), closed: repeated_version_line_is_duplicate_key.\npointer.rs:197 > to >= in validate | REAL GAP, closed: write_accepts_max_size_rejects_above (size i64::MAX must encode).\npointer.rs:237, 240 x13, 245 x2, 247, 248 encoded_len/decimal_len | REAL GAP, closed: encoded_len_matches_written_length (every decimal width 0..i64::MAX, 0 to 2 extensions). The TooLarge guard depends on encoded_len being exact.\npointer.rs:294 > to >= in check_envelope | REAL GAP, closed: max_pointer_bytes_boundary_is_inclusive (1024 bytes parses; 1025 is TooLarge on both parse and validate).\npointer.rs:362 - to + in extension_priority | EQUIVALENT: priority is only compared relatively. Adding 48 keeps the order and cannot overflow (max 105).\nhex.rs:63 | to ^ in decode_oid | EQUIVALENT: hi<<4 and lo have disjoint bits.\napply_resolution.rs:70 Display -> Ok(default) | REAL GAP (message), closed: tests::display_messages.\napply_resolution.rs:259 guard -> true/false in resolve_record_to_side | REAL GAP (Prime Invariant), closed: resolve_to_deleting_side_respects_bystanders. With the true mutant, choosing a deleting side silently dropped a bystander's edit.\napply_resolution.rs:269 bystander_names x2 | REAL GAP (message), closed by the same test.\napply_resolution.rs:325 x3, 335 bystanders_missing_from | REAL GAP (this function had no unit test), closed: bystanders_missing_from_reports_exactly_the_missing_ones.\napply_resolution.rs:365 == to != (whole-file shortcut) | REAL GAP, closed: single_whole_file_atom_takes_the_sides_bytes (non-UTF-8 side bytes, not the lossy atom text).\napply_resolution.rs:402 || to && | REAL GAP, closed: line_atoms_refuse_when_a_side_deleted_the_file. The mutant silently ignored a deleting third side.\napply_resolution.rs:511 x3, 532 x3, 541 splice_region_atoms | REAL GAP (AST splice had no test; the proptests never produce AST atoms for f.txt), closed: splice_region_atoms_places_each_choice (out-of-order atoms, gap, adjacent ranges, overlap refusal, per-atom choice).\napply_resolution.rs:487 acc == r guard -> false | EQUIVALENT: diff3(base, acc, acc) is Clean(acc). The guard is a shortcut only.\ncapture.rs:72 materialize_recovery_ref x2 | REAL GAP, closed: materialize_recovery_ref_format.\ncapture.rs:436 capture_before_materialize_repair -> Ok(None) | REAL GAP, closed: capture_before_materialize_repair_pins_full_tree_snapshot.\ncapture.rs:275 delete ! (fail-closed rehash filter), 293 tracked_files x2 | REAL GAP (the fail-closed widening path had no test), closed: hidden_divergent_paths_fail_closed_widens_rehash_to_other_tracked_files. The test makes the detector's git add -A fail with an unreadable untracked file and skips when run as root.\ncapture.rs:542 initialize_temporary_index -> Ok(()) | EQUIVALENT FOR READERS: checked by hand in a scratch repo. Without the HEAD seed, only the stash's index parent (W^2) lacks the untouched files. The main snapshot tree, which is what recover reads, is identical.\ncapture.rs:168 delete ! (warning gate) | OUTSIDE LIB SCOPE, covered: a manual mutation turned tests/destroy_hidden_divergence_bn_2k9e.rs RED (force_destroy_keeps_masked_bytes_alongside_visible_dirt at :288, merge_destroy_snapshots_stat_masked_stale_bytes at :337). Reverted.\ncapture.rs:315 warn_hidden_divergence -> () | stderr only; the same integration test asserts WARNING_MARKER.\ncapture.rs:324 x2 (> to == / >=) | COSMETIC: this only changes the \"...and N more\" line when exactly 5 paths are shown. Not asserted.\ncapture.rs:465 empty_snapshot_error x2 | error text on a branch that needs git stash create to return nothing for non-empty input. Not asserted.\ncapture.rs:812 warn_on_reset_failure -> () | stderr diagnostic only.\ncapture.rs:974 emit_recovery_surface -> () | OUTSIDE LIB SCOPE, covered: a manual mutation turned tests/recovery_contract.rs RED (4 tests). Reverted.\ncapture.rs:1009 emit_recovery_surface_failed -> () | stderr contract on the capture-failure path. Not checked by an integration test.\n\nNo survivor revealed a production bug. No production code was changed.\nGates: cargo build --release -p maw-cli OK; just check OK (105 test-result lines, 0 FAILED); cargo test -p maw-lfs OK."}	blake3:uGDgww25gHBRcbBq9Kd5OS569d_Ij0cw5hEYmZXw32U
1790474930248864	maw-lsz75n	itc:AQ		item.comment	bn-2dyz	{"body":"bn-2dyz done in workspace bn-2dyz, commit bc2f5d8d (not merged).\n1 CONFIG SPLIT (confirmed): merge build/--check read .maw/manifold/config.toml; get_backend, FF-absorb reconcile (auto_absorb_ff), sibling auto-rebase (auto_rebase_siblings), rebase/resolve sanity config and git_compat_refs read .maw/config.toml via LayoutFlavor::bootstrap_config_path. Fix: bootstrap_config_path removed; LayoutFlavor::manifold_config_path is canonical (manifold_dir/config.toml, both layouts); legacy_manifold_config_path = .maw/config.toml (consolidated only). ManifoldConfig::load_for_root / load_for_manifold_dir / load_with_legacy adopt legacy-only [merge]/[workspace] keys with a deprecation warning; canonical wins on conflict (warn); invalid legacy ignored (warn). All readers routed through it; cli prints warnings once per process.\nRegression: tests/consolidated_leftovers_bn_2dyz.rs canonical_manifold_config_auto_absorb_ff_false_is_honored_by_merge. Mutation: reconcile call site reverted to load root/.maw/config.toml -> RED (merge must refuse (FF-absorb disabled), got success). Reverted -> green. Control test default_config_ff_absorbs; legacy test legacy_bootstrap_setting_is_honored_with_deprecation_warning.\n2 QUARANTINES (confirmed: ws list showed (ready to merge) + Merge ready: maw ws merge merge-quarantine-ID --destroy; ws status gave Fix: maw ws merge ... --check; sync --all errored on it). Fix: list/status show quarantine + promote/abandon (JSON fix_command maw merge promote ID); refuse_quarantine_operand in ws merge/--check/--plan and ws sync (text+json); sync --all and exec auto-sync skip. Tests ws_list_shows_quarantine_with_promote_abandon_not_merge_ready, ws_sync_and_merge_refuse_quarantine_and_leave_it_untouched + list unit test. Mutation: neutering refuse_quarantine_operand, sync is_quarantine and list quarantine_id -> both RED; neutering only the sync skip -> RED (sync --all failed for 1 workspace). Note: in this repro a manual ws sync of a quarantine was already refused by the orphan guard (HEAD has commits not in target epoch history), so the old failure mode was a confusing refusal rather than a rebase.\n3 collect.rs fileids now via LayoutFlavor manifold_dir. Unit test collect_reads_fileids_from_consolidated_manifold_dir; mutation back to root/.manifold/fileids -> RED (left: None, right: Some(FileId(...))).\nGates: cargo build --release -p maw-cli ok; just fmt-check clippy nodefault-check ok; just test ok (0 FAILED); just proptests dst-fast formal-fast contract-drift ok; cargo test -p maw-core -p maw-assurance ok."}	blake3:jEZLUFL0bnlTGSq0QxYN5Gi7meopuezPvrLmUCkvOZQ
