1790475623759634	maw-lsz75n	itc:AQ		item.comment	bn-1svi	{"body":"bn-1svi done in workspace bn-2dyz, commit a8ccc693 (not merged).\nCause confirmed: sync_fp_auto_sync_before_checkout_aborts_cleanly armed the process-global FP_AUTO_SYNC_BEFORE_CHECKOUT (Error) while sibling lib tests ran sync_worktree_to_epoch in parallel; victims were sync_proceeds_when_expected_head_matches and sync_succeeds_for_clean_fast_forward. Audit: the bn-2byw FP_REBASE_BEFORE_SETHEAD callback test in sync/rebase.rs was also unscoped (epoch_drift test already thread-checks its callback; failpoints.rs own tests hold TEST_REGISTRY_LOCK).\nFix: maw_core::failpoints::set_for_this_thread(name, action) -> ThreadFailpointGuard: thread-local registry consulted by check() before the global one, disarmed on guard drop (also on panic). Both tests migrated. check() now clones the action and releases the lock before running it (a Panic action used to poison the global mutex).\nEvidence: new unit test thread_scoped_failpoint_fires_only_on_arming_thread. Mutation: set_for_this_thread writes the GLOBAL registry (old behavior) -> unit test RED (must not fire on another thread; left Err(scoped) right Ok) and cargo test -p maw-cli --features failpoints --lib failed 16 of 30 parallel runs (sync_proceeds_when_expected_head_matches, once also sync_succeeds_for_clean_fast_forward). Reverted -> 30 of 30 parallel runs green (694 passed each).\nGates: just sg1-faithful-test ok; cargo build --release -p maw-cli ok; just fmt-check clippy nodefault-check ok; clippy with failpoints features ok; just test ok (one earlier run hit an unrelated flake in tests/concurrent_create.rs concurrent_different_name_creates_all_succeed_in_parallel, index.lock ENOENT during concurrent worktree add; 10 reruns green, full rerun green; that is the bn-1u93 area); just proptests dst-fast formal-fast contract-drift ok; cargo test -p maw-core ok."}	blake3:b-qAbvkonlw3BLBGBudaRngx5-JfgCX52aiXybApMRo
