1790529331709593	maw-68q58s	itc:AQ		item.comment	bn-3rhz	{"body":"FINDING 1 (FIXED, data loss) src/merge/quarantine.rs commit_quarantine_edits (promote path). An agent that fixes a quarantine with git commit leaves a clean worktree; commit_quarantine_edits saw no edits and returned the ORIGINAL candidate. Validation ran on the fixed worktree, the UNFIXED candidate was promoted to epoch+main, and the best-effort abandon_quarantine then deleted the worktree holding the only ref to the fix (no recovery pin). Repro: test promote_uses_commits_made_in_quarantine (commit fix.txt in the quarantine, promote) - pre-fix: left aad5f832 (candidate) != right 24048f91 (fix). Fix: promote builds on the quarantine HEAD, which must be the candidate or descend from it (else QuarantineError::Git, refs untouched; test promote_refuses_head_not_descending_from_candidate). Also the CAS-failure message that tells the user to run maw merge abandon now names the quarantine commit and how to keep it. Mutations: return candidate again -> promote_uses_commits_made_in_quarantine RED; ancestry check disabled -> promote_refuses_head_not_descending_from_candidate RED. Both reverted. Commit da333444."}	blake3:iUVxrB7vKmNz6ULPISsa0KEoeYvOVBasgPE_2S3reiE
1790529331755891	maw-68q58s	itc:AQ		item.comment	bn-3rhz	{"body":"FINDING 2 (FIXED, crash-safety / repo wedge) crates/maw-cli/src/workspace/merge.rs reconcile_epoch_with_branch (bn-302v journal refusal). FF-absorb refused only under Commit/Cleanup journals, but abort_merge_state's epoch-drift gate refuses to clear ANY non-terminal journal once the epoch moved off epoch_before, and PREPARE only auto-takes-over a pre-COMMIT journal whose owner is provably dead. A crashed BUILD/VALIDATE merge whose pid is reused (Live) or on a host without /proc (Indeterminate) + a direct trunk commit: next ws merge FF-absorbed (epoch moved), PREPARE refused and printed run maw ws merge --abort, and --abort then refused forever. Repro: test ff_absorb_refuses_under_crashed_build_journal_and_recovery_converges (FP_BUILD_AFTER_MERGE_COMPUTE=abort, journal owner_pid set to 1) - pre-fix output: Absorbed 1 upstream commit(s) ... Error: PREPARE: merge already in progress (phase: build, owned by a running process); epoch assert RED. Fix: FF-absorb proceeds under a non-terminal journal only if it is pre-COMMIT and staleness()==Orphaned (exactly what PREPARE takes over). Control test ff_absorb_proceeds_under_provably_orphaned_build_journal keeps the auto-recovery. Mutations: taken_over = pre_commit || orphaned -> build-journal + commit-journal tests RED; always block -> orphaned control RED. Reverted. Commit 99de5501."}	blake3:jbFGzdLM60ojItbERn4jBXwMfxIRIfp1VU7OK7AVMok
1790529331790102	maw-68q58s	itc:AQ		item.comment	bn-3rhz	{"body":"FINDING 3 (FIXED, same stranding class, outside listed files) crates/maw-cli/src/epoch.rs sync() and crates/maw-cli/src/undo.rs run(): both move refs/manifold/epoch/current under the epoch lock with NO merge-journal check (bn-302v added it only to FF-absorb, doctor --repair, merge promote). maw epoch sync is the documented fix after a direct trunk commit, so: merge crashes in COMMIT before the CAS, user commits on main, runs maw epoch sync -> epoch moves -> maw ws merge --abort refuses forever. Same for maw undo. Repro tests: epoch_sync_refuses_under_crashed_commit_journal (pre-fix: Epoch synced: 190dca6f -> dac9906c, RED) and undo_refuses_under_crashed_commit_journal (pre-fix: Undid merge 30d38976, RED). Fix: both refuse via epoch_drift::unfinished_merge_phase (fails closed on unreadable journal, like doctor) and print the --abort recovery. The red-first runs are the mutation (removing the check restores the defect). Commit 0d4e8410."}	blake3:MEJfYkNCOXdsB8c6ulqgoecf2TJBRcuvWXkv-7Uha5s
1790529331826751	maw-68q58s	itc:AQ		item.comment	bn-3rhz	{"body":"SWEEP NOTES - checked, no defect (or accepted):\n- checkout_impl.rs set_head_detached_cas: create_new HEAD.lock, re-read under lock, write+fsync, rename; lock removed on every error path and a foreign lock never removed. Symbolic HEAD compared by resolved OID; git commit on a branch also takes HEAD.lock, so the CAS excludes it. kill -9 between create and rename leaves a stale HEAD.lock: FF-absorb then skips that sibling (RefConflict, reported) and git commit fails with git's own remove-the-lock message. Same as git itself; ACCEPTED, fail-closed.\n- worktree_impl.rs bn-1u93: kill -9 mid worktree_add leaves the admin dir locked (initializing) so prune never removes it; maw's worktree_remove ignores the marker, so ws destroy still cleans it. Same as git worktree add; ACCEPTED. Empty gitdir skip + gitdir-written-last via rename look correct.\n- Lock ordering: every per-workspace lock (WorkspaceRebaseLock) is try_acquire; the only blocking lock is the epoch flock, taken first. No deadlock possible. flock is kernel-released on crash.\n- FF-absorb sibling path (ff_advance_prepare, sync_ff_paths_in_worktree, epoch ref last): re-check under lock uses (own delta + ff_paths) vs fresh dirty with component-prefix conflicts (ff_plan::paths_conflict), fails closed on unreadable HEAD/diff; ff_paths materialized unchecked only when that re-check proved them disjoint. Crash windows covered by the bn-302v failpoint tests (all green). Residual (documented in code): agent write between re-check and materialization; CAS failure after materialization leaves absorbed content as uncommitted edits (forward content, no loss).\n- refs_impl.rs delete_ref_cas + changes close: CAS against the judged OID, DeleteReferenceMustExist mapped to RefConflict. OK.\n- merge_state.rs: advance_to_commit single write, fsync parent dir, Cleanup-no-Aborted. abort_merge() in merge.rs still removes the journal when state.abort() is refused; it is never called after the Cleanup advance, so no effect. Minor inaccuracy: the Commit->Aborted comment says every abort from Commit happens with refs NOT at the candidate, but merge.rs PartialCommit + recover_partial_commit Err arm aborts after the epoch moved (candidate stays reachable from the epoch ref, sources not destroyed - no loss). NOT FIXED (comment only).\n- Pre-existing liveness gap (not a regression): a crash after the COMMIT CAS leaves a Commit/Cleanup journal that PREPARE refuses and --abort refuses (RefusedPostCommit); recover_from_merge_state (RetryCleanup/CheckCommit) has no production caller, so the only way out is deleting merge-state.json by hand as the message says. No data loss. NOT FIXED - candidate follow-up bone.\n- quarantine.rs abandon_quarantine deletes the worktree without a recovery pin (Prime Invariant item 3 does not cover it). Mitigated by the new CAS-failure message; NOT FIXED otherwise - candidate follow-up.\n- quarantine commit_quarantine_edits still moves HEAD with a raw fs::write (no reflog, outside the bn-8flz guarded primitive). No loss; NOT FIXED.\n- failpoints.rs thread registry: fp! compiles to Ok(()) without the failpoints feature, so nothing leaks into production. OK.\n- sync/ quarantine refusal and auto-rebase SkippedQuarantine: consistent. reconcile_epoch_with_branch has a duplicated quarantine skip block (cosmetic, left).\nGates: cargo build --release -p maw-cli OK; just check exit 0 (107 test result: ok, 0 FAILED); just sg1-faithful-test exit 0; cargo test -p maw-cli --features failpoints --test ff_absorb_sibling_order_bn_302v 10/10."}	blake3:uvRvt50OusxHYaOatmKuLlglNkpH_ns7PmfsAp2gIL4
1790529796380350	maw-68q58s	itc:AQ		item.comment	bn-22nk	{"body":"Codex (gpt-6-astra via vessel) sweep report, verbatim:\n\n1. src/merge/resolve.rs:1140 — data-loss. AST atom resolution discarded a participant’s clean edit to another function. Fixed in the working tree: unsafe AST atoms now fall back to diff3. Test: ast_atom_resolution_keeps_clean_participant_edits.\n\n2. src/merge/apply_resolution.rs:578 — data-loss. Conflicting function insertions used variant coordinates as base replacement ranges, overwriting an existing function. Fixed by the same reconstruction guard. Test: ast_atom_resolution_added_node_keeps_following_base.\n\n3. src/merge/apply_resolution.rs:430 — data-loss. Choosing content beginning with “||||||| literal documentation” returned empty bytes. Fixed by refusing ambiguous atom parsing; file-level resolution remains available. Test: atom_resolution_refuses_ambiguous_literal_markers.\n\nMutation evidence: all three tests failed before fixing. Removing each guard reproduced its failures. Restoring the guards passed the tests and final gate.\n\nPassed commands:\n- TMPDIR=/var/tmp/bn-22nk cargo test --lib --features proptests merge::\n- TMPDIR=/var/tmp/bn-22nk cargo test -p maw-core merge::\n- TMPDIR=/var/tmp/bn-22nk cargo build --release -p maw-cli\n- TMPDIR=/var/tmp/bn-22nk just check\n\nThe final gate exited 0. Searching its full output for “test result: FAILED” found no matches. Log: /var/tmp/bn-22nk/just-check-final.log.\n\nCommits: none. Git could not create /home/bob/src/maw/.git/worktrees/bn-22nk/index.lock: “Read-only file system.” Both modified files remain intact and unstaged. A patch is saved at /var/tmp/bn-22nk/merge-sweep-fixes.patch.\n\nNext action: commit once the worktree’s Git admin directory is writable, using the requested subject and co-author trailer.\n\n\n\nLead verification: disabled both guards -> all 3 new tests red; restored; just check green on the lead's run; committed as 910cbcb6 on the codex's behalf (sandbox kept .git read-only)."}	blake3:7EjsytK_GpGoAm-LjVN2owLdSWl8BVXfjpameSEZuGQ
1790529813728786	maw-68q58s	itc:AQ		item.move	bn-22nk	{"state":"done"}	blake3:C4tmbBYOTO8iwDVAnBrDlArkw8mWygqzmnTrdnMCius
1790529840993281	maw-68q58s	itc:AQ		item.comment	bn-ggo5	{"body":"Sweep C findings (workspace bn-ggo5, commit 371b2ce8). Upgrade scenarios run with a pre.15 binary built from the tag (git archive) creating repos, then the trunk binary operating on them.\n\nFIXED\nF1 (HIGH, data loss, new in consolidated since bn-1cth): crates/maw-cli/src/merge_cmd.rs abandon() -- with no quarantine state for <id> but .maw/workspaces/merge-quarantine-<id> present, it called abandon_quarantine which remove_dir_all'd the workspace. A user workspace named merge-quarantine-foo (creatable via ws create before this fix, or by older maw) is told by ws merge/sync refusals \"Or discard it: maw merge abandon foo\"; following that deleted the workspace + uncommitted work with NO recovery snapshot (maw ws recover: none). Pre.15 resolved <root>/ws/... in consolidated so it deleted nothing. Repro: tests/sweep_c_bn_ggo5.rs abandon_without_recorded_quarantine_never_deletes_a_workspace (RED before: \"[OK] Quarantine 'foo' abandoned\", file gone). Fix: refuse, point at maw ws destroy <name> (snapshots). Partial-create leftovers (worktree, no state) now also go through ws destroy. NOTE for bn-3rhz: abandon_quarantine in src/merge/quarantine.rs itself still deletes with no state check; I fixed only the CLI caller (did not edit quarantine.rs).\nF2 (MED): crates/maw-core/src/model/types.rs check_create_name_bytes -- merge-quarantine-* names were accepted by ws create/attach/recover --to, but ws sync/merge refuse them forever and list advertises promote/abandon. Now reserved at creation (WorkspaceNameRule::ReservedQuarantinePrefix); parsing existing names unchanged. Test create_refuses_merge_quarantine_prefix + unit test (RED before). Kani create_rejects_exactly_epoch_delta_names_le_12_bytes re-run: SUCCESSFUL (its <=12-byte domain cannot reach the 17-byte prefix; doc now says so).\nF3 (MED, LFS integrity, regression from bn-z9t3): crates/maw-git/src/lfs_clean.rs:232 used strict Pointer::parse to decide pass-through. Real git-lfs 3.8 `git lfs clean` passes through non-canonical pointers (no final newline, leading/interior/trailing blank lines, CRLF, hawser and git-media version URLs, size 012, size +12, trailing space, ext line after oid); maw cleaned them into a NEW object = pointer-to-pointer blob, dropping the real object reference from the tree (pre.15's prefix sniff passed most of these). Fix: new maw_lfs::git_lfs_clean_passes_through mirroring git-lfs copyToTemp/DecodeFrom/decodeKV (v3.7 source). Differential test crates/maw-lfs/tests/conformance.rs pointer_shaped_clean_passthrough_matches_git_lfs runs 23 inputs through real git-lfs clean vs maw write_blob_with_path (RED before: 10 mismatches), plus a git-lfs-free unit table in pointer.rs. Mutation check: len cutoff, hawser alias, CR strip, blank-line skip, negative size, dup ext priority, trim, extra-line, plus-sign each went RED; all reverted.\nF4 (LOW): crates/maw-core/src/config.rs load_with_legacy -- consolidated .maw/config.toml is also the .maw.toml fallback, so [merge] auto_resolve_from_main is legal there; adopting it into ManifoldConfig (deny_unknown_fields) failed and voided ALL legacy keys, and the warning told the user to move it into .maw/manifold/config.toml (which would make every merge fail to parse config). Pre.15 silently ignored the whole file, so not a regression, but the advice was harmful. Fix: skip that key. Test load_for_root_legacy_maw_toml_only_key_does_not_block_adoption (RED before; mutation section==workspace -> RED).\n\nVERIFIED OK (no change)\n- Legacy consolidated repo from pre.15 with [merge] auto_rebase_siblings in .maw/config.toml: new binary honors it with a deprecation warning, merges fine. v2 legacy layout: config read from .manifold/config.toml, no legacy fallback, quarantine list/display/abandon fine.\n- Legacy quarantine at <root>/ws/merge-quarantine-<id> in consolidated (pre.15): merge list finds it, abandon removes it. It is not shown in maw ws list (pre-existing) and appears as ?? ws/ in trunk git status until abandoned (pre-existing, pre.15 created it there).\n- Existing workspace named epoch-delta (created by pre.15): listable; merge refused while stale; destroy + recover --to ed2 restores its edits. ReservedWorkspaceId message path is sound.\n- ref_gc pin age (bn-3maj): all writers (destroy, clean-, materialize-, invariant-, undo) embed the precise UTC ts; legacy names fall back to destroy record then commit time; unknown kept.\n- path_safety (bn-2wav): validate_show_path identical to pre.15; restore destination now accepts a leading ./ (harmless, lookup fails as before); undo strictly safer (rejects \"\" and \".\"). Non-UTF-8: validate_show_path takes &str (clap rejects non-UTF-8 argv); is_contained_relative_path works on OsStr components. Backslashes are ordinary name bytes on Linux (correct).\n- hex.rs / batch.rs: byte-based decode removes a char-boundary panic on non-ASCII server oids. ordering.rs / patch.rs FileId codec: fine.\n\nNOT FIXED (noted)\n- load_manifold_config(root).unwrap_or_default() call sites (rebase.rs:636, merge.rs:5364/6276, mod.rs:2329) silently default on an invalid canonical config (pre-existing; merge path errors earlier at merge.rs:2190).\n- lfs_materialize / checkout smudge still use strict Pointer::parse, so non-canonical pointer blobs are left unsmudged where git-lfs would smudge (pre-existing since before pre.15).\n- Legacy workspaces named merge-quarantine-* still cannot be synced/merged (refusal by name); way out is ws destroy + ws recover --to (works)."}	blake3:jFEWjuEOtn3KqK6BbHy7S6qry9SX2h8pBnqMG4xRokg
