1790530805303815	maw-68q58s	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-jfj2	{"description":"FOUND BY: sweeps bn-3rhz and bn-ggo5 (2026-09-27). src/merge/quarantine.rs\nabandon_quarantine removes the quarantine worktree (and state dir) without\ncapturing a recovery snapshot/ref. Since bn-3rhz, promote builds on the quarantine's\nHEAD, so agents are expected to COMMIT fixes inside the quarantine — abandoning then\nsilently destroys those commits (and any uncommitted edits). Every other\nworkspace-removal path pins under refs/manifold/recovery/ (capture.rs, destroy\nrecords) so `maw ws recover` can find it.\nAlso check promote's post-success cleanup (removes the worktree after the refs moved —\nits HEAD is then reachable from main, but uncommitted edits made after promote\nstarted would be lost) and bn-ggo5's CLI guard in crates/maw-cli/src/merge_cmd.rs.\nSide issue from bn-3rhz: commit_quarantine_edits moves HEAD with raw fs::write (no\nreflog) — use the maw-git HEAD mover.\n\nFIX: before removal, capture the quarantine exactly like `maw ws destroy` does\n(reuse the capture/destroy-record machinery so `maw ws recover merge-quarantine-<id>`\nlists it, --show/--restore-file/--to work). Fail closed: if the pin fails, do not\ndelete. Print the recovery command in abandon's success output.\n\nACCEPTANCE: red-first CLI test — quarantine, commit a fix inside it, add an\nuncommitted edit, abandon, then `maw ws recover` finds both and `--to` restores them.\njust check green.\n","kind":"bug","labels":["release","data-integrity","prime-invariant"],"parent":"bn-1eyd","size":"s","title":"Release blocker: quarantine abandon/cleanup deletes the worktree without a recovery pin","urgency":"urgent"}	blake3:92D8Lv4eqNLVAPXFsW-6kEzDBY-5PHFdMrkekeI4tHQ
1790530805453083	maw-68q58s	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-1fcox	{"description":"FOUND BY: sweep bn-3rhz (pre-existing, no data loss). A crash after the COMMIT-phase\nref CAS succeeded leaves merge-state.json that PREPARE refuses and `ws merge --abort`\nrefuses; recover_from_merge_state (RetryCleanup / CheckCommit) is never called in\nproduction, so the only way out is deleting merge-state.json by hand — and now\nFF-absorb, doctor --repair, epoch sync and undo all refuse under it (bn-302v, bn-3rhz),\nso a stuck journal blocks a lot. Wire recovery (CheckCommit -> finalize/cleanup) into\nPREPARE or a `maw ws merge --recover`, model it in crates/maw-assurance, and fix the\nslightly-wrong Commit->Aborted comment in merge_state.rs (a PartialCommit path aborts\nafter the epoch moved).\n","kind":"bug","labels":["crash-safety"],"size":"s","title":"Crash after COMMIT CAS leaves a merge journal nothing can clear (only manual delete)"}	blake3:zMU8ZtEIU2ts6i0oN9XH-b-9DIAXjIH44fb7XOA2lfw
1790530805599728	maw-68q58s	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-hcbc8	{"description":"FOUND BY: sweep bn-ggo5. Several call sites silently use defaults when the manifold\nconfig is invalid (e.g. a typo disables safety settings without warning). Make them\nwarn loudly (or error for safety-relevant keys). Also: LFS smudge still uses the\nstrict pointer parser, so non-canonical pointers that git-lfs smudges stay as pointer\ntext in maw-materialized worktrees — use maw_lfs::git_lfs_clean_passes_through-style\ntolerant decoding for smudge (bn-ggo5 added it for clean).\n","kind":"bug","labels":["config"],"size":"xs","title":"load_manifold_config().unwrap_or_default() call sites fail open on invalid config"}	blake3:700MzgCoDa7Wlc04pl4lqRcNk9h2kcfZvwOFot_9oaE
