1790540111197567	maw-nzv80n	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-30v6e	{"description":"CONTEXT (2026-09-27): the local SG1 1e8 soak (scripts/sg1-soak/, state\n~/.local/state/maw-sg1-soak) has been HALTED since 2026-07-06 at 95,999,616 /\n1e8 op-steps. Both recorded \"violations\" are environmental, not oracle findings:\n  violations/base-4296464296-...log: in-proc driver init: git init ... Disk quota exceeded\n    (panic at crates/maw-assurance/tests/sg1_dst.rs:293)\n  violations/base-4296464796-...log: git hash-object -w --stdin failed: ... Disk quota\n    exceeded (panic at crates/maw-assurance/src/in_proc.rs:975)\n/tmp is a per-user-quota tmpfs on this box; the soak writes temp repos there.\nscripts/sg1-soak/slot.sh treats ANY non-zero exit of the pinned binary as an Oracle\nviolation and writes STOP. Also the pinned harness is from 2026-06-18 (pre.6), so its\nevidence predates many releases of fixes. User approved (2026-09-27): reset accrual\nand restart on the pre.16 harness.\n\nWORKER SCOPE (code, in a maw workspace)\n1. Harness: make infrastructure I/O failures distinguishable from oracle\n   violations. In crates/maw-assurance (sg1_dst test + in_proc driver + wherever\n   temp repos / git subprocesses are created), classify errors whose cause is\n   EDQUOT / ENOSPC / EMFILE / ENFILE (io::ErrorKind::StorageFull/QuotaExceeded or\n   matching \"Disk quota exceeded\" / \"No space left on device\" / \"Too many open\n   files\" in git stderr) as INFRA: print a single marker line\n   `[sg1] INFRA-FAILURE: <reason>` and exit with a dedicated code (e.g. 75,\n   EX_TEMPFAIL). Oracle violations and any other panic keep failing as today\n   (fail closed: unknown error = violation). Do not let the classifier swallow\n   real oracle failures — test both directions.\n2. slot.sh: rc==75 (or the marker) => infra: log to $STATE/infra/<ts>.log, do NOT\n   write STOP, do NOT add op-steps, do NOT consume... (the seed range was allocated;\n   record it in ledger.jsonl with status \"infra\" so the manifest stays honest and the\n   range is not reused). After N (3) consecutive infra failures write STOP with a\n   distinct \"INFRA-HALT\" message so a full disk still gets human attention.\n   status.sh: show infra count and distinguish INFRA-HALT from violation STOP.\n3. systemd/sg1-soak@.service: Environment=TMPDIR=/var/tmp/maw-sg1-soak (and ensure\n   slot.sh mkdir -p's it); README: document TMPDIR, infra handling, and the reset\n   procedure (archive old state dir instead of rm -rf).\n4. Tests: a unit/integration test for the classifier (simulated EDQUOT io::Error and\n   git stderr), and a bats-free shell test or cargo test that runs slot.sh against a\n   stub binary exiting 75 / 1 / 0 and checks STOP/ledger behaviour.\nLEAD DOES AFTER MERGE (not the worker): build release harness on trunk, archive\n~/.local/state/maw-sg1-soak -> ~/.local/state/maw-sg1-soak.pre6-archive, setup.sh,\n`just sg1-per-commit-smoke`, reinstall units, restart timers, note in\nnotes/sg1-soak-campaign.md that the pre.6 campaign was abandoned at 96% due to\ninfra-classified halts + stale harness.\n","kind":"task","labels":["v1-0","dst","soak"],"parent":"bn-2yzz","size":"s","title":"SG1 soak: infra failures (EDQUOT/ENOSPC) must not count as Oracle violations; TMPDIR off /tmp; re-pin on pre.16","urgency":"urgent"}	blake3:Afvwf-lj-R9-y4BMDMPUJQjYQN0m6My-pWYfC3ffdFg
