1790541884599781	maw-nzv80n	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-2eszz	{"description":"From bn-1ijl (bones field report, 2026-09-25): after working around a sync failure by\nmaking a new workspace and `git cherry-pick`ing commits, `maw ws destroy` refused with\n\"14 unmerged changes\" because it compares commit reachability and the cherry-picks have\nnew hashes, although the content is identical to what landed on the epoch.\nDo NOT weaken the refusal (Prime Invariant). Add a diagnostic: when the workspace's\nHEAD tree (and worktree) equals the epoch tree, or every unmerged commit's patch is\nalready contained in the epoch (patch-id match), say so in the refusal and suggest\n`maw ws destroy <ws> --force` (which still snapshots). Test both the hint and that the\nrefusal still happens.\n","kind":"task","labels":["ux","destroy"],"size":"xs","title":"ws destroy: explain 'N unmerged changes' when the workspace tree already matches the epoch (cherry-picked content)"}	blake3:srPTlOlT1955itOi2dCWU2eyat7NsOslhzHxtERS8v0
1790542021797588	maw-nzv80n	itc:AQ		item.comment	bn-hcbc8	{"body":"bn-hcbc8 evidence (ws bn-hcbc8; commits a9790436 config, 010a4d19 lfs smudge)\n\nRED-FIRST\n- tests/invalid_config_bn_hcbc8.rs: all 3 red on trunk. Merge red showed the real bug: \"Absorbed 1 upstream commit(s) into epoch\" (FF-absorb ran on default auto_absorb_ff=true), THEN \"BUILD: config error ... unknown field `auto_absorb_f`\". Sync with typo config succeeded silently; ws list/status printed no warning.\n- crates/maw-lfs/tests/conformance.rs smudge_decodes_what_git_lfs_smudge_decodes: 16 mismatches vs real git-lfs 3.8 on trunk (12 non-canonical pointers left as pointer text; size 0 not empty; size mismatch + extension pointers smudged where git-lfs refuses).\n\nGIT-LFS 3.8 SMUDGE PROBE (object re-stored before every case; git-lfs DELETES a local object whose size disagrees with the pointer, which poisons naive probes)\n- decode set == clean-passthrough set for blobs < 1024 bytes (incl. leading tab/VT/space, blank lines, CRLF, hawser/git-media, size 012/+12/-0)\n- size 0 -> empty output even when the object is missing or the pointer has extensions\n- size mismatch / missing object / unconfigured extension -> rc 2, pointer stays\n- >= 1024 bytes: git-lfs decodes the first 1024 bytes only and DISCARDS the tail (pointer + 1100 newlines + \"TAIL\" smudges). maw deliberately does not mimic this (test smudge_never_discards_content_past_the_pointer_cutoff).\n\nMUTATIONS (scratchpad hcbc8_mutants.py; all restored)\nM1 merge preflight -> unwrap_or_default: RED\nM2 sync entry preflight removed: RED\nM3 get_backend silent default: RED\nM4 smudge uses strict parser: RED\nM5 no size-mismatch check: RED\nM6 no extension refusal: RED\nM7 no size-0 empty: RED\nM8 decode accepts >=1024: RED\nM9 materialize_verify no decoded-identity fallback: RED\nM10 materializer strict-parser gate: RED\n\nGATES: cargo build --release -p maw-cli OK; just check green (110 ok results, 0 FAILED) run for both commits; cargo test -p maw-lfs -p maw-git green; clippy --workspace --all-targets clean.\n"}	blake3:bdSG6yyZDtNScVbtI9-JcVgdP1yOtKq9m1cCECOglq0
1790542255072644	maw-nzv80n	itc:AQ		item.comment	bn-30v6e	{"body":"bn-30v6e worker evidence (ws bn-30v6e, commit a8ab4883)\n\nMutation evidence (each applied, targeted tests run, reverted):\nM1 classifier ignores 'Disk quota exceeded' text: exit=101\n    test infra::tests::git_stderr_from_the_halted_campaign_classifies ... FAILED\n    test infra::tests::panic_payloads_classify_both_directions ... FAILED\n    test result: FAILED. 5 passed; 2 failed; 0 ignored; 0 measured; 121 filtered out; finished in 0.00s\nM2 oracle B: infra GitError swallows a real finding: exit=101\n    test in_proc::infra_triage_tests::oracle_b_real_finding_wins_over_infra_git_error ... FAILED\n    test result: FAILED. 6 passed; 1 failed; 0 ignored; 0 measured; 121 filtered out; finished in 0.10s\nM3 oracle A: every GitError treated as infra: exit=101\n    test in_proc::infra_triage_tests::oracle_a_only_git_error_with_infra_stderr_classifies ... FAILED\n    test result: FAILED. 6 passed; 1 failed; 0 ignored; 0 measured; 121 filtered out; finished in 0.08s\nM4 harness exits 75 even after a violation: exit=101\n    test sg1_infra_disposition_prefers_violations ... FAILED\n    test result: FAILED. 1 passed; 1 failed; 0 ignored; 0 measured; 5 filtered out; finished in 0.25s\nM5 harness treats every panic as infra: exit=101\n    test sg1_infra_exit_contract ... FAILED\n    test result: FAILED. 1 passed; 1 failed; 0 ignored; 0 measured; 5 filtered out; finished in 0.13s\nM6 slot.sh drops the marker requirement: exit=101\n    test every_non_infra_failure_shape_is_still_a_violation ... FAILED\n    test result: FAILED. 2 passed; 1 failed; 0 ignored; 0 measured; 0 filtered out; finished in 0.16s\nM7 slot.sh drops the violation veto: exit=101\n    test every_non_infra_failure_shape_is_still_a_violation ... FAILED\n    test result: FAILED. 2 passed; 1 failed; 0 ignored; 0 measured; 0 filtered out; finished in 0.15s\nM8 slot.sh never INFRA-HALTs: exit=101\n    test infra_slots_record_but_do_not_accrue_or_halt_until_the_streak_limit ... FAILED\n    test result: FAILED. 2 passed; 1 failed; 0 ignored; 0 measured; 0 filtered out; finished in 0.14s\nM9 slot.sh accepts marker with any exit code: exit=101\n    test every_non_infra_failure_shape_is_still_a_violation ... FAILED\n    test result: FAILED. 2 passed; 1 failed; 0 ignored; 0 measured; 0 filtered out; finished in 0.15s\nM10 driver ignores infra apply_op errors (old behaviour): exit=101\n    test sg1_infra_real_git_failures_classify_both_directions ... FAILED\n    test result: ok. 1 passed; 0 failed; 0 ignored; 0 measured; 7 filtered out; finished in 0.19s\n    test result: FAILED. 2 passed; 1 failed; 0 ignored; 0 measured; 5 filtered out; finished in 0.19s\n\nGates: cargo build --release -p maw-cli OK; just check exit 0 (0 FAILED/error); cargo test -p maw-assurance --features oracles: lib 127 ok, sg1_dst 7 ok, sg1_soak_slot 3 ok; just sg1-per-commit-smoke OK; SG1_PLANT_AND_FAIL=1 -> rc 101, no INFRA marker.\n"}	blake3:eObN_6Pz1B6wSYJZhAnjSa0jaGjS1pzoaVuw7IWIlJY
1790542515376326	maw-nzv80n	itc:AQ		item.move	bn-hcbc8	{"state":"done"}	blake3:qQp5_RbV9wNLVuyQO0VLHg-sbnlPyXzIECuKYbeJLQc
1790542658647991	maw-nzv80n	itc:AQ		item.comment	bn-1fcox	{"body":"bn-1fcox worker evidence (workspace bn-1fcox, commit 0cb1ad80 after sync onto 26acf4bb)\n\nREPRO (pre-fix, MAW_FP=FP_COMMIT_AFTER_EPOCH_CAS=abort on `ws merge a --destroy`): refs at candidate, journal phase=commit; `git status` in root shows `D a.txt` (default worktree still at old epoch under HEAD=new epoch — a commit there reverts the merge); ws a not destroyed; `--abort` refuses; next merge refuses (stale siblings), and once past that PREPARE's stale_completed silently overwrote the journal WITHOUT cleanup. fsck --repair also deleted orphaned journals in any phase.\n\nRED-FIRST (new crates/maw-cli/tests/merge_crash_recovery_bn_1fcox.rs run against pre-fix trunk code): 6/6 FAILED — --recover unknown; --abort \"Refused to abort merge\"; next merge after a crash in CLEANUP succeeded but left ws a undestroyed (\"a's --destroy was never finished\"). With fix: 6/6 pass.\n\nCLI MUTATIONS (each applied, failpoint suite run, reverted):\nM1 skip target checkout in finalize -> 2 FAILED (recover_finishes_cleanup, abort_finishes_instead_of_refusing)\nM2 skip --destroy in finalize -> 4 FAILED\nM3 classify Unknown as Landed -> unprovable_ref_state_is_refused_and_journal_kept FAILED\nM4 drop auto-recovery at ws merge start -> crash_in_cleanup_then_next_merge_recovers_automatically FAILED\nM5 fsck deletes post-CAS journal again -> crash_after_cas_then_recover_finishes_cleanup FAILED\n\nSTATERIGHT (crates/maw-assurance): Recover now = production decide_journal_recovery(classify_cas_landing(..)) under the epoch lock; ghost target_stale + property P_TARGET_CHECKED_OUT (\"no journal => merge target checked out\").\nGreen: fast_merge_crash_recover_racing_trunk, fast_merge_crash_recover_racing_trunk_into_branch (RECOVERED_POST_CAS + RECOVERED_PRE_CAS reachable), all existing fast_* and deep_everything (formal-check 38 ok).\nMust-fail mutations (pre-bn-1fcox shapes): PostCasAbortOnly -> P_RECOVERY_CONVERGES counterexample; PostCasClearWithoutCleanup -> P_TARGET_CHECKED_OUT counterexample (default and into-branch configs). Existing bn-302v journal mutations still caught (landing uses exact epoch compare).\n\nGATES: cargo build --release -p maw-cli; just check (111 ok, 0 FAILED, before and after sync); cargo test -p maw-core (820 ok); just formal-check (38 ok); cargo test -p maw-assurance --features stateright; just sg1-faithful-test (all ok); clippy default + --features failpoints clean.\n"}	blake3:mS_PPQhej1gTohd2bqFUcUk8khAiprVsBiuT8815S-E
1790543101032422	maw-nzv80n	itc:AQ		item.move	bn-30v6e	{"state":"done"}	blake3:pCrkMyvkPkDdo6vzhPDCv0cLtl4AWSV0hQqgWDj7veM
1790543105104058	maw-nzv80n	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-25pac	{"description":"FOUND BY: bn-30v6e worker; confirmed by lead reading trunk 2026-09-27.\ncrates/maw-assurance/src/in_proc.rs check_oracles (~:885):\n  - capture_state(root) Err => `return StepVerdict::Clean; // best-effort`\n  - oracle_a.check_step Err => ignored (`Err(_) => {}`)\n  - per-ws head via git_capture_opt(...).unwrap_or_default() => empty head_oid, so\n    Oracle A silently skips that workspace's witnesses\n  - (per worker) plan-step errors are ignored\nSo a seed can be counted as a clean SG1 soak run while the oracles never actually\njudged it. This makes the v1.0 gate evidence potentially vacuous. MUST be fixed before\nthe soak is re-pinned and restarted (bn-30v6e merged the infra classification).\n\nFIX\n- Fail closed: any oracle/infrastructure error in check_oracles that is not positively\n  classified as INFRA (crates/maw-assurance/src/infra.rs from bn-30v6e) becomes a\n  distinct violation verdict (e.g. StepVerdict::HarnessError(detail)) that fails the\n  seed exactly like an oracle violation (exit non-zero, no marker).\n- Plan-step errors: decide per step type whether an error is an expected outcome of\n  the op under fault injection (e.g. a refused merge) — keep those as data — versus a\n  harness malfunction (fail). Document the classification.\n- Vacuity guard: per seed, count oracle checks actually performed and witnesses\n  harvested; if a seed ends with zero Oracle A witnesses or zero successful checks\n  where the plan created workspaces, fail it as HarnessError. Print totals in the soak\n  summary line so slot ledgers record them (extend ledger.jsonl rows via slot.sh if\n  simple).\n- Tests: both directions (a forced capture_state error / check_step error now fails;\n  normal runs stay clean), and a mutation check restoring each fail-open path goes\n  green-when-it-should-be-red.\n- Re-run `just sg1-per-commit-smoke` and a short soak locally (e.g. 50 seeds x 64\n  steps via the pinned-binary path or the test directly) and report violation/clean\n  counts — if real harness errors appear in normal runs, report them (they are\n  findings), don't mask them.\n","kind":"bug","labels":["v1-0","dst","soak","verification"],"parent":"bn-2yzz","size":"s","title":"SG1 soak driver fails open: oracle errors and unreadable state count as Clean (vacuous gate evidence)","urgency":"urgent"}	blake3:brKkxxtpfyJl4zDkXuMD0-pdCsxSiPfz1xUlRy5ErJs
1790543120349188	maw-nzv80n	itc:AQ		item.move	bn-25pac	{"state":"doing"}	blake3:wx6c4OuK3PVsYguZUFt9Nk64Y0lAOuer4JnOCwM-rmY
1790543120360128	maw-nzv80n	itc:AQ		item.assign	bn-25pac	{"action":"assign","agent":"maw-nzv80n"}	blake3:Zwt3viUgaBr33ODVIZJY7Xs6WaI7XOchnbG8RXUPytE
1790543690472422	maw-nzv80n	itc:AQ		item.move	bn-1fcox	{"state":"done"}	blake3:JD09xeQQtTm9VrJNw793pXYUbgnZXm2BkFnUd0MsU_Y
1790543772080628	maw-nzv80n	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-qi5br	{"description":"FOUND BY: bn-hcbc8 worker (which fixed the same pattern for the manifold config via\nrequire_manifold_config / load_manifold_config_or_warn in\ncrates/maw-cli/src/workspace/mod.rs). MawConfig::load (.maw.toml) is used with a silent\ndefault fallback at ~15 sites (e.g. epoch.rs, create.rs, epoch_lock.rs,\ninvariant_audit.rs, sync/mod.rs): an unparseable .maw.toml silently means branch\n\"main\", default lock wait settings, audit on. Apply the same policy: mutating\ncommands refuse with file/line/parse error + fix line; read-only commands warn once.\nRed-first test with a broken .maw.toml (e.g. a merge whose configured branch is not\nmain must not silently operate on main).\n","kind":"bug","labels":["config"],"size":"s","title":"MawConfig (.maw.toml) load fails open at ~15 sites: invalid file silently falls back to defaults"}	blake3:WQ8p8X8-Arhjx6T2U703u5ASCoWRkt3z-BpbJfUxD9Q
1790543772242708	maw-nzv80n	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-28s78	{"description":"FOUND BY: bn-1fcox worker. Recovery of a landed post-CAS merge\n(crates/maw-cli/src/workspace/merge/recover.rs) (1) does not run post-merge hooks, (2)\npasses an empty `resolved_paths` to update_default_workspace — check what that\nparameter controls and whether recovery can reconstruct it from the journal or must\nrecord it before the CAS, (3) maw-core's run_cleanup_phase / recover_from_merge_state\nhave no production callers — delete them or route recovery through them (no dead\nparallel implementation). Decide (1) explicitly: hooks may have side effects; running\nthem late may be wrong — at minimum print that hooks were skipped and how to run them.\n","kind":"task","labels":["crash-safety"],"size":"xs","title":"Merge crash recovery gaps: post-merge hooks not run, empty resolved_paths, dead maw-core recovery fns"}	blake3:Z9yPIlwDwSCpn6-2J1kvxALLfZy8R2j2FMGZZ9Iqab4
1790543795731812	maw-nzv80n	itc:AQ		item.move	bn-2eszz	{"state":"doing"}	blake3:8xuAtUxQd3A3nAV8lC_rIfKx_TJ28fLFi3fGLi_Li5g
1790543795743902	maw-nzv80n	itc:AQ		item.assign	bn-2eszz	{"action":"assign","agent":"maw-nzv80n"}	blake3:8s0NRnA7XT4CYYuAsVeI4JhccLN8HAMLJIt5ecEqSxU
1790543796299533	maw-nzv80n	itc:AQ		item.move	bn-qi5br	{"state":"doing"}	blake3:rfHk42wSJzHrIhqBanyp2Fmt4pbmahL9bPCZKzGs4Aw
