1790545843291727	maw-nzv80n	itc:AQ		item.comment	bn-25pac	{"body":"bn-25pac worker evidence (ws bn-25pac, commit 72c21ae0 after sync onto 6c698905)\n\nFIX\n- StepVerdict::HarnessError{site,detail} (same_class compares site only). Fails the seed like an oracle violation; infra-classified failures still exit 75 via bn-30v6e.\n- Fail-closed sites: capture_state Err; Oracle A check_step Err (both per-step and fast-mode harvest); unreadable ws/ dir; extant ws dir with no refs/manifold/ws/<ws> (was unwrap_or_default -> skipped); every apply_op Err. apply_op doc table lists the modelled Ok no-op outcomes (ws gone, no tip to merge, no recovery ref, etc.); any Err is a harness malfunction. git_capture no longer returns empty stdout on failure; resolve_ref (rev-parse --verify --quiet) distinguishes absent from error; git_pipe*/walk_files return Result.\n- Vacuity guard: DriveStats {oracle_a_checks, oracle_b_checks, witnesses, workspaces_created/observed, commits_made/observed}; zero checks / created-but-unobserved / observed-commits-with-0-witnesses => HarnessError. Per-observation cross-check: an extant ws with pending evidence missing from Oracle A's view => HarnessError(ws_unobserved).\n- Summary lines print oracle_a_checks/oracle_b_checks/witnesses/workspaces_observed/commits_observed/harness_errors; slot.sh records oracle_a_checks/witnesses/harness_errors in clean ledger rows (null for older pinned binaries) and treats HARNESS-ERROR as a violation sign.\n\nFINDINGS\n1. Every in-proc destroy was a silent no-op: recovery ref name was \"dst-<secs> +0000\" (space => git \"bad ref name\"); do_destroy returned Err before removing dir/refs, apply error swallowed. Also broke merge --destroy cleanup, and therefore Recover (no recovery refs ever) and Gc recovery drains. First fail-closed soak run: 51/51 seeds HarnessError(apply_op:Destroy / apply_op:Merge). Fixed (secs only).\n2. Oracle A errored (\"fatal: bad object\") whenever a step both pruned a previous frontier root and advanced another root -- i.e. on work-loss steps; the driver swallowed it as clean. Fixed in oracle_a.rs: previous roots missing from the ODB are dropped from ^exclusions (existing_objects via cat-file --batch-check) and force a full rescan.\n3. Consequence: planted-violation smoke (WorkLoss on ws-0, 4x12) only tripped because destroys never happened. Smoke now plants on all 8 slots, requires an ORACLE verdict (harness errors fail it), and runs 8 seeds x 24 steps (3/8 trip).\n\nMUTATIONS (each restores one fail-open path; all RED, reverted)\nM1 capture_state Err -> Clean: capture_state_error_is_harness_error FAILED, sg1_capture_state_failure_fails_closed FAILED\nM2 Oracle A Err ignored: oracle_a_tooling_error_is_harness_error FAILED, sg1_oracle_a_tooling_failure_fails_closed FAILED\nM3 missing ws state ref -> empty head: extant_ws_without_state_ref_is_harness_error FAILED\nM4 plan-step Err ignored: plan_step_error_is_harness_error(+_in_fast_mode_too) FAILED, sg1_infra_real_git_failures_classify_both_directions FAILED\nM5 vacuity guard removed: vacuity_guard_is_wired_into_drive FAILED\nM6 ws_unobserved cross-check removed: blind_workspace_observation_is_caught FAILED\nM7 bad recovery ref name restored: destroy_really_destroys_and_pins_recovery FAILED\nM8 Oracle A exclusion fix reverted: work_loss_with_concurrent_root_advance_is_judged FAILED (HarnessError oracle_a_check bad object)\n\nGATES\n- cargo test -p maw-assurance --features oracles: 140+9+4 passed, 0 failed\n- just sg1-assurance-clippy: clean\n- just sg1-per-commit-smoke: OK, 3 of 8 seeds tripped (oracle verdicts), harness_errors=0\n- just check: green (0 FAILED)\n- Soak (release, sg1_nightly_soak): SG1_NIGHTLY_SEEDS=50 x 64: 51 clean / 0 violations, oracle_a_checks=3315 witnesses=777 harness_errors=0. SG1_NIGHTLY_SEEDS=200 x 64: 201 clean / 0 violations, oracle_a_checks=13065 oracle_b_checks=13065 witnesses=2959 workspaces_observed=3595 commits_observed=1267 harness_errors=0, driver 145s (~0.72 s/seed).\n"}	blake3:JLRN7Ox8ThsebTmZxInwVe3Ndb0-a1DK_Jfa-KDfDKU
