1790546681538143	maw-nzv80n	itc:AQ		item.move	bn-25pac	{"state":"done"}	blake3:NJIjdicLcpJuKHTtCh3Y1wQoe_5UCLRFg2G8BheZRe0
1790546852668678	maw-nzv80n	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-3fcbu	{"description":"FOUND BY: bn-28s78 worker (pre-existing, live and recovered merges alike). If a\nworkspace changes a file's mode (chmod +x, committed) and the trunk has an uncommitted\nedit to that same file, the merge's dirty-trunk preserve/replay recreates the file from\nthe stash as 644, so the merged mode change is silently reverted in the worktree (and\nthe next trunk commit would commit the revert). Cause per worker: stash_apply recreates\nthe file with default mode. Red-first CLI test; fix so replay preserves the merged\ncommit's mode unless the user's own change touched the mode.\n","kind":"bug","labels":["merge","data-integrity"],"size":"s","title":"Dirty-trunk replay across a merge resets a workspace's file-mode change (e.g. +x) to 644"}	blake3:HfHZdQ9R8XMvhgDHhkL1lbbDi7YDZx5t9tAsmgxiWkY
1790546852816375	maw-nzv80n	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-1losw	{"description":"From bn-qi5br and bn-28s78 workers (2026-09-27):\n1. crates/maw-cli/src/workspace/destroy_preview.rs:133 and create.rs:747 still use\n   `if let Ok(config)` for the default-workspace guard; `ws destroy --dry-run` takes no\n   epoch lock so it previews silently on an invalid .maw.toml. Use MawConfig::require /\n   load_or_warn (bn-qi5br).\n2. .maw.toml structs lack deny_unknown_fields, so a misspelled key is silently ignored\n   (only syntax/type errors trip bn-qi5br's policy). Warn on unknown keys (don't hard-fail\n   — forward compatibility), with the key path and nearest valid key.\n3. Crash recovery of a landed merge (crates/maw-cli/src/workspace/merge/recover.rs) does\n   not write the target's Snapshot op and passes workspace_base_before=None where the\n   live merge uses the backend's base epoch for non-root targets. Check whether history\n   / undo depend on either; fix or document.\n","kind":"task","labels":["config","crash-safety"],"size":"xs","title":"Config/recovery small leftovers: destroy --dry-run default-ws guard, .maw.toml unknown keys, recovery Snapshot op"}	blake3:idjLIYlLpyiQc4I-PtMthGtoqvWCiY95_TE9l9EPx7o
1790546871775195	maw-nzv80n	itc:AQ		item.move	bn-1losw	{"state":"doing"}	blake3:LnyRhm3gk65HZu79bFwuI70eB4VT5s0v1A8thF7Gcvg
