1790546872803184	maw-nzv80n	itc:AQ		item.move	bn-3fcbu	{"state":"doing"}	blake3:nkc0ghfWYzCZNiuqZ0ROk5XMikd_g5LDSQGDIdNBYjk
1790546872818205	maw-nzv80n	itc:AQ		item.assign	bn-3fcbu	{"action":"assign","agent":"maw-nzv80n"}	blake3:q3JPazhv914XZXCwfozGLwNlSxYx2WltaXc3_qHqhlk
1790547668007241	maw-nzv80n	itc:AQ		item.comment	bn-3fcbu	{"body":"FIX (ws bn-3fcbu, commit 8ff45d92): crates/maw-cli/src/workspace/working_copy.rs — new reconcile_replayed_exec_bits() runs after every snapshot replay (replay_snapshot uses HEAD as \"ours\"; replay_snapshot_with_merge_protection uses epoch_after on both its no-overlap and 3-way branches). 3-way on the exec bit per replayed regular file: base = snapshot's first parent, theirs = snapshot tree, ours = merged commit. User changed mode -> user wins; otherwise merged mode applied. Only regular files; never follows a symlink (file or any parent component inside the ws). Best-effort (warn on failure).\n\nRED FIRST: crates/maw-cli/tests/dirty_trunk_replay_mode_bn_3fcbu.rs — before the fix 4/5 failed (mode-only chmod +x, chmod+content overlap, symlink scenario, crash-recovered merge via FP_CLEANUP_BEFORE_DEFAULT_CHECKOUT=abort + --recover); users_uncommitted_mode_change_wins passed already (regression guard). After fix 5/5 green, and each asserts a subsequent trunk `git commit -a` keeps 100755.\n\nMUTATIONS (all killed):\nM1 drop user-wins branch -> users_uncommitted_mode_change_wins FAILED\nM2 drop step-5b reconcile (3-way path) -> merged_chmod_and_content_survive_overlapping_dirty_edit FAILED\nM3 drop no-overlap reconcile -> merged_chmod_survives_dirty_trunk_content_edit, symlinks_are_not_followed_and_survive_replay, recovered_merge_keeps_merged_chmod FAILED\nM4 follow symlinks in set_worktree_exec_bit -> unit test set_worktree_exec_bit_never_follows_symlinks FAILED\n\nGATES: cargo build --release -p maw-cli OK; TMPDIR=/var/tmp/bn-3fcbu just check green (no FAILED/error); failpoints: merge_crash_recovery_bn_28s78, _bn_1fcox, dirty_trunk_replay_mode_bn_3fcbu all green.\n\nOUT OF SCOPE (pre-existing, fails closed): workspace converts a symlink into a regular file while trunk has an uncommitted retarget of that symlink -> replay aborts with \"refusing to write conflict markers ... is a symlink\", snapshot preserved (no data loss, but merge reports replay failure rather than a conflict).\n"}	blake3:FOce6lQfgm6Q_nRdjzSLeNpDRamFj8a4k-DfzFNcnQ8
1790547996988316	maw-nzv80n	itc:AQ		item.move	bn-3fcbu	{"state":"done"}	blake3:0597IldacawZRsS5mAz2E97_UIY4vOg-ltGCaQPmEnI
1790548010653209	maw-nzv80n	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-2ygs0	{"description":"FOUND BY: bn-3fcbu worker (pre-existing). If a merged workspace replaces a symlink with\na regular file while the trunk has an uncommitted retarget of that symlink, the\ndirty-trunk replay (crates/maw-cli/src/workspace/working_copy.rs) aborts with\n\"refusing to write conflict markers ... is a symlink\". Nothing is lost (the snapshot\nis pinned), but the merge reports a failed replay rather than a normal, resolvable\nconflict. Treat type changes (symlink<->file) as a conflict-as-data case: keep the\nmerged side in the worktree, record the user's symlink target in the conflict\nsidecar / recovery output, and tell the user how to restore it. Red-first CLI test.\n","kind":"bug","labels":["merge"],"size":"xs","title":"Dirty-trunk replay aborts (instead of reporting a conflict) when a workspace turns a symlink into a file the trunk retargeted"}	blake3:AkyXFoHynii88m-rDTrbBDpnyWvm4u2fDT871RnZmgQ
1790548081261323	maw-nzv80n	itc:AQ		item.move	bn-2ygs0	{"state":"doing"}	blake3:jrMqOsbwVlGbB8q-8q6DXP2OcgD0jV5tu48MVLDfwNI
1790548081276910	maw-nzv80n	itc:AQ		item.assign	bn-2ygs0	{"action":"assign","agent":"maw-nzv80n"}	blake3:Wef8KqBVgM-Tt3S1JFYeYijhTYKkEhSRh2peKunh_hU
1790549226446545	maw-nzv80n	itc:AQ		item.comment	bn-2ygs0	{"body":"bn-2ygs0 evidence (commit c7d5c054, ws bn-2ygs0)\n\nTests: crates/maw-cli/tests/dirty_trunk_replay_type_change_bn_2ygs0.rs (8 CLI tests; each runs the printed restore command verbatim).\nRED before fix: 5/6 initial tests failed (symlink->file, retarget, dangling retarget, recovered merge: \"replay_snapshot failed: refusing to write conflict markers ... is a symlink\"; file->symlink and dangling retarget: no conflict reported). Same-bytes symlink->file test RED before the overlap-check + fidelity fixes (fidelity backstop overwrote the merged file with the bytes of the user's symlink TARGET).\n\nMutations (each reverted):\nM1 conflict case does not write merged entry back -> 6 tests RED\nM2 no symlink classification -> 7 RED\nM3 committed_content_changed bytes-only -> same_bytes test RED\nM4 drop ours==theirs shortcut -> identical_retarget_is_clean RED\n\nGates: cargo build --release -p maw-cli OK; just check green (117 test-result lines, 0 FAILED); clippy -p maw-cli --features failpoints --all-targets -D warnings clean; failpoints tests (bn_2ygs0, bn_3fcbu, bn_28s78, bn_1fcox) green.\n"}	blake3:TAPmyHyAn7G_x8EEzFVX1qbd_ngTL6Xben9jz2XUvAI
1790549284712376	maw-nzv80n	itc:AQ		item.comment	bn-1losw	{"body":"bn-1losw evidence (ws bn-1losw; commits 707a8a74, e18fbf5a, 15c9d5f3)\n\n1. destroy guard (707a8a74): tests ws_destroy_dry_run_refuses_invalid_maw_toml, ws_destroy_force_residual_refuses_invalid_maw_toml (tests/invalid_maw_toml_bn_qi5br.rs). RED before fix (both commands succeeded on a broken .maw.toml; --force purged residual state before the epoch lock), GREEN after MawConfig::require at destroy_preview.rs and create.rs.\n\n2. unknown keys (e18fbf5a): new crates/maw-cli/src/workspace/maw_toml_keys.rs (known-key table; same-leaf-in-other-section match, else Levenshtein <= max(2,len/3)); warnings via emit_config_warnings (once per process), never fails. [merge] sub-keys left to maw-core's layered loader (already warns). Tests: unknown_maw_toml_keys_warn_with_path_and_suggestion (RED before), known_maw_toml_keys_do_not_warn, 5 unit tests. Mutation: disabling section sub-key detection -> integration test RED.\n\n3. recovery oplog parity (15c9d5f3): crates/maw-cli/tests/merge_recovery_oplog_parity_bn_1losw.rs (--features failpoints).\n - Pre-fix, crash at FP_CLEANUP_BEFORE_DEFAULT_CHECKOUT + recover: target ops [merge, create] vs live [snapshot, merge, create] -> ops log differs; a later `maw ws undo` on the target would Compensate against a different op.\n - Pre-fix, crash at FP_CLEANUP_AFTER_CAPTURE (after checkout+Snapshot) + recover: [merge, snapshot, merge, create] -- DUPLICATE Merge op (merge_op_already_recorded looked only at head, which was the Snapshot).\n - Repo-level `maw undo` skips Snapshot ops and behaved the same either way (asserted). `maw ws history default` errors \"not found\" in the consolidated layout (pre-existing), so `maw ops log` is the observer.\n - Fix: target_ops() sees through a Snapshot head; recovery writes the Snapshot (shared record_target_snapshot_op helper) before the checkout, only when the checkout has not run and the Merge op is the head.\n - Mutation: target_ops returning Unrecorded for Snapshot->Merge -> recovery_after_target_checkout_does_not_snapshot_again RED (duplicate merge).\n - workspace_base_before=None: identical to live in the consolidated layout (live also passes None when target path == root). Legacy v2 layout only differs if the target's epoch ref is missing or lags behind a HEAD at epoch_before (backend self-heal); documented at the call site, not changed (post-CAS the backend cannot reproduce the pre-merge answer).\n\nGates: cargo build --release -p maw-cli; just check green (0 FAILED); cargo clippy -p maw-cli --features failpoints --all-targets -D warnings clean; failpoints tests merge_recovery_oplog_parity_bn_1losw (2), merge_crash_recovery_bn_28s78 (3), merge_crash_recovery_bn_1fcox (6) green.\n"}	blake3:EJ6vsC73wS2RxT7OQumaKU35Eza11DQoit4VCFzXxJs
1790549561241050	maw-nzv80n	itc:AQ		item.move	bn-2ygs0	{"state":"done"}	blake3:cLibBUqHkrsxmVNcxlOiRyTg8HNyDkIMhhr8-ngcsck
1790549978752774	maw-nzv80n	itc:AQ		item.move	bn-1losw	{"state":"done"}	blake3:VNslftUAcXiliCKYyp1VXxTtbTTVRacuwU43h1iCQho
1790550000177112	maw-nzv80n	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-3jqfk	{"description":"FOUND BY: bn-2ygs0 worker. capture_pre_merge_dirty in\ncrates/maw-cli/src/workspace/merge.rs uses is_file() (follows symlinks), so a dirty\nsymlink in the trunk is recorded as the contents of the file it points to. That feeds\npin_pre_merge_recovery_ref — the fallback recovery ref used when the snapshot fails —\nso recovery would restore a regular file where the user had a symlink (and a dangling\nsymlink may be skipped entirely). Use symlink_metadata; store symlinks as mode 120000\nblobs of the link text. Red-first test through the fallback path (force the snapshot\nto fail via a failpoint), then `maw ws recover ... --restore-file` restores the link.\nAlso check the directory case: a path the user turned into a directory, or a\ndirectory in the merged tree, in dirty-trunk replay (bn-2ygs0 left these on the old\nbehaviour and refuses to replace a directory) — make it a reported conflict-as-data\ncase like the symlink ones if it is not already.\n","kind":"bug","labels":["merge","recovery","prime-invariant"],"size":"xs","title":"Pre-merge dirty capture follows symlinks: fallback recovery pin stores a dirty symlink as its target's contents"}	blake3:cjPpGnL6tJDzW8u7VBrhzI0DZajHWi8l6ZAf1NRB5wA
1790550000329997	maw-nzv80n	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-15fzo	{"description":"FOUND BY: bn-1losw worker.\n1. `maw ws history default` fails \"Workspace 'default' not found\" in the consolidated\n   layout; only `maw ops log` shows the default op log. Fix name resolution\n   (default = repo root) and test.\n2. If crash recovery itself crashes inside update_default_workspace after the checkout\n   but before the per-workspace epoch ref is written, the next recovery anchors the\n   replay at epoch_before against an already-merged tree. Construct the double-crash\n   with failpoints and either make the ref write precede/accompany the checkout or make\n   recovery detect the already-checked-out state.\n3. `maw ops log` orders ops by millisecond timestamp; ops written in the same ms can\n   appear in either order. Add a stable tiebreak (op-log chain order / sequence).\n","kind":"task","labels":["ux","crash-safety"],"size":"xs","title":"Small leftovers: `maw ws history default` not found (consolidated), recovery re-crash anchor, ops log same-ms ordering"}	blake3:jvx3uTK91qEryhPu_u-LBw0o28qaA6dGfqN7K6xjZ2s
1790550081364551	maw-nzv80n	itc:AQ		item.move	bn-15fzo	{"state":"doing"}	blake3:JfQPiSxZxlS0cOvP3AUoecWxzALp-X5F2d7pWANutW8
1790550081376060	maw-nzv80n	itc:AQ		item.assign	bn-15fzo	{"action":"assign","agent":"maw-nzv80n"}	blake3:G2Ov1U5Y_5g6gLeuj5198z1CZVabxkDV1dNVNAYA_jI
1790550081573500	maw-nzv80n	itc:AQ		item.move	bn-3jqfk	{"state":"doing"}	blake3:0NkPXEvT0xq1SRJeBv6sOGd6TigrA1OQc6r-r5y0CXo
1790550081584511	maw-nzv80n	itc:AQ		item.assign	bn-3jqfk	{"action":"assign","agent":"maw-nzv80n"}	blake3:XCDHl_4z2jvHmK5EQ9qPuKDbU7-1wGUnXJWxg8fJSCA
1790551355796356	maw-nzv80n	itc:AQ		item.comment	bn-3jqfk	{"body":"bn-3jqfk evidence (workspace bn-3jqfk, commit 09881c55)\n\nTests: crates/maw-cli/tests/pre_merge_capture_symlink_bn_3jqfk.rs (9 tests). The 4 fallback tests need --features failpoints (just sg1-faithful-test) and force the snapshot to fail with the new failpoint FP_UPDATE_DEFAULT_BEFORE_SNAPSHOT=error.\n\nRED on pre-fix code (only the failpoint added): 8/8 failed.\n- fallback_keeps_local_symlink_retarget: pin had (\"100644\", \"c\\n\") at link, not (\"120000\", \"c.txt\"). The link on disk was not restored.\n- fallback_pins_new_dangling_symlink: the dangling link was not in the pin.\n- fallback_keeps_local_file_to_symlink: pin had (\"100644\",\"target\"); the repair wrote the target's bytes into a regular f.txt.\n- fallback_prints_restore_for_merge_changed_symlink: no restore command printed; the user's link was only in the pin.\n- 4 directory cases (merged file->dir, merged dir->file, local file->dir, local dir->file): \"replay failed, snapshot preserved\". stash_apply gave 'Is a directory' / 'File exists', or delete/modify markers were written into a directory. The unrelated dirty edits were not replayed either.\n\nGREEN after the fix: 9/9 (a new-untracked-file-vs-merged-new-dir case was added).\n\nMutations (each applied, the test file run, then reverted):\n- M1 capture follows symlinks again (is_file + read): 4 fallback tests RED.\n- M2 pin writes a symlink as EntryMode::Blob: 4 fallback tests RED.\n- M3 report_fallback_unreplayed not called: fallback_prints_restore_for_merge_changed_symlink RED.\n- M4 split_directory_collisions always returns no collisions: all 5 directory tests RED.\n- M5 merge_changed_path without the directory-blocked clause: local_dir_to_file_vs_merged_edit_inside_is_a_conflict RED (fidelity repair prints \"Automatic repair FAILED\" for a reported conflict).\n\nGates: cargo build --release -p maw-cli OK. just check green (0 failed). just sg1-faithful-test green, including the 2ygs0, 3fcbu, 1losw and 28s78 tests and 706 lib tests. cargo clippy -p maw-cli --features failpoints --all-targets -D warnings clean.\n\nBehaviour:\n- Pre-merge capture is Vec<(PathBuf, DiskSide)> (symlink_metadata, never followed). A path that cannot be read is skipped, never recorded as a deletion.\n- The pin writes symlinks as 120000 and keeps 100755. Removals are applied before upserts, so file<->dir swaps can be pinned.\n- The fidelity repair compares whole entries. A file-over-file repair keeps the old write path and the LFS logic. Any other repair goes through write_worktree_entry, which never follows a link and refuses to replace a directory.\n- The fallback prints each dirty path that the merge also changed. The output has \"yours (uncommitted): ...\" plus \"restore yours: maw ws recover --ref R --restore-file P\", \"rm -f\", or \"inspect yours: ... --show P\" when a directory is in the way.\n- Replay: snapshot paths where the user has a file or symlink and the merged tree has a directory (or a file at an ancestor) are collisions. Related paths (ancestors and descendants in the snapshot) are grouped with them. The whole group is left out of a filtered snapshot commit on the same base. The merged side stays on disk. Each path is reported as conflict_type \"directory_change\" (EntryKind::Directory added), with an inspect command pointing at the pinned snapshot.\n"}	blake3:y-aJ6bHlRJhgt6PtcS66lE59yFv5YCW7-n1EOJTxzc8
1790551446018264	maw-nzv80n	itc:AQ		item.comment	bn-15fzo	{"body":"bn-15fzo worker evidence (ws bn-15fzo, commits 6f3d407e, 3ba037dd, cbf0cb8a)\n\n1. ws history default (6f3d407e): history.rs resolves default/configured default name via LayoutFlavor::default_target_path. Test tests/ws_history_default_bn_15fzo.rs. Mutation (`if false && (name == default...)`) -> ws_history_default_resolves_in_consolidated_layout RED; revert GREEN.\n\n2. Re-crash anchor (3ba037dd): new failpoint FP_CLEANUP_AFTER_DEFAULT_CHECKOUT (after checkout, before replay + epoch ref). Reproduced before fix: double crash (FP_CLEANUP_BEFORE_DEFAULT_CHECKOUT then recovery crash at FP_CLEANUP_AFTER_DEFAULT_CHECKOUT) and single live crash at the new FP both ended with f.txt = \"base\" (user edit only in a recovery ref); clean target got a bogus Snapshot op ([create, merge, snapshot] vs live [create, merge]).\nFix: durable .maw/manifold/target-checkout-<ws>.json intent {epoch_after, anchor, snapshot, recovery_ref} written before checkout, cleared with the epoch-ref write; resume path cleans tree to merged commit (pins residual unless it equals anchor tree or replayed-snapshot tree) and replays the intent snapshot vs its anchor. recover.rs skips the snapshot-op when intent pending; live merge records Snapshot op before checkout.\nTests tests/merge_recovery_recrash_bn_15fzo.rs (failpoints): 3 tests assert f.txt/untracked new.txt/shared.txt (merge hunk + user hunk)/a.txt, HEAD on main at epoch, status = exactly the user paths, op-kind parity with the live merge.\nMutations: resume disabled (`&& false`) -> live_crash + double-crash tests RED; recover guard disabled (`true ||`) -> clean_target test RED ([create, merge, snapshot]). Reverted -> GREEN.\n\n3. ops log ordering (cbf0cb8a): tiebreak (timestamp desc, op-DAG generation desc, id desc). Test same_timestamp_ops_keep_chain_order (9 chained ops same ts). Mutation (generation(b) vs generation(b)) -> RED; revert GREEN.\n\nGates: cargo build --release -p maw-cli; just check exit 0 (120 ok test results, no FAILED); clippy -D warnings with and without --features failpoints clean; failpoints suites (bn_1losw, bn_1fcox, bn_28s78, bn_3fcbu, bn_2ygs0, bn_15fzo) green; maw-core --features failpoints failpoints tests green (glob test updated for the new FP_CLEANUP_* site); maw-assurance + maw-scenario tests green.\n"}	blake3:u_1YvGkkAHU3uhlx66lRpyNfz_GKwTcBoqrGD40odeA
1790551779220696	maw-nzv80n	itc:AQ		item.move	bn-3jqfk	{"state":"done"}	blake3:pKRyBgc5e4w6JE9jM6xMnCubrtzg9X8oQ7XrFtCKpXA
1790552254379265	maw-nzv80n	itc:AQ		item.move	bn-15fzo	{"state":"done"}	blake3:QuefjgyU12wA4zVsdJH-5oA_l45mnMr5lQKP-pe9edA
1790552336564256	maw-nzv80n	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-1eg2u	{"description":"From the bn-3jqfk and bn-15fzo workers (2026-09-27). None lose data (all pinned), but\neach is a rough edge:\n1. Snapshot-failed fallback's force checkout replaces a directory the user created\n   (incl. untracked files) with the merged file; files are safe in the pin and named in\n   the report, but there is no one-step restore for directory conflicts (only\n   `maw ws recover --show`). Add a restore path.\n2. `directory_change` conflict wording calls the merged side of p/x \"deleted\" when p is\n   now a file — say \"replaced by file p\".\n3. The replay's filtered snapshot copy (split_directory_collisions) is an unreferenced\n   commit gc can remove mid-operation; pin it for the duration or derive it on demand.\n4. The snapshot-failed fallback writes no checkout intent, so a crash inside it keeps\n   the old behaviour (edits pinned + repaired from memory, not replayed on resume).\n5. A resumed checkout that finds tree content that is neither the anchor nor the\n   replayed snapshot pins it and warns, but does not merge it back.\n6. DST: FP_UPDATE_DEFAULT_BEFORE_SNAPSHOT (bn-3jqfk) and\n   FP_CLEANUP_AFTER_DEFAULT_CHECKOUT (bn-15fzo) are NOT in CRASHABLE_BY_PHASE /\n   DANGEROUS_FAILPOINTS (adding them reshuffles cleanup-phase seeds and pinned digests).\n   Decide deliberately: adding them changes the SG1 harness, which forces a soak\n   re-pin (the pre.16-era campaign started 2026-09-27 22:06Z). Cheapest if done\n   early in the campaign.\n","kind":"task","labels":["merge","crash-safety","dst"],"size":"s","title":"Dirty-trunk replay/crash leftovers from bn-3jqfk + bn-15fzo; decide DST coverage of the new failpoints"}	blake3:LR8i7lH-vvfiBb_DCQEHhxam6F3OI44Acb3smf7Jotw
1790555126929414	edict-83n310	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-39nsp	{"description":"Filed from edict (bn-3pto, part of edict goal bn-30a0: trimming the edict-managed AGENTS.md section down to tool pointers such as \"see maw --help / maw tldr\").\n\nAgents are about to be pointed at maw's own help instead of an edict-maintained quick reference. The top-level help leads them astray in three ways (maw 1.0.0-pre.16):\n\n1. QUICK START says `maw ws create <your-name> --from origin/main`. Edict projects create from `main` (the local trunk), and origin/main can lag the trunk.\n2. WORKFLOW step 5 and the `maw ws merge --help` examples show `maw ws merge <a> <b> --into default` without `--message`. A non-interactive run fails: \"No --message provided and stdin is not a terminal.\" Agents always run non-interactively.\n3. Nothing says that an orchestrator may gate merges. In edict projects, reviewed work must merge through `edict protocol merge <ws>` (review log, clean check, risk:critical gate). An agent that follows maw's WORKFLOW verbatim skips that gate.\n\nProposed:\n- QUICK START and WORKFLOW: `--from main`; merge example `maw ws merge <name> --into default --destroy --message \"feat: ...\"`.\n- Every merge example in `maw ws merge --help` includes `--message`, or the help states it is required when stdin is not a TTY.\n- One WORKFLOW line: \"If your project uses an orchestrator (e.g. edict), merge through it; it runs maw ws merge for you after its checks.\"\n- Same fixes in `maw tldr` and `maw agents show` if they carry the same examples.\n\nAcceptance: `maw --help`, `maw ws merge --help`, `maw tldr` and `maw agents show` examples all run successfully non-interactively as written, and none present a bare merge as the only way to land reviewed work.","kind":"task","labels":["docs"],"size":"s","title":"Top-level --help and merge examples lead agents off the edict workflow (--from origin/main, no --message, no orchestrator gate)"}	blake3:gpqZtMq9KZFKxZ5kAvYGcd3fz_vmpxkOWxSAcfyYp-M
1790555224977744	maw-nzv80n	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-214ep	{"description":"User approved 2026-09-27: (1) sweep + cut/push pre.17; (2) add the two new crash\nfailpoints to the DST crash lists and re-pin the soak.\nORDER: DST failpoints task and three sweeps in parallel -> merge -> cut pre.17 ->\nre-pin the SG1 soak ONCE on the pre.17 harness (state dir e.g.\n~/.local/state/maw-sg1-soak-pre17; drop-in ~/.config/systemd/user/sg1-soak@.service.d/state.conf).\nSweep method: same as bn-1eyd (sample changed functions, trace end to end, real\ndefects only, red-first + mutation-check, every finding as a bone comment).\n","kind":"goal","labels":["release"],"size":"l","title":"Release v1.0.0-pre.17: DST crash coverage for new failpoints, fresh-eyes sweep of pre.16..HEAD, release, soak re-pin"}	blake3:7x4PaEDFjAW99xrgrsrr3kxkdK549wSXwa05JY7BGRU
1790555250682965	maw-nzv80n	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-1sbjf	{"description":"bn-3jqfk added FP_UPDATE_DEFAULT_BEFORE_SNAPSHOT and bn-15fzo added\nFP_CLEANUP_AFTER_DEFAULT_CHECKOUT (crates/maw-core failpoints, KNOWN_FAILPOINTS,\nnotes/assurance/failpoints.md), each guarding a crash window that lost/hid trunk edits.\nNeither is in the DST crash lists: CRASHABLE_BY_PHASE (crates/maw-scenario/src/lib.rs:96)\nand DANGEROUS_FAILPOINTS (crates/maw-assurance/src/fault.rs:67). Add them (right phase;\nFP_UPDATE_DEFAULT_BEFORE_SNAPSHOT is an `error`-style point — check whether the crash\nharness can use it as a crash or only as an injected error, and wire the appropriate\naction). User approved the seed reshuffle / soak re-pin.\n- Update pinned op-stream digests and any seed-pinned expectations deliberately (explain\n  each change in the commit message).\n- Prove the DST harness actually reaches them: a targeted DST test/seed that crashes at\n  each point and asserts the oracles judge the recovery (and that neutering the\n  bn-15fzo checkout-intent resume or the bn-3jqfk symlink capture makes that seed red).\n- Run `just dst-fast`, `cargo test -p maw-scenario`, `cargo test -p maw-assurance\n  --features oracles`, `just sg1-per-commit-smoke`, `just sg1-faithful-test`, and a short\n  soak (e.g. 200 x 64) reporting harness_errors/witness counts.\n","kind":"task","labels":["dst","crash-safety"],"parent":"bn-214ep","size":"s","title":"DST: crash-test FP_UPDATE_DEFAULT_BEFORE_SNAPSHOT and FP_CLEANUP_AFTER_DEFAULT_CHECKOUT"}	blake3:LL_WwmU6NcdinB1v35Y08p3ZiWu1GmjMH4kBkQPk934
1790555250875593	maw-nzv80n	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-1bkr0	{"description":"Fresh-eyes sweep by codex via vessel. SLICE (git diff v1.0.0-pre.16..HEAD):\ncrates/maw-cli/src/workspace/merge/recover.rs, merge/checkout_intent.rs,\ncrates/maw-cli/src/workspace/merge.rs (update_default_workspace, capture_pre_merge_dirty,\npin_pre_merge_recovery_ref, verify_trunk_replay_fidelity, report_fallback_unreplayed,\njournal/PREPARE/--recover/--abort paths), crates/maw-cli/src/workspace/working_copy.rs\n(replay, exec-bit reconcile, symlink/dir type changes, split_directory_collisions),\ncrates/maw-core/src/merge_state.rs (classify_cas_landing, decide_journal_recovery,\nclear_merge_journal), src/merge/prepare.rs. Focus: any path where a user's committed or\nuncommitted work can be lost or silently replaced, crash between any two steps, double\ncrash, symlink/dir/mode edge cases, printed recovery commands that don't work.\n","kind":"task","labels":["release","sweep"],"parent":"bn-214ep","size":"m","title":"pre.17 sweep A (codex gpt-6-astra): crash recovery + dirty-trunk replay changed since pre.16"}	blake3:dVNSjRC8YYIE2UuyAqyVxLKE955boybppsoWB0OTKzU
1790555251063653	maw-nzv80n	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-15ebo	{"description":"Fresh-eyes sweep. SLICE (git diff v1.0.0-pre.16..HEAD): config loading policy\n(crates/maw-cli/src/workspace/mod.rs require_manifold_config / load_*_or_warn,\nMawConfig::require / load_or_warn, maw_toml_keys.rs, epoch_lock.rs WaitPolicy::resolve —\nevery call site: is anything still fail-open, or now wrongly fail-closed for a read-only\nor recovery path?), maw-lfs pointer.rs/store.rs git_lfs_decode + smudge callers\n(lfs_materialize.rs, materialize_verify.rs, checkout smudge, doctor, push collection),\ndestroy_content_check.rs + destroy_guidance.rs, ops_log.rs, history.rs,\ncrates/maw-git/src/diff_impl.rs + crates/maw-core/src/merge/diff_extract.rs (bn-1ijl),\ndoctor.rs, fsck/invariants.rs, init.rs. Focus: upgrade path for existing repos (a\npreviously-tolerated config now refusing), LFS false positives/negatives, misleading\nguidance text, panics.\n","kind":"task","labels":["release","sweep"],"parent":"bn-214ep","size":"m","title":"pre.17 sweep B: config fail-closed, LFS decode/smudge, destroy/ops/history, diff extraction changed since pre.16"}	blake3:XJaGLJtm_I6poazvymPBY7kcS7u7XJKSN8cwyRDLO8A
1790555251256281	maw-nzv80n	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-2qamr	{"description":"Fresh-eyes sweep of the v1.0 gate instrument itself. SLICE (git diff\nv1.0.0-pre.16..HEAD): crates/maw-assurance/src/in_proc.rs (HarnessError, vacuity guard,\nDriveStats, apply_op expected-outcome list), infra.rs (classifier), oracle_a.rs\n(pruned-root rescan), tests/sg1_dst.rs, scripts/sg1-soak/slot.sh + status.sh + setup.sh,\ncrates/maw-assurance/src/model.rs changes. Focus: remaining fail-open paths (an error or\nskipped check that can still count as clean), infra misclassification in either\ndirection, vacuity guard holes (a seed that exercises nothing yet passes), ledger/Wilson\naccounting errors, anything that could make the soak's 1e8 evidence overstate\ncoverage. Do NOT edit CRASHABLE_BY_PHASE / DANGEROUS_FAILPOINTS (another worker owns\nthem) and do NOT touch the live soak state/units/timers.\n","kind":"task","labels":["release","sweep","dst"],"parent":"bn-214ep","size":"m","title":"pre.17 sweep C: SG1 soak harness, in-proc driver and oracles changed since pre.16"}	blake3:ku6tsZMIzqxlioTP-Ohd9qoMmJYxWmUR1xCHePprJtk
