1790555727167667	edict-83n310	itc:AQ		item.comment	bn-39nsp	{"body":"More from edict's audit: 'maw agents show' resolves conflicts by hand-editing markers then 'git add -A' (current flow: maw ws resolve --list / --keep), and mentions 'maw push' without saying who pushes (in edict projects only the lead pushes). maw --help also says 'maw exec default -- bn', which is wrong for the root layout (bn runs at the repo root)."}	blake3:cSNLLfMPUTI0cYWXuao7ExVC6OE80HR7CL4Kum4xosU
1790556479332323	maw-nzv80n	itc:AQ		item.comment	bn-15ebo	{"body":"Sweep B findings (workspace bn-15ebo, commit 91c1c305). Regression tests: tests/config_upgrade_sweep_bn_15ebo.rs (4 tests, all RED before the fix; reverting each fix makes its test RED again, then restored). just check green (exit 0).\n\nFIXED\n1. crates/maw-cli/src/workspace/mod.rs default_workspace_path (~2311): `maw ws recover <ws> --restore-file <p>` refused on an invalid .maw.toml (\"`maw ws recover` refuses...\") even in the consolidated layout, where the default workspace is the repo root no matter what the config says. Repro: maw init; ws create w; add new.txt; ws destroy w --force; echo 'repo = [' > .maw.toml; maw ws recover w --restore-file new.txt -> refused. Fix: consolidated returns the root with no config read; v2 (path depends on default_workspace) still requires the config, now labelled \"maw ws recover --restore-file\".\n2. crates/maw-cli/src/workspace/recover.rs restore_to / restore_ref_to: `--to` with an invalid .maw.toml logged `[AUDIT] {\"event_type\":\"restore\",...}` and printed \"Creating workspace...\" and then failed with \"`maw ws create` refuses\" (a command the user did not run). DECISION: --to SHOULD refuse. It goes through create's resolve_epoch, which reads the configured branch and may rewrite refs/manifold/epoch/current toward it, so running on defaults could move the epoch. Fix: check first (require_config_for_restore_to), before the audit event; message names `maw ws recover --to`, says nothing changed, the snapshot stays pinned, and --show / --search still work.\n3. crates/maw-cli/src/migrate.rs run(): the only config check was in phase_d (require at ~510), AFTER Phase B pinned snapshots and Phase C moved ws/<name> to the new layout, so a .maw.toml typo left a half-migrated repo (resumable, but the repo is left in a state between layouts). Repro: v2 TestRepo + ws alpha + broken .maw.toml; maw migrate -> fails in phase D with ws/alpha already moved. Fix: require once before Phase A (after the --dry-run branch).\n4. crates/maw-cli/src/workspace/maw_toml_keys.rs + mod.rs try_load: in the consolidated layout .maw/config.toml is both the .maw.toml fallback and the deprecated manifold location. A pre-bn-2dyz repo with `[workspace] backend = ...` there got two warnings that contradict each other: \"[workspace] backend is read from a deprecated location\" AND \"unknown key `workspace` is ignored\". Fix: unknown_keys takes a read_elsewhere list; for that file it skips maw_core::config::LEGACY_ADOPTED_SECTIONS (now pub). A made-up [bogus] section there still warns (tested).\n\nREVIEWED, CORRECT AS IS (per-command decisions)\n- merge --recover / --abort (EpochLock::acquire -> WaitPolicy::resolve, plus merge/recover.rs:219 MawConfig::load) refuse on an invalid .maw.toml. Refusing is correct here: journals from older binaries have no target_branch, and observe() then uses config.branch() to decide whether the CAS landed, so running on defaults could clear a journal for a merge that did land. The journal is kept and the message says how to fix it. (File owned by bn-1bkr0; no edit.)\n- ws destroy / destroy --dry-run / ws clean / undo / gc / fsck --repair / doctor --repair / epoch sync / ws create / init / upgrade: refuse. They all read branch or default_workspace to make decisions, and a refusal loses nothing (destroy refuses before any snapshot or removal).\n- Read-only commands (status, list, history, fsck, doctor checks, cd) use load_or_warn and keep working. Verified by hand.\n- ManifoldConfig has deny_unknown_fields. For sync this is a new refusal (pre.16 sync used unwrap_or_default); pre.16 merge already refused (load_manifold_config_layered ?). Problems in the legacy .maw/config.toml only warn. Accepted as the bn-hcbc8 policy.\n- LFS (pointer.rs git_lfs_decode, store.rs open_for_smudge, checkout_impl smudge, lfs_materialize, materialize_verify fallback, lfs_push, doctor stubs): traced size-0, extension, size-mismatch, missing-object, CRLF/leading-zero and >=1024-byte cases. Each caller either keeps the pointer text with a warning or smudges exactly what git-lfs smudges. The verify fallback runs only on LFS-attr regular files. Found no defect.\n- destroy_content_check.rs: it only diagnoses (the refusal is never relaxed), and every inspection failure gives no hint. diff_trees does not detect renames, so a workspace rename's old path still shows up in the epoch diff. No false hint found.\n- ops_log.rs generations/sort: a total order, and cycle-safe. history.rs default mapping is correct.\n- diff_impl.rs rename tree-skip + diff_extract gitlink old-side change: covered by the proptest and tests/diff_tree_shapes.rs. No defect.\n\nNOT FIXED (out of my slice; owner bn-1bkr0)\n- crates/maw-cli/src/workspace/merge/recover.rs:392: `load_manifold_config(root).unwrap_or_default()` in finalize. With an invalid manifold config.toml, `maw ws merge --recover` (post-CAS finalize) silently falls back to auto_rebase_siblings = default and rebases siblings, even if the user turned that off. No warning is printed. This is the fail-open pattern bn-hcbc8 removed elsewhere. Suggested fix: use load_manifold_config_or_warn, and skip the sibling auto-rebase when the config is invalid. Skipping is always safe (siblings stay put and `maw ws sync` catches them up), and recovery still does not refuse.\n- Minor, existing before this range: restore_to/restore_ref_to still log the restore audit event before snapshot resolution and create, so the event is logged even when those later fail for other reasons.\n"}	blake3:akH6FYv1-tReo_WmGpaoyEz8xsUy7AV7-G1H_geH4pU
1790556514202390	maw-nzv80n	itc:AQ		item.comment	bn-1bkr0	{"body":"From sweep B (bn-15ebo): crates/maw-cli/src/workspace/merge/recover.rs:392 uses load_manifold_config(root).unwrap_or_default(); on a broken manifold config.toml the --recover finalize silently uses default auto_rebase_siblings and rebases siblings even if the user disabled it. Suggested: load_manifold_config_or_warn and SKIP sibling rebase when config is invalid (safe; later ws sync catches up; recovery must not refuse). Lead to apply after codex sweep lands if codex does not."}	blake3:aif-cC4tfBrMCYTYDt887SH36LBb58CoVexbI9EvgZA
1790556516311864	maw-nzv80n	itc:AQ		item.comment	bn-2qamr	{"body":"Sweep C findings (bn-2qamr), commit 7b1fc399 in workspace bn-2qamr. Four real defects: all fixed red-first and mutation-checked.\n\nF1 (fail-open, came in with bn-25pac): the known_violation corpus pins accept any verdict.\nsg1_per_commit_corpus treated a `known_violation` entry as reproduced on ANY non-clean verdict. After bn-25pac, StepVerdict::HarnessError counts as a violation. So a harness that cannot apply the plan, or an Oracle A/B tooling error (OracleA \"Other\" / OracleB \"GitError\"), kept the two permanent regression pins (lost-commits-2026-02-05, bn-cm63) green without any oracle judging them. A different oracle class also passed.\nFix: known_violation_mismatch() requires an oracle finding whose kind is named in the entry's description. It rejects Clean, HarnessError and tooling kinds.\nRed-first: sg1_known_violation_rejects_harness_error_and_other_classes, and sg1_known_violation_pin_is_not_satisfied_by_a_broken_harness (end to end: the real lost-commits entry with ws/<first ws> obstructed gives HarnessError apply_op:WsCreate, which the old logic accepted). Both were RED before the fix.\nMutations, each KILLED: accept HarnessError; drop the class check; drop the tooling-kind check.\n\nF2 (op-step overstatement): slot.sh counted clean*STEPS, and `clean` includes CANONICAL_BN_CM63_SEED, which the harness replays identically in every slot. The live pre16 ledger shows clean=501 for slot_seeds=500. The Wilson N was therefore about 0.2% too high: DONE at 1e8 meant about 99.8M distinct op-steps, with about 3.1k duplicate replays of seed 1 counted as independent trials.\nFix: accrue SLOT_SEEDS*STEPS (ledger gains range_clean, and clean is kept as is). This only happens when the harness begin line echoes back the allocated seeds, steps and base seed. Otherwise it fails closed as VIOLATION_OR_ERROR. An env value the harness cannot parse falls back to its default without error, which would mis-count and could overlap other slots.\nI checked the real binary's output end to end in a temp state dir: SLOT_SEEDS=3, STEPS=4 gives op_steps=12.\nMutations: count clean*STEPS KILLED; drop steps check KILLED; drop base check KILLED. Dropping the seeds check SURVIVES because the end-seeds bound covers the same case. That is intended redundancy.\n\nF3 (DONE masks a violation): with PARALLEL>1, a slot that crosses the target writes DONE even if a peer wrote a VIOLATION STOP during its run. status.sh checked DONE before STOP, so it printed \"DONE — 1e8 reached with 0 violations\".\nFix: DONE is written only with no STOP and no VIOLATION_OR_ERROR ledger row. status.sh checks STOP first and prints DONE only when viol==0; otherwise it prints NOT A PASS.\nTest: a_peer_violation_is_never_reported_as_done. Mutations KILLED: DONE under STOP; status reporting DONE first.\n\nF4 (INFRA-HALT overwrites a peer's VIOLATION STOP): the infra-halt branch wrote STOP with a plain truncating redirect. The INFRA-HALT text tells the operator to \"free disk then rm STOP to resume\", so following it would resume past a real finding.\nFix: write it under noclobber (O_EXCL). A violation still overwrites an INFRA-HALT.\nTest: infra_halt_never_overwrites_a_peer_violation_stop. Mutation (clobber) KILLED.\n\nReviewed, no defect found: infra.rs classifier (positive-match only; typed payload; violation outranks infra); in_proc apply_op/observe_state/check_oracles fail-closed paths; vacuity guard plus the ws_unobserved cross-check; oracle_a existing_objects pruned-root rescan (a pruned root sets retreated, which forces the full rescan); model.rs bn-1fcox target_stale/P_TARGET_CHECKED_OUT; setup.sh.\n\nNotes, not fixed:\n(a) The vacuity guard is per seed only. A harness or generator regression that stops producing commits would pass every seed with witnesses=0. CI unit tests and the op-stream digests cover this today; the slot ledger records witnesses but does not gate on them.\n(b) The pre.6 archive campaign ledger (~/.local/state/maw-sg1-soak) has 2 VIOLATION_OR_ERROR rows and was resumed. Under F3, DONE can never be written for that state dir. It is archive only.\n(c) Oracle B B3 skips an unreadable merge-state file. This is pre-existing and not reachable in-proc, because the in-proc tier never writes merge-state.\n(d) slot.sh is read live from the trunk checkout. After merge, the running pre16 campaign accrues 32000 per slot, not 32064. Its existing cumulative already includes the canonical-seed overcount (64 per clean slot). The pre.17 re-pin resets it anyway.\n\nGates: cargo build --release -p maw-cli; TMPDIR=/var/tmp/bn-2qamr just check green (no FAILED); cargo clippy -p maw-assurance --all-targets --features oracles -D warnings clean; maw-assurance --lib 140 ok, sg1_dst 11 ok (1 ignored), sg1_soak_slot 7 ok.\n"}	blake3:96nso_B3QNETSu9ih1Y32aMyB38PJVCDtFX8onF3fBA
1790556964216420	maw-nzv80n	itc:AQ		item.move	bn-15ebo	{"state":"done"}	blake3:TRfWwxlTwOcDOQRTXQjElUnlchqr7qR-jXEGV-sluRU
1790557628904257	maw-nzv80n	itc:AQ		item.comment	bn-1sbjf	{"body":"bn-1sbjf evidence (workspace bn-1sbjf, commit 9eb81b7a after sync onto 56fab1c5)\n\nWIRING\n- CRASHABLE_BY_PHASE cleanup += FP_UPDATE_DEFAULT_BEFORE_SNAPSHOT, FP_CLEANUP_AFTER_DEFAULT_CHECKOUT.\n- DANGEROUS_FAILPOINTS += FP_CLEANUP_AFTER_DEFAULT_CHECKOUT.\n- FP_UPDATE_DEFAULT_BEFORE_SNAPSHOT is error-style: new fault::HANDLED_ERROR_FAILPOINTS + production_fp_spec(); faulted production tier arms =error for it (drives the bn-3jqfk fallback), =abort elsewhere. FaultPlan::from_seed already gives it Unwind(error)/Panic since it is not dangerous.\n\nDIGESTS (re-pinned, campaign reset): default 0x61c78834e645f514->0x47e80c0396be778b; production 0x7353896eacca2728->0x6449230202ed7fc2; escape-heavy 0xceffff94f36bdfd6->0x8e09b3f9d8e9cdf1. Diff of 3 profiles x 256 seeds x 128 steps with fault names masked: 0 lines (ops/phases/git_times identical); only cleanup fault names reshuffle (134/136 over 2 sites -> 66/68/69/67 over 4).\n\nTARGETED DST (tests/dst_production_tier.rs, #[ignore], in `just sg1-production-tier-faults`), plan maw-scenario::bn_1sbjf_target_update_crash_plan:\n- bn_1sbjf_crash_after_default_checkout_is_recovered: GREEN. Non-vacuity asserted: merge crashed, journal + target-checkout intent on disk, merged tree on disk and user edit NOT on disk before the recovering merge.\n  MUTATION: ignore the checkout intent in update_default_workspace (resume guard `&& env NEUTER`) -> RED: \"uncommitted trunk bytes at 'base.txt' are not back on disk after recovery (left 'base content\\n')\". Oracles stayed green (TrunkDirtyPreservation accepts recovery-ref survival) - the strict end-state check is what catches it.\n- bn_1sbjf_failed_snapshot_fallback_keeps_trunk_edits_and_symlink: GREEN; output contains \"snapshot_working_copy failed\", merge exit 0.\n  MUTATION: DiskSide::capture uses metadata() (follows links, pre-bn-3jqfk) -> RED: \"bn-3jqfk: the user's symlink retarget was lost (left base.txt, right trunk/untracked.txt)\".\n  Both mutations reverted.\n  NOTE: mutation runs need BOTH target/debug/maw (plain binary runs the unfaulted recovering merge) and the failpoints bin rebuilt.\n\nGATES\n- just check (after sync): rc=0, no FAILED.\n- cargo test -p maw-scenario: 27 passed. cargo test -p maw-assurance --features oracles: 142+9+4 passed.\n- just dst-fast: in just check, green.\n- just sg1-per-commit-smoke: planted-violation smoke OK.\n- just sg1-faithful-test: rc=0, 18 result lines all ok.\n- just sg1-production-tier-faults: 16x24 0 violations (7 faults injected) + 2 bn_1sbjf tests pass. Extra: DST_TRACES=48 DST_STEPS=40 faulted: 1920 op-steps, 44 faults, 0 violations.\n- Soak: SG1_NIGHTLY_SEEDS=200 SG1_NIGHTLY_STEPS=64 sg1_nightly_soak (release): seeds=201 clean=201 violations=0 oracle_a_checks=13065 witnesses=2959 harness_errors=0.\n"}	blake3:jVidJeot7EgvfblALd5HVXMrdSV0JEjI1cs0-uNDVKg
1790558013933623	maw-nzv80n	itc:AQ		item.move	bn-1bkr0	{"state":"done"}	blake3:bDexaq0M5UKtLazJ6o4FVPm77JDwxU8m6pfjfTgxT20
1790558539838511	maw-nzv80n	itc:AQ		item.move	bn-2qamr	{"state":"done"}	blake3:fFsL80_GlK9BwClw1hqlK2McOpEi_q4Ka6FU3RUP5Rw
1790558655576723	maw-nzv80n	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-2zubk	{"description":"FOUND BY: bn-1sbjf worker (2026-09-27).\n1. TrunkDirtyPreservation accepts uncommitted trunk bytes that survive ONLY in a\n   recovery ref. That upholds the Prime Invariant (nothing lost) but cannot distinguish\n   a correct merge from one that silently moved the user's edits into a ref and left\n   the worktree without them — exactly the bn-15fzo and bn-3jqfk regressions, which the\n   oracles stayed GREEN on when those fixes were neutered (only a new strict end-state\n   check in the targeted tests caught them). Add an oracle (or a stricter mode of the\n   existing one) that flags displacement unless the operation also reported it to the\n   user (e.g. a type_change/directory_change conflict or a printed recovery command in\n   its output). Run it in the production tier + soak; mutation-check against neutered\n   bn-15fzo / bn-3jqfk fixes. NOTE: changing the soak's oracles changes the harness —\n   coordinate with the soak re-pin (cheapest before a long campaign).\n2. crates/maw-assurance fault::read_merge_phase reads .manifold/merge-state.json, not the\n   consolidated .maw/manifold/ path, so SubprocFault may never observe a merge phase on\n   consolidated repos (phase-targeted faults in the production tier may be inert). Fix\n   via layout detection; add a test that a phase-targeted fault actually fires in a\n   consolidated repo.\n3. `cargo clippy -p maw-assurance --features oracles` fails on existing code\n   (model.rs:1620 suspicious_operation_groupings, model.rs:2307 doc paragraph too long);\n   `just clippy` doesn't enable those features. Fix, and make sure the CI lane that\n   runs sg1-assurance-clippy would have caught it.\n","kind":"bug","labels":["dst","verification"],"size":"s","title":"DST oracles cannot see edits silently displaced into a recovery ref; production-tier fault injector reads legacy .manifold path"}	blake3:vsQ2VYw8W24l3KEVDi9tV4MMaF3p66LYTzz60-kUYGY
1790559011852687	maw-nzv80n	itc:AQ		item.move	bn-1sbjf	{"state":"done"}	blake3:1AYIpUzKNfYZea4M_i6PaxEivTg93Gs3vZFplNGMPBc
