1790559084644104	maw-nzv80n	itc:AQ		item.assign	bn-2zubk	{"action":"assign","agent":"maw-nzv80n"}	blake3:FmG7CH2Kjss9DXhgytoBahZnFq6DAjb-3wS1RUoHcWg
1790561523331044	maw-nzv80n	itc:AQ		item.comment	bn-2zubk	{"body":"bn-2zubk evidence (workspace bn-2zubk, commit 8358551b, synced onto eff4fad1 pre.17)\n\n(1) DISPLACEMENT ORACLE: oracle_escape::TrunkDirtyDisplacement (strict companion of TrunkDirtyPreservation). Recorded dirty trunk files AND symlinks must stay on disk unless the op output reported the move: a line naming the path + a recovery handle (maw ws resolve / maw ws recover / stash apply / Snapshot preserved at / git show), or a whole-snapshot notice (replay_snapshot failed / pre-merge edits pinned at). The always-printed \"recovery snapshot pinned\" line does NOT count. A paragraph naming the path that CLAIMS \"was restored\"/\"already on disk\" while it is not on disk is flagged (claimed_on_disk). Crashed ops defer judgement to the next completed merge. Wired into run_seed + drive_plan_on (unfaulted, faulted, regression plans); execute_op now keeps op output; bn_1sbjf symlink is registered via before_step.\nMUTATIONS (production code, reverted; both binaries rebuilt):\n- bn-15fzo resume skipped (checkout_intent::read(..)?.filter(|_| false)): bn_1sbjf_crash_after_default_checkout_is_recovered RED from the ORACLE: \"step=8 op=merge TrunkDirtyDisplacement: ... 'base.txt' left the default worktree across a crash and the recovering merge and the user was never told ... survives only in a recovery ref\" (+ trunk/untracked.txt).\n- bn-3jqfk capture follows links (DiskSide::capture uses metadata()): bn_1sbjf_failed_snapshot_fallback... RED from the ORACLE: 'base.txt' and 'link' \"... the op output FALSELY claimed the user's version is back on disk\". (First cut accepted this: under the regression maw prints \"replay did not reproduce your edits to 'link' ... Restore: maw ws recover ... --restore-file link (your version is already on disk)\" - hence the false-claim rule.)\n- bn-1sbjf worker's variant (resume guard `&& false`): only the strict end-state assert catches it; the oracle is green because that path goes through the stale-intent arm which prints \"left its pre-merge edits pinned at <ref>\" - a real report by design (code reading).\n(2) read_merge_phase / oracle G3 / trace snapshot now use layout-aware maw_assurance::merge_state_path (pinned vs maw-core in fault::tests::read_phase_is_layout_aware). New #[ignore] bn_2zubk_phase_targeted_fault_fires_in_consolidated_repo (in sg1-production-tier-faults): maw-init consolidated repo, SubprocFault at cleanup/FP_CLEANUP_BEFORE_DEFAULT_CHECKOUT -> Recovered, journal gone, work on trunk. MUTATION legacy path -> RED PhaseNotObserved. Also fixed SubprocFault::recover_with_retry: a cleared journal counts as recovered (post-CAS recovery finishes the merge, then the same invocation refuses the now-stale source -> exit 1 -> was RecoveryExhausted).\n(3) model.rs clippy fixed; sg1-assurance-clippy lints maw-assurance --all-features (oracles did not imply stateright) and is a dep of `just check`; ci_lane_wiring pins both (mutation: recipe back to --features oracles -> RED).\nGATES: just check rc=0 (0 FAILED); maw-assurance --features oracles 149+11+7 ok; maw-scenario 27 ok; sg1-per-commit-smoke OK; sg1-production-tier-faults: 16x24 0 violations, 22 displacement judgements, 7 faults + bn_1sbjf x2 + bn_2zubk ok; sg1-assurance-clippy clean.\nSoak 200x64 (in-proc, release): seeds=201 clean=201 violations=0 oracle_a_checks=13065 witnesses=2959 harness_errors=0. NOTE the in-proc soak has no default worktree and DirtyTrunkWrite is a no-op there, so the displacement oracle cannot run in it; its coverage is the production tier.\nDeep production: unfaulted 48x48: 0 violations, 180 displacement judgements (2 reported). Faulted 48x48 DST_ESCAPE_WEIGHT=8: 0 displacement violations (139 judgements, 2 reported) but 5 seeds RED from PRE-EXISTING oracles, all first at a gc op (OracleA G1 seeds 5,10,26,46; TrunkDirtyPreservation seed 12) - gc --recovery-snapshots --older-than 0 pruning recovery-only content; not caused by this bone, needs triage.\n"}	blake3:FJb_tFgUXemYzjU32vcv3x9LmJmhnLA-vt1hZfu27GY
1790561914528515	maw-nzv80n	itc:AQ		item.move	bn-2zubk	{"state":"done"}	blake3:PTyB1YHAVNEQFynGcUO51ZoUEEyYoQcCbVYqWkM6wEg
